{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FxApisRjBjrita3LYYUvhh","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Spec: Container Lifecycle Management\n     2→\n     3→## Problem Statement\n     4→\n     5→Vista needs to manage Docker containers for ralph loops: one container per loop, built from a modified claudebox image, with project files mounted at the project root. For OpenCode loops, Vista also needs to manage an `opencode serve` instance on the host and proxy API calls from containers to it.\n     6→\n     7→## Proposed Solution\n     8→\n     9→A `ContainerManager` service that owns container lifecycle (create, monitor, teardown) and an `OpenCodeServeManager` that owns the host-side `opencode serve` process. Both are coordinated by the `RalphService` at loop start/stop time.\n    10→\n    11→### Container Naming\n    12→\n    13→Each loop gets its own container:\n    14→\n    15→```\n    16→vista-ralph-{job_id}\n    17→```\n    18→\n    19→Examples:\n    20→- `vista-ralph-a1b2c3d4`\n    21→- `vista-ralph-f9e8d7c6`\n    22→\n    23→### Docker Labels\n    24→\n    25→Every managed container gets these labels:\n    26→\n    27→| Label | Value | Purpose |\n    28→|-------|-------|---------|\n    29→| `managed-by` | `vista-ralph` | Identifies Vista-managed containers |\n    30→| `vista-job-id` | `{job_id}` | Links container to ralph job |\n    31→| `vista-provider` | `claude` or `opencode` | Which execution path |\n    32→| `vista-session` | `{vista_session_id}` | Vista server session (for orphan detection) |\n    33→| `vista-project` | `{project_root_hash}` | Which project |\n    34→\n    35→### Container Lifecycle\n    36→\n    37→```\n    38→                    create_job()\n    39→     [none] ──────────────────────→ [creating]\n    40→                                        │\n    41→                                        ▼\n    42→                                    [running] ── loop iterations\n    43→                                        │\n    44→                           loop completes / ralph_stop\n    45→                                        │\n    46→                                        ▼\n    47→                                    [removing]\n    48→                                        │\n    49→                                        ▼\n    50→                                    [removed]\n    51→\n    52→     Vista startup  → find orphans by label → remove\n    53→     Vista shutdown  → stop + remove all managed containers\n    54→```\n    55→\n    56→### ContainerManager API\n    57→\n    58→```python\n    59→class ContainerManager:\n    60→    def __init__(self, docker_client, session_id: str):\n    61→        self.docker = docker_client\n    62→        self.session_id = session_id\n    63→\n    64→    async def create_loop_container(\n    65→        self,\n    66→        job_id: str,\n    67→        provider_name: str,\n    68→        project_root: Path,\n    69→        credentials: list[DockerCredentialConfig],\n    70→        image: str,\n    71→        network: bool = True,\n    72→    ) -> ContainerInfo:\n    73→        \"\"\"Create a new container for a ralph loop.\n    74→\n    75→        1. Build volume mounts:\n    76→           - Project root → /workspace/ (rw)\n    77→           - Credential mounts (from providers)\n    78→        2. Build environment variables (from credential providers)\n    79→        3. Create and start container\n    80→        4. Return ContainerInfo\n    81→        \"\"\"\n    82→\n    83→    async def exec_in_container(\n    84→        self,\n    85→        container_name: str,\n    86→        command: list[str],\n    87→        workdir: str = \"/workspace\",\n    88→        env: dict = None,\n    89→        stdout_handle=None,\n    90→    ) -> ExecHandle:\n    91→        \"\"\"Run a command inside a container via docker exec.\n    92→\n    93→        Returns ExecHandle with host_pid for tracking.\n    94→        Supports streaming stdout to a file handle.\n    95→        \"\"\"\n    96→\n    97→    async def remove_container(self, container_name: str) -> None:\n    98→        \"\"\"Stop and remove a container.\"\"\"\n    99→\n   100→    async def cleanup_orphans(self) -> list[str]:\n   101→        \"\"\"Find and remove containers from previous Vista sessions.\n   102→\n   103→        Looks for containers with label managed-by=vista-ralph\n   104→        where vista-session != current session_id.\n   105→        Returns list of removed container names.\n   106→        \"\"\"\n   107→\n   108→    async def shutdown_all(self) -> None:\n   109→        \"\"\"Stop and remove all containers managed by this session.\"\"\"\n   110→\n   111→    def list_containers(self) -> list[ContainerInfo]:\n   112→        \"\"\"List all managed containers with their status.\"\"\"\n   113→```\n   114→\n   115→### Container Creation\n   116→\n   117→```python\n   118→container = docker.containers.create(\n   119→    image=image,\n   120→    name=f\"vista-ralph-{job_id}\",\n   121→    labels={\n   122→        \"managed-by\": \"vista-ralph\",\n   123→        \"vista-job-id\": job_id,\n   124→        \"vista-provider\": provider_name,\n   125→        \"vista-session\": self.session_id,\n   126→        \"vista-project\": hashlib.sha256(str(project_root).encode()).hexdigest()[:8],\n   127→    },\n   128→    volumes={\n   129→        # Project root → /workspace/ (always full project)\n   130→        str(project_root): {\"bind\": \"/workspace\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n   131→        # Credential mounts (from providers)\n   132→        **self._build_credential_mounts(credentials),\n   133→    },\n   134→    environment={\n   135→        \"DEVCONTAINER\": \"true\",\n   136→        **self._build_env_vars(credentials),\n   137→    },\n   138→    network_mode=\"bridge\" if network else \"none\",\n   139→    user=f\"{host_uid}:{host_gid}\",\n   140→    working_dir=\"/workspace\",\n   141→    stdin_open=False,\n   142→    tty=False,\n   143→    # Extra host entry so container can reach Vista server\n   144→    extra_hosts={\"host.docker.internal\": \"host-gateway\"},\n   145→    command=\"sleep infinity\",  # Keep container alive for exec\n   146→    detach=True,\n   147→)\n   148→container.start()\n   149→```\n   150→\n   151→**Key details:**\n   152→- `command=\"sleep infinity\"` keeps the container running for the duration of the loop\n   153→- Loop iterations use `docker exec` to run inside the existing container\n   154→- `extra_hosts` ensures `host.docker.internal` resolves on Linux (Docker Desktop on Windows/macOS provides this automatically)\n   155→- `user=f\"{host_uid}:{host_gid}\"` ensures files created in container have correct ownership on host\n   156→- Project root is ALWAYS mounted as `/workspace/` with full read-write access\n   157→- Agents can always access `.vista/features/`, `.vista/ralph/`, source code, and `.git/`\n   158→\n   159→### Loop Execution Inside Container\n   160→\n   161→**Claude Code loops:**\n   162→```python\n   163→# Loop script runs claude -p natively inside container\n   164→exec_handle = await container_manager.exec_in_container(\n   165→    container_name=f\"vista-ralph-{job_id}\",\n   166→    command=[\"bash\", \"/workspace/.vista/ralph/{slug}/{job_id}/loop.sh\"],\n   167→    workdir=\"/workspace\",\n   168→    stdout_handle=output_log_handle,\n   169→)\n   170→```\n   171→\n   172→**OpenCode loops:**\n   173→```python\n   174→# Loop script calls Vista's proxy endpoint from inside container\n   175→exec_handle = await container_manager.exec_in_container(\n   176→    container_name=f\"vista-ralph-{job_id}\",\n   177→    command=[\"bash\", \"/workspace/.vista/ralph/{slug}/{job_id}/loop.sh\"],\n   178→    workdir=\"/workspace\",\n   179→    env={\n   180→        \"VISTA_HOST\": \"host.docker.internal\",\n   181→        \"VISTA_PORT\": str(vista_port),\n   182→        \"OPENCODE_SESSION\": session_id,\n   183→    },\n   184→    stdout_handle=output_log_handle,\n   185→)\n   186→```\n   187→\n   188→The loop script for OpenCode loops uses `curl` (or a small helper) to call the Vista proxy instead of invoking `opencode run` directly. See [ralph-mcp-integration](ralph-mcp-integration.md) for the loop script template changes.\n   189→\n   190→### OpenCode Serve Manager\n   191→\n   192→```python\n   193→class OpenCodeServeManager:\n   194→    \"\"\"Manages the host-side opencode serve process.\"\"\"\n   195→\n   196→    def __init__(self, port: int = 4096):\n   197→        self.port = port\n   198→        self.process: subprocess.Popen | None = None\n   199→        self.sessions: dict[str, str] = {}  # job_id → session_id\n   200→\n   201→    async def ensure_running(self) -> None:\n   202→        \"\"\"Start opencode serve if not already running.\n   203→\n   204→        Command: opencode serve --port {self.port} --hostname 127.0.0.1\n   205→        Process runs in background, managed by Vista.\n   206→        Health check: GET http://localhost:{port}/doc (OpenAPI spec)\n   207→        \"\"\"\n   208→\n   209→    async def create_session(self, job_id: str, cwd: str) -> str:\n   210→        \"\"\"Create a new session on the opencode serve instance.\n   211→\n   212→        Returns session_id for use in API calls.\n   213→        Session is scoped to cwd (project root).\n   214→        \"\"\"\n   215→\n   216→    async def close_session(self, job_id: str) -> None:\n   217→        \"\"\"Close a session when a loop finishes.\"\"\"\n   218→\n   219→    async def stop(self) -> None:\n   220→        \"\"\"Stop the opencode serve process.\"\"\"\n   221→\n   222→    def is_running(self) -> bool:\n   223→        \"\"\"Check if opencode serve process is alive.\"\"\"\n   224→```\n   225→\n   226→### Orphan Cleanup on Startup\n   227→\n   228→```python\n   229→async def cleanup_orphans(self):\n   230→    \"\"\"Called during Vista server startup.\"\"\"\n   231→    containers = docker.containers.list(\n   232→        all=True,  # Include stopped containers\n   233→        filters={\"label\": \"managed-by=vista-ralph\"}\n   234→    )\n   235→    orphans = []\n   236→    for c in containers:\n   237→        if c.labels.get(\"vista-session\") != self.session_id:\n   238→            c.stop(timeout=10)\n   239→            c.remove()\n   240→            orphans.append(c.name)\n   241→    return orphans\n   242→```\n   243→\n   244→### Container Removal on Loop Finish\n   245→\n   246→When a loop completes (naturally or via `ralph_stop`):\n   247→\n   248→```python\n   249→async def on_loop_finish(self, job_id: str):\n   250→    container_name = f\"vista-ralph-{job_id}\"\n   251→    # For OpenCode loops: close the serve session\n   252→    if job_id in self.opencode_serve_manager.sessions:\n   253→        await self.opencode_serve_manager.close_session(job_id)\n   254→    # Remove the container\n   255→    await self.container_manager.remove_container(container_name)\n   256→```\n   257→\n   258→### Docker Image Management\n   259→\n   260→The modified claudebox image is built once and cached:\n   261→\n   262→```python\n   263→async def ensure_image(self, image_name: str = \"vista-ralph:latest\") -> str:\n   264→    \"\"\"Ensure the sandbox Docker image exists.\n   265→\n   266→    1. Check if image exists locally\n   267→    2. If not, build from Vista's Dockerfile (based on claudebox)\n   268→    3. Return image name\n   269→\n   270→    Build args: USER_ID, GROUP_ID (from host), NODE_VERSION\n   271→    \"\"\"\n   272→```\n   273→\n   274→Image rebuild is triggered when:\n   275→- Vista detects the Dockerfile has changed (hash stored in settings)\n   276→- Image doesn't exist locally\n   277→- Rebuild requested via internal API (`POST /api/sandbox/image/build`)\n   278→\n   279→## Edge Cases\n   280→\n   281→- **Docker not installed/running**: `docker.from_env()` raises `DockerException`. Caught at startup, sandbox marked as unavailable with clear error message.\n   282→- **Image not found**: `create_loop_container` fails with error \"Image not found. Build the sandbox image from settings.\"\n   283→- **Container dies during loop**: `ralph_status` detects container is gone. Job marked as failed.\n   284→- **`opencode serve` crashes**: Vista detects via health check. Restarts automatically. In-flight loops may fail and need retry.\n   285→- **Multiple Vista instances**: Each has a unique `session_id`. Orphan cleanup only removes containers from OTHER sessions.\n   286→- **Concurrent loops**: Each gets its own container. No shared state. Containers operate on the same project files via separate bind mounts (safe for most operations, may conflict on git operations).\n   287→- **Loop script needs `opencode serve` but it's not running**: Vista auto-starts it on first OpenCode loop. Container creation waits for serve health check to pass.\n   288→\n   289→## Dependencies\n   290→\n   291→- `docker` Python SDK (new dependency)\n   292→- Spec: [credential-management](credential-management.md) - Provides `DockerCredentialConfig` for volume/env setup\n   293→- Spec: [ralph-mcp-integration](ralph-mcp-integration.md) - Modified spawn flow and loop script templates\n   294→- `vista/server/services/ralph_service.py` - Modified to route through sandbox when enabled\n   295→\n   296→## Testing Strategy\n   297→\n   298→- Unit tests for container naming and label generation\n   299→- Unit tests for volume mount construction (project root + credentials)\n   300→- Integration tests with real Docker: create → exec → remove\n   301→- Integration test: orphan cleanup with mock containers from \"old sessions\"\n   302→- Integration test: `opencode serve` start, health check, session create/close, stop\n   303→- Concurrency test: two loop containers running simultaneously\n   304→- Container removal test: loop finish triggers cleanup\n   305→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6fe45d16-ab3a-4e41-9b98-035326f9b7c3","uuid":"0d70661a-4d38-4788-849a-677efd3b8cba","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/.vista/features/docker-sandbox/specs/container-lifecycle.md","content":"# Spec: Container Lifecycle Management\n\n## Problem Statement\n\nVista needs to manage Docker containers for ralph loops: one container per loop, built from a modified claudebox image, with project files mounted at the project root. For OpenCode loops, Vista also needs to manage an `opencode serve` instance on the host and proxy API calls from containers to it.\n\n## Proposed Solution\n\nA `ContainerManager` service that owns container lifecycle (create, monitor, teardown) and an `OpenCodeServeManager` that owns the host-side `opencode serve` process. Both are coordinated by the `RalphService` at loop start/stop time.\n\n### Container Naming\n\nEach loop gets its own container:\n\n```\nvista-ralph-{job_id}\n```\n\nExamples:\n- `vista-ralph-a1b2c3d4`\n- `vista-ralph-f9e8d7c6`\n\n### Docker Labels\n\nEvery managed container gets these labels:\n\n| Label | Value | Purpose |\n|-------|-------|---------|\n| `managed-by` | `vista-ralph` | Identifies Vista-managed containers |\n| `vista-job-id` | `{job_id}` | Links container to ralph job |\n| `vista-provider` | `claude` or `opencode` | Which execution path |\n| `vista-session` | `{vista_session_id}` | Vista server session (for orphan detection) |\n| `vista-project` | `{project_root_hash}` | Which project |\n\n### Container Lifecycle\n\n```\n                    create_job()\n     [none] ──────────────────────→ [creating]\n                                        │\n                                        ▼\n                                    [running] ── loop iterations\n                                        │\n                           loop completes / ralph_stop\n                                        │\n                                        ▼\n                                    [removing]\n                                        │\n                                        ▼\n                                    [removed]\n\n     Vista startup  → find orphans by label → remove\n     Vista shutdown  → stop + remove all managed containers\n```\n\n### ContainerManager API\n\n```python\nclass ContainerManager:\n    def __init__(self, docker_client, session_id: str):\n        self.docker = docker_client\n        self.session_id = session_id\n\n    async def create_loop_container(\n        self,\n        job_id: str,\n        provider_name: str,\n        project_root: Path,\n        credentials: list[DockerCredentialConfig],\n        image: str,\n        network: bool = True,\n    ) -> ContainerInfo:\n        \"\"\"Create a new container for a ralph loop.\n\n        1. Build volume mounts:\n           - Project root → /workspace/ (rw)\n           - Credential mounts (from providers)\n        2. Build environment variables (from credential providers)\n        3. Create and start container\n        4. Return ContainerInfo\n        \"\"\"\n\n    async def exec_in_container(\n        self,\n        container_name: str,\n        command: list[str],\n        workdir: str = \"/workspace\",\n        env: dict = None,\n        stdout_handle=None,\n    ) -> ExecHandle:\n        \"\"\"Run a command inside a container via docker exec.\n\n        Returns ExecHandle with host_pid for tracking.\n        Supports streaming stdout to a file handle.\n        \"\"\"\n\n    async def remove_container(self, container_name: str) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Stop and remove a container.\"\"\"\n\n    async def cleanup_orphans(self) -> list[str]:\n        \"\"\"Find and remove containers from previous Vista sessions.\n\n        Looks for containers with label managed-by=vista-ralph\n        where vista-session != current session_id.\n        Returns list of removed container names.\n        \"\"\"\n\n    async def shutdown_all(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Stop and remove all containers managed by this session.\"\"\"\n\n    def list_containers(self) -> list[ContainerInfo]:\n        \"\"\"List all managed containers with their status.\"\"\"\n```\n\n### Container Creation\n\n```python\ncontainer = docker.containers.create(\n    image=image,\n    name=f\"vista-ralph-{job_id}\",\n    labels={\n        \"managed-by\": \"vista-ralph\",\n        \"vista-job-id\": job_id,\n        \"vista-provider\": provider_name,\n        \"vista-session\": self.session_id,\n        \"vista-project\": hashlib.sha256(str(project_root).encode()).hexdigest()[:8],\n    },\n    volumes={\n        # Project root → /workspace/ (always full project)\n        str(project_root): {\"bind\": \"/workspace\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n        # Credential mounts (from providers)\n        **self._build_credential_mounts(credentials),\n    },\n    environment={\n        \"DEVCONTAINER\": \"true\",\n        **self._build_env_vars(credentials),\n    },\n    network_mode=\"bridge\" if network else \"none\",\n    user=f\"{host_uid}:{host_gid}\",\n    working_dir=\"/workspace\",\n    stdin_open=False,\n    tty=False,\n    # Extra host entry so container can reach Vista server\n    extra_hosts={\"host.docker.internal\": \"host-gateway\"},\n    command=\"sleep infinity\",  # Keep container alive for exec\n    detach=True,\n)\ncontainer.start()\n```\n\n**Key details:**\n- `command=\"sleep infinity\"` keeps the container running for the duration of the loop\n- Loop iterations use `docker exec` to run inside the existing container\n- `extra_hosts` ensures `host.docker.internal` resolves on Linux (Docker Desktop on Windows/macOS provides this automatically)\n- `user=f\"{host_uid}:{host_gid}\"` ensures files created in container have correct ownership on host\n- Project root is ALWAYS mounted as `/workspace/` with full read-write access\n- Agents can always access `.vista/features/`, `.vista/ralph/`, source code, and `.git/`\n\n### Loop Execution Inside Container\n\n**Claude Code loops:**\n```python\n# Loop script runs claude -p natively inside container\nexec_handle = await container_manager.exec_in_container(\n    container_name=f\"vista-ralph-{job_id}\",\n    command=[\"bash\", \"/workspace/.vista/ralph/{slug}/{job_id}/loop.sh\"],\n    workdir=\"/workspace\",\n    stdout_handle=output_log_handle,\n)\n```\n\n**OpenCode loops:**\n```python\n# Loop script calls Vista's proxy endpoint from inside container\nexec_handle = await container_manager.exec_in_container(\n    container_name=f\"vista-ralph-{job_id}\",\n    command=[\"bash\", \"/workspace/.vista/ralph/{slug}/{job_id}/loop.sh\"],\n    workdir=\"/workspace\",\n    env={\n        \"VISTA_HOST\": \"host.docker.internal\",\n        \"VISTA_PORT\": str(vista_port),\n        \"OPENCODE_SESSION\": session_id,\n    },\n    stdout_handle=output_log_handle,\n)\n```\n\nThe loop script for OpenCode loops uses `curl` (or a small helper) to call the Vista proxy instead of invoking `opencode run` directly. See [ralph-mcp-integration](ralph-mcp-integration.md) for the loop script template changes.\n\n### OpenCode Serve Manager\n\n```python\nclass OpenCodeServeManager:\n    \"\"\"Manages the host-side opencode serve process.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, port: int = 4096):\n        self.port = port\n        self.process: subprocess.Popen | None = None\n        self.sessions: dict[str, str] = {}  # job_id → session_id\n\n    async def ensure_running(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Start opencode serve if not already running.\n\n        Command: opencode serve --port {self.port} --hostname 127.0.0.1\n        Process runs in background, managed by Vista.\n        Health check: GET http://localhost:{port}/doc (OpenAPI spec)\n        \"\"\"\n\n    async def create_session(self, job_id: str, cwd: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Create a new session on the opencode serve instance.\n\n        Returns session_id for use in API calls.\n        Session is scoped to cwd (project root).\n        \"\"\"\n\n    async def close_session(self, job_id: str) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Close a session when a loop finishes.\"\"\"\n\n    async def stop(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Stop the opencode serve process.\"\"\"\n\n    def is_running(self) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Check if opencode serve process is alive.\"\"\"\n```\n\n### Orphan Cleanup on Startup\n\n```python\nasync def cleanup_orphans(self):\n    \"\"\"Called during Vista server startup.\"\"\"\n    containers = docker.containers.list(\n        all=True,  # Include stopped containers\n        filters={\"label\": \"managed-by=vista-ralph\"}\n    )\n    orphans = []\n    for c in containers:\n        if c.labels.get(\"vista-session\") != self.session_id:\n            c.stop(timeout=10)\n            c.remove()\n            orphans.append(c.name)\n    return orphans\n```\n\n### Container Removal on Loop Finish\n\nWhen a loop completes (naturally or via `ralph_stop`):\n\n```python\nasync def on_loop_finish(self, job_id: str):\n    container_name = f\"vista-ralph-{job_id}\"\n    # For OpenCode loops: close the serve session\n    if job_id in self.opencode_serve_manager.sessions:\n        await self.opencode_serve_manager.close_session(job_id)\n    # Remove the container\n    await self.container_manager.remove_container(container_name)\n```\n\n### Docker Image Management\n\nThe modified claudebox image is built once and cached:\n\n```python\nasync def ensure_image(self, image_name: str = \"vista-ralph:latest\") -> str:\n    \"\"\"Ensure the sandbox Docker image exists.\n\n    1. Check if image exists locally\n    2. If not, build from Vista's Dockerfile (based on claudebox)\n    3. Return image name\n\n    Build args: USER_ID, GROUP_ID (from host), NODE_VERSION\n    \"\"\"\n```\n\nImage rebuild is triggered when:\n- Vista detects the Dockerfile has changed (hash stored in settings)\n- Image doesn't exist locally\n- Rebuild requested via internal API (`POST /api/sandbox/image/build`)\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- **Docker not installed/running**: `docker.from_env()` raises `DockerException`. Caught at startup, sandbox marked as unavailable with clear error message.\n- **Image not found**: `create_loop_container` fails with error \"Image not found. Build the sandbox image from settings.\"\n- **Container dies during loop**: `ralph_status` detects container is gone. Job marked as failed.\n- **`opencode serve` crashes**: Vista detects via health check. Restarts automatically. In-flight loops may fail and need retry.\n- **Multiple Vista instances**: Each has a unique `session_id`. Orphan cleanup only removes containers from OTHER sessions.\n- **Concurrent loops**: Each gets its own container. No shared state. Containers operate on the same project files via separate bind mounts (safe for most operations, may conflict on git operations).\n- **Loop script needs `opencode serve` but it's not running**: Vista auto-starts it on first OpenCode loop. Container creation waits for serve health check to pass.\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- `docker` Python SDK (new dependency)\n- Spec: [credential-management](credential-management.md) - Provides `DockerCredentialConfig` for volume/env setup\n- Spec: [ralph-mcp-integration](ralph-mcp-integration.md) - Modified spawn flow and loop script templates\n- `vista/server/services/ralph_service.py` - Modified to route through sandbox when enabled\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n- Unit tests for container naming and label generation\n- Unit tests for volume mount construction (project root + credentials)\n- Integration tests with real Docker: create → exec → remove\n- Integration test: orphan cleanup with mock containers from \"old sessions\"\n- Integration test: `opencode serve` start, health check, session create/close, stop\n- Concurrency test: two loop containers running simultaneously\n- Container removal test: loop finish triggers cleanup\n","numLines":305,"startLine":1,"totalLines":305}}}
