{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QXnn62eBubLYCzftrbHaAp","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Spec: Credential Management\n     2→\n     3→## Problem Statement\n     4→\n     5→Docker containers need host credentials to function: Claude Code needs OAuth tokens and API keys, git needs SSH keys and identity config. The challenge is mounting these automatically without user intervention, handling platform differences (Windows vs Linux vs macOS), and validating that mounted credentials actually work inside the container.\n     6→\n     7→With the split execution model, OpenCode loops do NOT need AI credentials in the container — `opencode serve` runs on the host with native auth. This dramatically simplifies the credential story.\n     8→\n     9→## Proposed Solution\n    10→\n    11→A **credential provider** pattern where each provider encapsulates the logic to detect, mount, and validate a specific credential type. Providers are scoped to what's actually needed in the container — git/SSH credentials (both paths) and Claude auth (Claude Code path only).\n    12→\n    13→### What Goes in the Container vs What Stays on Host\n    14→\n    15→| Credential | Claude Code Loops | OpenCode Loops | Why |\n    16→|---|---|---|---|\n    17→| `~/.claude/` (OAuth + session) | Mounted (rw) | Not needed | Claude Code runs inside container |\n    18→| `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` | Forwarded as env var | Not needed | Claude Code may use API key auth |\n    19→| `~/.ssh/` | Mounted (ro) | Mounted (ro) | Both paths: git push/pull from container |\n    20→| `~/.gitconfig` | Mounted (ro) | Mounted (ro) | Both paths: git identity for commits |\n    21→| `~/.config/gh/` | Mounted (ro) | Mounted (ro) | Both paths: `gh` CLI for PR creation |\n    22→| AI provider keys (OpenAI, etc.) | N/A | Stays on host | `opencode serve` handles on host |\n    23→\n    24→### Credential Provider Interface\n    25→\n    26→```python\n    27→class CredentialProvider:\n    28→    name: str                    # e.g., \"claude_auth\"\n    29→    display_name: str            # e.g., \"Claude Code Auth\"\n    30→    description: str             # e.g., \"OAuth tokens and session state for Claude Code\"\n    31→    applies_to: list[str]        # [\"claude\"] or [\"claude\", \"opencode\"] or [\"*\"]\n    32→\n    33→    def detect(self) -> CredentialDetection:\n    34→        \"\"\"Check if this credential exists on the host.\n    35→        Returns detection result with source location and method.\"\"\"\n    36→\n    37→    def get_docker_config(self) -> DockerCredentialConfig:\n    38→        \"\"\"Generate Docker mount/env configuration for this credential.\n    39→        Only called if credential is detected and enabled.\"\"\"\n    40→\n    41→    def get_validation_command(self) -> str:\n    42→        \"\"\"Return a shell command to run inside the container to verify\n    43→        the credential is accessible and functional.\"\"\"\n    44→```\n    45→\n    46→### Built-In Providers\n    47→\n    48→#### ClaudeAuthProvider\n    49→- **Applies to**: Claude Code loops only\n    50→- **Detects**: `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` env var, then `~/.claude/` directory\n    51→- **Docker config**:\n    52→  - If env var: passes as `-e ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...`\n    53→  - Config dir: mounts `~/.claude/` → `/home/{user}/.claude/` (read-write)\n    54→  - **Must be read-write**: Claude Code writes session state, token cache, and settings to this directory. Read-only mount causes errors.\n    55→- **Validation**: `claude --version` (confirms CLI + auth)\n    56→- **Platform notes**:\n    57→  - Windows: `C:\\Users\\{user}\\.claude\\`\n    58→  - Linux/macOS: `~/.claude/`\n    59→\n    60→#### GitSshProvider\n    61→- **Applies to**: All loops (`[\"*\"]`)\n    62→- **Detects**: `~/.ssh/` directory with key files (`id_rsa`, `id_ed25519`, etc.)\n    63→- **Docker config**: mounts `~/.ssh/` → `/home/{user}/.ssh/` (read-only)\n    64→- **Validation**: `ssh -T git@github.com` (or configured remote host)\n    65→- **Platform notes**:\n    66→  - Windows: `C:\\Users\\{user}\\.ssh\\`\n    67→  - Linux/macOS: `~/.ssh/`\n    68→\n    69→#### GitConfigProvider\n    70→- **Applies to**: All loops (`[\"*\"]`)\n    71→- **Detects**: `~/.gitconfig` file\n    72→- **Docker config**: mounts `~/.gitconfig` → `/home/{user}/.gitconfig` (read-only)\n    73→- **Validation**: `git config user.name && git config user.email`\n    74→- **Platform notes**:\n    75→  - Windows: `C:\\Users\\{user}\\.gitconfig`\n    76→  - Linux/macOS: `~/.gitconfig`\n    77→\n    78→#### GitHubCliProvider\n    79→- **Applies to**: All loops (`[\"*\"]`)\n    80→- **Detects**: `~/.config/gh/` directory (Linux/macOS) or `%APPDATA%\\GitHub CLI\\` (Windows)\n    81→- **Docker config**: mounts config dir → `/home/{user}/.config/gh/` (read-only)\n    82→- **Validation**: `gh auth status`\n    83→\n    84→#### CustomMountProvider\n    85→- **User-defined** mounts from settings\n    86→- **Detects**: checks if the host path exists\n    87→- **Docker config**: mounts as specified (user provides host path, container path, mode)\n    88→- **Validation**: `test -r {container_path}` (simple readability check)\n    89→\n    90→### Detection Result\n    91→\n    92→```python\n    93→@dataclass\n    94→class CredentialDetection:\n    95→    found: bool\n    96→    method: str           # \"env_var\", \"config_dir\", \"config_file\", \"not_found\"\n    97→    source_path: str      # Host path or env var name\n    98→    display_info: str     # Human-readable: \"Found via env var ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\"\n    99→```\n   100→\n   101→### Docker Credential Config\n   102→\n   103→```python\n   104→@dataclass\n   105→class DockerCredentialConfig:\n   106→    env_vars: dict[str, str]           # -e KEY=VALUE\n   107→    mounts: list[DockerMount]          # -v host:container:mode\n   108→\n   109→@dataclass\n   110→class DockerMount:\n   111→    host_path: str       # Absolute path on host (pre-translation)\n   112→    container_path: str  # Path inside container\n   113→    mode: str            # \"ro\" or \"rw\"\n   114→```\n   115→\n   116→### Path Translation\n   117→\n   118→Each provider uses a `PathTranslator` that auto-converts host paths to Docker-compatible mount paths:\n   119→\n   120→```python\n   121→class PathTranslator:\n   122→    def translate(self, host_path: str) -> str:\n   123→        \"\"\"Convert host path to Docker bind mount path.\n   124→\n   125→        Windows: C:\\\\Users\\\\Grove\\\\.ssh → /c/Users/Grove/.ssh\n   126→        WSL:     /mnt/c/Users/Grove/.ssh (no change needed)\n   127→        Linux:   /home/user/.ssh (no change needed)\n   128→        macOS:   /Users/user/.ssh (no change needed)\n   129→        \"\"\"\n   130→```\n   131→\n   132→### UID/GID Matching\n   133→\n   134→Critical for bind mount file permissions. The container user must match the host user's UID/GID:\n   135→\n   136→```python\n   137→def get_host_uid_gid() -> tuple[int, int]:\n   138→    \"\"\"Get the current user's UID and GID.\n   139→\n   140→    Windows/WSL2: Docker Desktop handles translation (use defaults 1000:1000)\n   141→    Linux: os.getuid(), os.getgid()\n   142→    macOS: os.getuid(), os.getgid()\n   143→    \"\"\"\n   144→```\n   145→\n   146→The claudebox Dockerfile already accepts `USER_ID` and `GROUP_ID` build args. Vista passes the host user's IDs when building the image.\n   147→\n   148→### Settings Schema\n   149→\n   150→```json\n   151→{\n   152→  \"ralph\": {\n   153→    \"sandbox\": {\n   154→      \"credentials\": {\n   155→        \"claude_auth\": true,\n   156→        \"git_ssh\": true,\n   157→        \"git_config\": true,\n   158→        \"github_cli\": false,\n   159→        \"custom\": []\n   160→      }\n   161→    }\n   162→  }\n   163→}\n   164→```\n   165→\n   166→- `true` = enabled (provider will detect and mount)\n   167→- `false` = disabled (credential not shared, even if detected)\n   168→- Custom entries are always evaluated if present\n   169→- Providers with `applies_to` that don't match the current loop provider are skipped automatically\n   170→\n   171→### Credential Gathering at Loop Start\n   172→\n   173→```python\n   174→def gather_credentials(provider_name: str, settings: dict) -> list[DockerCredentialConfig]:\n   175→    \"\"\"Collect Docker credential configs for a loop.\n   176→\n   177→    1. Iterate all built-in providers\n   178→    2. Skip providers where applies_to doesn't match provider_name\n   179→    3. Skip providers disabled in settings\n   180→    4. Run detect() on remaining providers\n   181→    5. For detected providers, call get_docker_config()\n   182→    6. Return list of configs to apply to container\n   183→    \"\"\"\n   184→```\n   185→\n   186→### Credential Validation Flow\n   187→\n   188→Runs automatically at Vista startup when `sandbox.enabled = true`, and available via internal API (`POST /api/sandbox/credentials/validate`):\n   189→\n   190→1. Vista collects all enabled providers\n   191→2. Each enabled provider runs `detect()` — results logged (found/not found)\n   192→3. Vista creates a temporary container with credential mounts from all detected+enabled providers\n   193→4. For each provider, runs `get_validation_command()` inside the container\n   194→5. Collects pass/fail results\n   195→6. Logs structured report to Vista server output (and returns via API if called programmatically)\n   196→7. Tears down temporary container\n   197→\n   198→## Edge Cases\n   199→\n   200→- **`~/.claude/` mounted read-only**: Claude Code writes session state here. Must be read-write or Claude Code will error. This differs from claudebox which uses a copy-per-project pattern — for ralph loops, direct rw mount is simpler.\n   201→- **Credential detected but mount fails**: Docker may reject certain paths (permissions, symlinks). Validation catches this.\n   202→- **Env var vs file for same credential**: Provider prefers env var if both exist (simpler Docker config).\n   203→- **SSH agent forwarding**: Not supported in v1. Only file-based SSH keys are mounted.\n   204→- **Windows Credential Manager**: Git credentials stored in Windows Credential Manager are not directly mountable. Users need SSH keys or `.git-credentials` file instead.\n   205→- **Docker not running**: All detection still works (detection is host-side). Mounting and validation fail with clear \"Docker not running\" error.\n   206→- **OpenCode loop with claude_auth enabled**: Provider is skipped because `applies_to: [\"claude\"]` doesn't match. No error.\n   207→\n   208→## Dependencies\n   209→\n   210→- `vista/server/config.py` - Settings loading for credential toggle states\n   211→- Spec: [container-lifecycle](container-lifecycle.md) - Creates containers with credential mounts\n   212→- Spec: [dashboard-ui](dashboard-ui.md) - Sandbox toggle (no credential UI in this phase)\n   213→\n   214→## Testing Strategy\n   215→\n   216→- Unit tests per provider: detection logic with mocked filesystem/env\n   217→- Unit tests for path translation: Windows, Linux, macOS paths\n   218→- Unit tests for Docker config generation: correct `-v` and `-e` flags\n   219→- Unit tests for `applies_to` filtering (Claude-only creds skipped for OpenCode loops)\n   220→- Unit tests for UID/GID detection per platform\n   221→- Integration test: full validation flow with real Docker container\n   222→- Platform-specific tests: Windows path detection, Linux path detection\n   223→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6fe45d16-ab3a-4e41-9b98-035326f9b7c3","uuid":"0dc79f83-f63e-481f-8b1d-25020f5215fa","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/.vista/features/docker-sandbox/specs/credential-management.md","content":"# Spec: Credential Management\n\n## Problem Statement\n\nDocker containers need host credentials to function: Claude Code needs OAuth tokens and API keys, git needs SSH keys and identity config. The challenge is mounting these automatically without user intervention, handling platform differences (Windows vs Linux vs macOS), and validating that mounted credentials actually work inside the container.\n\nWith the split execution model, OpenCode loops do NOT need AI credentials in the container — `opencode serve` runs on the host with native auth. This dramatically simplifies the credential story.\n\n## Proposed Solution\n\nA **credential provider** pattern where each provider encapsulates the logic to detect, mount, and validate a specific credential type. Providers are scoped to what's actually needed in the container — git/SSH credentials (both paths) and Claude auth (Claude Code path only).\n\n### What Goes in the Container vs What Stays on Host\n\n| Credential | Claude Code Loops | OpenCode Loops | Why |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `~/.claude/` (OAuth + session) | Mounted (rw) | Not needed | Claude Code runs inside container |\n| `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` | Forwarded as env var | Not needed | Claude Code may use API key auth |\n| `~/.ssh/` | Mounted (ro) | Mounted (ro) | Both paths: git push/pull from container |\n| `~/.gitconfig` | Mounted (ro) | Mounted (ro) | Both paths: git identity for commits |\n| `~/.config/gh/` | Mounted (ro) | Mounted (ro) | Both paths: `gh` CLI for PR creation |\n| AI provider keys (OpenAI, etc.) | N/A | Stays on host | `opencode serve` handles on host |\n\n### Credential Provider Interface\n\n```python\nclass CredentialProvider:\n    name: str                    # e.g., \"claude_auth\"\n    display_name: str            # e.g., \"Claude Code Auth\"\n    description: str             # e.g., \"OAuth tokens and session state for Claude Code\"\n    applies_to: list[str]        # [\"claude\"] or [\"claude\", \"opencode\"] or [\"*\"]\n\n    def detect(self) -> CredentialDetection:\n        \"\"\"Check if this credential exists on the host.\n        Returns detection result with source location and method.\"\"\"\n\n    def get_docker_config(self) -> DockerCredentialConfig:\n        \"\"\"Generate Docker mount/env configuration for this credential.\n        Only called if credential is detected and enabled.\"\"\"\n\n    def get_validation_command(self) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Return a shell command to run inside the container to verify\n        the credential is accessible and functional.\"\"\"\n```\n\n### Built-In Providers\n\n#### ClaudeAuthProvider\n- **Applies to**: Claude Code loops only\n- **Detects**: `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` env var, then `~/.claude/` directory\n- **Docker config**:\n  - If env var: passes as `-e ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...`\n  - Config dir: mounts `~/.claude/` → `/home/{user}/.claude/` (read-write)\n  - **Must be read-write**: Claude Code writes session state, token cache, and settings to this directory. Read-only mount causes errors.\n- **Validation**: `claude --version` (confirms CLI + auth)\n- **Platform notes**:\n  - Windows: `C:\\Users\\{user}\\.claude\\`\n  - Linux/macOS: `~/.claude/`\n\n#### GitSshProvider\n- **Applies to**: All loops (`[\"*\"]`)\n- **Detects**: `~/.ssh/` directory with key files (`id_rsa`, `id_ed25519`, etc.)\n- **Docker config**: mounts `~/.ssh/` → `/home/{user}/.ssh/` (read-only)\n- **Validation**: `ssh -T git@github.com` (or configured remote host)\n- **Platform notes**:\n  - Windows: `C:\\Users\\{user}\\.ssh\\`\n  - Linux/macOS: `~/.ssh/`\n\n#### GitConfigProvider\n- **Applies to**: All loops (`[\"*\"]`)\n- **Detects**: `~/.gitconfig` file\n- **Docker config**: mounts `~/.gitconfig` → `/home/{user}/.gitconfig` (read-only)\n- **Validation**: `git config user.name && git config user.email`\n- **Platform notes**:\n  - Windows: `C:\\Users\\{user}\\.gitconfig`\n  - Linux/macOS: `~/.gitconfig`\n\n#### GitHubCliProvider\n- **Applies to**: All loops (`[\"*\"]`)\n- **Detects**: `~/.config/gh/` directory (Linux/macOS) or `%APPDATA%\\GitHub CLI\\` (Windows)\n- **Docker config**: mounts config dir → `/home/{user}/.config/gh/` (read-only)\n- **Validation**: `gh auth status`\n\n#### CustomMountProvider\n- **User-defined** mounts from settings\n- **Detects**: checks if the host path exists\n- **Docker config**: mounts as specified (user provides host path, container path, mode)\n- **Validation**: `test -r {container_path}` (simple readability check)\n\n### Detection Result\n\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass CredentialDetection:\n    found: bool\n    method: str           # \"env_var\", \"config_dir\", \"config_file\", \"not_found\"\n    source_path: str      # Host path or env var name\n    display_info: str     # Human-readable: \"Found via env var ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\"\n```\n\n### Docker Credential Config\n\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass DockerCredentialConfig:\n    env_vars: dict[str, str]           # -e KEY=VALUE\n    mounts: list[DockerMount]          # -v host:container:mode\n\n@dataclass\nclass DockerMount:\n    host_path: str       # Absolute path on host (pre-translation)\n    container_path: str  # Path inside container\n    mode: str            # \"ro\" or \"rw\"\n```\n\n### Path Translation\n\nEach provider uses a `PathTranslator` that auto-converts host paths to Docker-compatible mount paths:\n\n```python\nclass PathTranslator:\n    def translate(self, host_path: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Convert host path to Docker bind mount path.\n\n        Windows: C:\\\\Users\\\\Grove\\\\.ssh → /c/Users/Grove/.ssh\n        WSL:     /mnt/c/Users/Grove/.ssh (no change needed)\n        Linux:   /home/user/.ssh (no change needed)\n        macOS:   /Users/user/.ssh (no change needed)\n        \"\"\"\n```\n\n### UID/GID Matching\n\nCritical for bind mount file permissions. The container user must match the host user's UID/GID:\n\n```python\ndef get_host_uid_gid() -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"Get the current user's UID and GID.\n\n    Windows/WSL2: Docker Desktop handles translation (use defaults 1000:1000)\n    Linux: os.getuid(), os.getgid()\n    macOS: os.getuid(), os.getgid()\n    \"\"\"\n```\n\nThe claudebox Dockerfile already accepts `USER_ID` and `GROUP_ID` build args. Vista passes the host user's IDs when building the image.\n\n### Settings Schema\n\n```json\n{\n  \"ralph\": {\n    \"sandbox\": {\n      \"credentials\": {\n        \"claude_auth\": true,\n        \"git_ssh\": true,\n        \"git_config\": true,\n        \"github_cli\": false,\n        \"custom\": []\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n- `true` = enabled (provider will detect and mount)\n- `false` = disabled (credential not shared, even if detected)\n- Custom entries are always evaluated if present\n- Providers with `applies_to` that don't match the current loop provider are skipped automatically\n\n### Credential Gathering at Loop Start\n\n```python\ndef gather_credentials(provider_name: str, settings: dict) -> list[DockerCredentialConfig]:\n    \"\"\"Collect Docker credential configs for a loop.\n\n    1. Iterate all built-in providers\n    2. Skip providers where applies_to doesn't match provider_name\n    3. Skip providers disabled in settings\n    4. Run detect() on remaining providers\n    5. For detected providers, call get_docker_config()\n    6. Return list of configs to apply to container\n    \"\"\"\n```\n\n### Credential Validation Flow\n\nRuns automatically at Vista startup when `sandbox.enabled = true`, and available via internal API (`POST /api/sandbox/credentials/validate`):\n\n1. Vista collects all enabled providers\n2. Each enabled provider runs `detect()` — results logged (found/not found)\n3. Vista creates a temporary container with credential mounts from all detected+enabled providers\n4. For each provider, runs `get_validation_command()` inside the container\n5. Collects pass/fail results\n6. Logs structured report to Vista server output (and returns via API if called programmatically)\n7. Tears down temporary container\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- **`~/.claude/` mounted read-only**: Claude Code writes session state here. Must be read-write or Claude Code will error. This differs from claudebox which uses a copy-per-project pattern — for ralph loops, direct rw mount is simpler.\n- **Credential detected but mount fails**: Docker may reject certain paths (permissions, symlinks). Validation catches this.\n- **Env var vs file for same credential**: Provider prefers env var if both exist (simpler Docker config).\n- **SSH agent forwarding**: Not supported in v1. Only file-based SSH keys are mounted.\n- **Windows Credential Manager**: Git credentials stored in Windows Credential Manager are not directly mountable. Users need SSH keys or `.git-credentials` file instead.\n- **Docker not running**: All detection still works (detection is host-side). Mounting and validation fail with clear \"Docker not running\" error.\n- **OpenCode loop with claude_auth enabled**: Provider is skipped because `applies_to: [\"claude\"]` doesn't match. No error.\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- `vista/server/config.py` - Settings loading for credential toggle states\n- Spec: [container-lifecycle](container-lifecycle.md) - Creates containers with credential mounts\n- Spec: [dashboard-ui](dashboard-ui.md) - Sandbox toggle (no credential UI in this phase)\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n- Unit tests per provider: detection logic with mocked filesystem/env\n- Unit tests for path translation: Windows, Linux, macOS paths\n- Unit tests for Docker config generation: correct `-v` and `-e` flags\n- Unit tests for `applies_to` filtering (Claude-only creds skipped for OpenCode loops)\n- Unit tests for UID/GID detection per platform\n- Integration test: full validation flow with real Docker container\n- Platform-specific tests: Windows path detection, Linux path detection\n","numLines":223,"startLine":1,"totalLines":223}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01VpJJWqjAVvuWCq1PYwLBux","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011ZhyjLkEEx6FMaNNz3HUSs","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/.vista/features/docker-sandbox/specs/dashboard-ui.md"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":217,"cache_read_input_tokens":48904,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":217},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6fe45d16-ab3a-4e41-9b98-035326f9b7c3","uuid":"6a849859-c94d-46e4-a0aa-444d7cfbec26"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011ZhyjLkEEx6FMaNNz3HUSs","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Spec: Dashboard UI for Sandbox Settings\n     2→\n     3→## Problem Statement\n     4→\n     5→Users need a simple way to enable or disable Docker sandboxing for ralph loops. The dashboard should surface a single toggle and provide clear inline feedback when something is wrong (e.g., Docker not installed or not running). Advanced sandbox configuration (credentials, profiles, model defaults, container controls, opencode serve management) is handled via `settings.json` — not the dashboard — in this phase.\n     6→\n     7→## Proposed Solution\n     8→\n     9→A single **toggle control** in the Vista dashboard's Ralph settings area, bound to `ralph.sandbox.enabled`. Optionally, inline status text next to the toggle communicates readiness or errors.\n    10→\n    11→### UI Layout\n    12→\n    13→```\n    14→┌─ Ralph Settings ───────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n    15→│                                                                 │\n    16→│  ...existing ralph settings (provider, model, iterations)...    │\n    17→│                                                                 │\n    18→│  Docker Sandbox  [toggle: OFF]                                  │\n    19→│                                                                 │\n    20→│  ─── When toggled ON: ─────────────────────────────────────── │\n    21→│                                                                 │\n    22→│  Docker Sandbox  [toggle: ON]   ● Docker running                │\n    23→│                                                                 │\n    24→│  ─── Or, if Docker is unavailable: ───────────────────────── │\n    25→│                                                                 │\n    26→│  Docker Sandbox  [toggle: ON]   ✕ Docker not running            │\n    27→│                                    Install Docker Desktop and   │\n    28→│                                    ensure it is running.        │\n    29→│                                                                 │\n    30→│  ─── Or, if image not built: ─────────────────────────────── │\n    31→│                                                                 │\n    32→│  Docker Sandbox  [toggle: ON]   ● Building image...             │\n    33→│                                                                 │\n    34→└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n    35→```\n    36→\n    37→### Behavior\n    38→\n    39→#### Toggle\n    40→\n    41→- Reads and writes `ralph.sandbox.enabled` in `settings.json`\n    42→- Default state: OFF\n    43→- Toggling ON triggers an immediate Docker availability check\n    44→- Toggling OFF requires no validation — loops revert to direct subprocess execution\n    45→\n    46→#### Inline Status Text\n    47→\n    48→Displayed next to the toggle only when sandbox is enabled. Shows one of:\n    49→\n    50→| Condition | Status Text | Style |\n    51→|-----------|-------------|-------|\n    52→| Docker running + image built | `Docker running` | Green dot |\n    53→| Docker running + image not built | `Building image...` | Amber dot (auto-builds on first enable) |\n    54→| Docker installed but not running | `Docker not running` | Red dot + guidance text |\n    55→| Docker not installed | `Docker Desktop required` | Red dot + install guidance |\n    56→\n    57→Status is checked:\n    58→1. On page load (if toggle is ON)\n    59→2. Immediately when toggle is switched ON\n    60→3. No polling — manual page refresh for updated status\n    61→\n    62→#### What Is NOT in the Dashboard\n    63→\n    64→The following are configured via `settings.json` only (not surfaced in the dashboard in this phase):\n    65→\n    66→- Credential toggles and custom mounts (`sandbox.credentials.*`)\n    67→- Access profiles (`sandbox.profiles.*`)\n    68→- Model-to-profile defaults (`sandbox.model_defaults`)\n    69→- Image name override (`sandbox.image`)\n    70→- Network policy (`sandbox.network`)\n    71→- OpenCode serve port and auto-start (`sandbox.opencode_serve.*`)\n    72→- Container listing, start/stop controls\n    73→- Credential validation (\"Test Credentials\")\n    74→- Image rebuild button\n    75→\n    76→These features are fully functional via the settings file and internal API, but are deferred from the dashboard UI to keep the initial experience minimal.\n    77→\n    78→### API Endpoints\n    79→\n    80→```\n    81→GET  /api/sandbox/status\n    82→  Returns: { docker_available, docker_running, image_built, image_name }\n    83→  Used by: Dashboard toggle to show inline status\n    84→\n    85→PUT  /api/sandbox/settings\n    86→  Body: { \"enabled\": true|false }\n    87→  Returns: validation result\n    88→  Used by: Dashboard toggle to persist state\n    89→```\n    90→\n    91→All other sandbox API endpoints (credential validation, container listing, serve management, image build) exist as internal APIs for programmatic use but are not called by the dashboard in this phase.\n    92→\n    93→### Detection on Page Load\n    94→\n    95→When the Ralph settings section loads:\n    96→\n    97→1. Read current `sandbox.enabled` state → set toggle position\n    98→2. If enabled, call `GET /api/sandbox/status` → display inline status text\n    99→3. If disabled, no status check needed\n   100→\n   101→### Save Flow\n   102→\n   103→1. User flips the toggle\n   104→2. Frontend sends `PUT /api/sandbox/settings` with `{ \"enabled\": true }` or `{ \"enabled\": false }`\n   105→3. Backend writes to `settings.json`\n   106→4. If enabling: also calls status check and displays result inline\n   107→5. If disabling: clears inline status text\n   108→\n   109→## Edge Cases\n   110→\n   111→- **Docker not installed**: Toggle can be switched ON, but inline status shows \"Docker Desktop required\" with install guidance. Loops will fail at container creation time with a clear error.\n   112→- **Docker not running**: Toggle can be switched ON, but inline status shows \"Docker not running.\" User must start Docker Desktop themselves.\n   113→- **Settings file locked**: Save fails with generic \"Could not write settings\" error.\n   114→- **Image auto-build on first enable**: When sandbox is first enabled and no image exists, Vista queues an image build. Status shows \"Building image...\" until complete.\n   115→\n   116→## Dependencies\n   117→\n   118→- `vista/server/routes/` — Sandbox status endpoint\n   119→- `vista/server/views/` — Toggle control in Ralph settings area\n   120→- Spec: [settings](settings.md) — Reads/writes `ralph.sandbox.enabled`\n   121→\n   122→## Testing Strategy\n   123→\n   124→- API test: `GET /api/sandbox/status` returns correct Docker and image state\n   125→- API test: `PUT /api/sandbox/settings` with `enabled: true` and `enabled: false`\n   126→- Frontend test: toggle renders correct state from settings\n   127→- Frontend test: inline status text appears when enabled, hidden when disabled\n   128→- Frontend test: error states display actionable guidance\n   129→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6fe45d16-ab3a-4e41-9b98-035326f9b7c3","uuid":"9f310f4f-d9ef-4d4d-a191-7925e7e72c0c","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/.vista/features/docker-sandbox/specs/dashboard-ui.md","content":"# Spec: Dashboard UI for Sandbox Settings\n\n## Problem Statement\n\nUsers need a simple way to enable or disable Docker sandboxing for ralph loops. The dashboard should surface a single toggle and provide clear inline feedback when something is wrong (e.g., Docker not installed or not running). Advanced sandbox configuration (credentials, profiles, model defaults, container controls, opencode serve management) is handled via `settings.json` — not the dashboard — in this phase.\n\n## Proposed Solution\n\nA single **toggle control** in the Vista dashboard's Ralph settings area, bound to `ralph.sandbox.enabled`. Optionally, inline status text next to the toggle communicates readiness or errors.\n\n### UI Layout\n\n```\n┌─ Ralph Settings ───────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                                                                 │\n│  ...existing ralph settings (provider, model, iterations)...    │\n│                                                                 │\n│  Docker Sandbox  [toggle: OFF]                                  │\n│                                                                 │\n│  ─── When toggled ON: ─────────────────────────────────────── │\n│                                                                 │\n│  Docker Sandbox  [toggle: ON]   ● Docker running                │\n│                                                                 │\n│  ─── Or, if Docker is unavailable: ───────────────────────── │\n│                                                                 │\n│  Docker Sandbox  [toggle: ON]   ✕ Docker not running            │\n│                                    Install Docker Desktop and   │\n│                                    ensure it is running.        │\n│                                                                 │\n│  ─── Or, if image not built: ─────────────────────────────── │\n│                                                                 │\n│  Docker Sandbox  [toggle: ON]   ● Building image...             │\n│                                                                 │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Behavior\n\n#### Toggle\n\n- Reads and writes `ralph.sandbox.enabled` in `settings.json`\n- Default state: OFF\n- Toggling ON triggers an immediate Docker availability check\n- Toggling OFF requires no validation — loops revert to direct subprocess execution\n\n#### Inline Status Text\n\nDisplayed next to the toggle only when sandbox is enabled. Shows one of:\n\n| Condition | Status Text | Style |\n|-----------|-------------|-------|\n| Docker running + image built | `Docker running` | Green dot |\n| Docker running + image not built | `Building image...` | Amber dot (auto-builds on first enable) |\n| Docker installed but not running | `Docker not running` | Red dot + guidance text |\n| Docker not installed | `Docker Desktop required` | Red dot + install guidance |\n\nStatus is checked:\n1. On page load (if toggle is ON)\n2. Immediately when toggle is switched ON\n3. No polling — manual page refresh for updated status\n\n#### What Is NOT in the Dashboard\n\nThe following are configured via `settings.json` only (not surfaced in the dashboard in this phase):\n\n- Credential toggles and custom mounts (`sandbox.credentials.*`)\n- Access profiles (`sandbox.profiles.*`)\n- Model-to-profile defaults (`sandbox.model_defaults`)\n- Image name override (`sandbox.image`)\n- Network policy (`sandbox.network`)\n- OpenCode serve port and auto-start (`sandbox.opencode_serve.*`)\n- Container listing, start/stop controls\n- Credential validation (\"Test Credentials\")\n- Image rebuild button\n\nThese features are fully functional via the settings file and internal API, but are deferred from the dashboard UI to keep the initial experience minimal.\n\n### API Endpoints\n\n```\nGET  /api/sandbox/status\n  Returns: { docker_available, docker_running, image_built, image_name }\n  Used by: Dashboard toggle to show inline status\n\nPUT  /api/sandbox/settings\n  Body: { \"enabled\": true|false }\n  Returns: validation result\n  Used by: Dashboard toggle to persist state\n```\n\nAll other sandbox API endpoints (credential validation, container listing, serve management, image build) exist as internal APIs for programmatic use but are not called by the dashboard in this phase.\n\n### Detection on Page Load\n\nWhen the Ralph settings section loads:\n\n1. Read current `sandbox.enabled` state → set toggle position\n2. If enabled, call `GET /api/sandbox/status` → display inline status text\n3. If disabled, no status check needed\n\n### Save Flow\n\n1. User flips the toggle\n2. Frontend sends `PUT /api/sandbox/settings` with `{ \"enabled\": true }` or `{ \"enabled\": false }`\n3. Backend writes to `settings.json`\n4. If enabling: also calls status check and displays result inline\n5. If disabling: clears inline status text\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- **Docker not installed**: Toggle can be switched ON, but inline status shows \"Docker Desktop required\" with install guidance. Loops will fail at container creation time with a clear error.\n- **Docker not running**: Toggle can be switched ON, but inline status shows \"Docker not running.\" User must start Docker Desktop themselves.\n- **Settings file locked**: Save fails with generic \"Could not write settings\" error.\n- **Image auto-build on first enable**: When sandbox is first enabled and no image exists, Vista queues an image build. Status shows \"Building image...\" until complete.\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- `vista/server/routes/` — Sandbox status endpoint\n- `vista/server/views/` — Toggle control in Ralph settings area\n- Spec: [settings](settings.md) — Reads/writes `ralph.sandbox.enabled`\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n- API test: `GET /api/sandbox/status` returns correct Docker and image state\n- API test: `PUT /api/sandbox/settings` with `enabled: true` and `enabled: false`\n- Frontend test: toggle renders correct state from settings\n- Frontend test: inline status text appears when enabled, hidden when disabled\n- Frontend test: error states display actionable guidance\n","numLines":129,"startLine":1,"totalLines":129}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01VpJJWqjAVvuWCq1PYwLBux","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YXeEqNzjJhLRU1MFknr6mz","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/.vista/features/docker-sandbox/specs/access-profiles.md"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":217,"cache_read_input_tokens":48904,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":217},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6fe45d16-ab3a-4e41-9b98-035326f9b7c3","uuid":"5e277341-356c-408a-9174-e6be0e8dbea1"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YXeEqNzjJhLRU1MFknr6mz","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Spec: Access Profiles\n     2→\n     3→## Problem Statement\n     4→\n     5→While the default sandbox behavior mounts the full project root (giving agents complete project access including feature specs), some use cases benefit from restricting what the agent can see. A cheap model doing research might only need read-only access, while an expensive model needs full read-write. Named profiles provide this flexibility without changing the default full-access behavior.\n     6→\n     7→## Proposed Solution\n     8→\n     9→Named **access profiles** stored in settings, each defining a set of directory mounts with access modes and an optional network policy override. The default profile is `full-access` (entire project root, read-write), which ensures agents can always reference feature specs, source code, and the full project context.\n    10→\n    11→> **Current phase:** Profiles are a configuration-level concept managed via `settings.json`. They are not exposed in the dashboard UI. The dashboard provides only a sandbox enable/disable toggle. Power users can define custom profiles by editing `settings.json` directly.\n    12→\n    13→### Profile Definition\n    14→\n    15→```python\n    16→@dataclass\n    17→class MountSpec:\n    18→    path: str        # Relative to project root, supports ${FEATURE} variable\n    19→    mode: str        # \"rw\" or \"ro\"\n    20→\n    21→@dataclass\n    22→class AccessProfile:\n    23→    name: str\n    24→    mounts: list[MountSpec]\n    25→    network: bool | None  # None = inherit global setting\n    26→```\n    27→\n    28→### Built-In Profiles\n    29→\n    30→#### `full-access` (DEFAULT)\n    31→Full project directory, read-write. The agent sees everything in the project including feature specs, architecture docs, source code, tests, and git history.\n    32→\n    33→```json\n    34→{\n    35→  \"mounts\": [\n    36→    { \"path\": \".\", \"mode\": \"rw\" }\n    37→  ]\n    38→}\n    39→```\n    40→\n    41→**Mounted as:** project root → `/workspace/`\n    42→\n    43→This is the default for all loops. Agents can always access:\n    44→- `.vista/features/{slug}/` — feature specs, PRDs, architecture docs\n    45→- `.vista/ralph/{slug}/` — job directories, progress files\n    46→- `src/`, `tests/`, etc. — full source tree\n    47→- `.git/` — commit and push capability\n    48→- `CLAUDE.md` — project instructions\n    49→\n    50→#### `feature-scoped`\n    51→Only the feature directory, source code, and git. Agent cannot see other features, configs outside src, etc.\n    52→\n    53→```json\n    54→{\n    55→  \"mounts\": [\n    56→    { \"path\": \".vista/features/${FEATURE}\", \"mode\": \"rw\" },\n    57→    { \"path\": \".vista/ralph/${FEATURE}\", \"mode\": \"rw\" },\n    58→    { \"path\": \"src\", \"mode\": \"rw\" },\n    59→    { \"path\": \"tests\", \"mode\": \"rw\" },\n    60→    { \"path\": \".git\", \"mode\": \"rw\" }\n    61→  ]\n    62→}\n    63→```\n    64→\n    65→**Mounted as:** Each path becomes a subdirectory under `/workspace/`. Only these subdirectories exist.\n    66→\n    67→**Variable substitution:** `${FEATURE}` is replaced with the feature/slug name at loop start time.\n    68→\n    69→#### `research-only`\n    70→Full project, read-only. No writes, no network. For exploratory/analytical loops.\n    71→\n    72→```json\n    73→{\n    74→  \"mounts\": [\n    75→    { \"path\": \".\", \"mode\": \"ro\" }\n    76→  ],\n    77→  \"network\": false\n    78→}\n    79→```\n    80→\n    81→**Note:** `research-only` with `network: false` will NOT work for OpenCode loops, since those require network access to reach `host.docker.internal`. It works for Claude Code loops only (Claude Code runs natively in the container with `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` mounted).\n    82→\n    83→### Profile Resolution\n    84→\n    85→When a ralph loop starts, the profile is resolved through this priority chain:\n    86→\n    87→```\n    88→1. Explicit override (user/LLM specifies profile in ralph_start)\n    89→   ↓ (if not specified)\n    90→2. Model default (from sandbox.model_defaults)\n    91→   ↓ (if model not in defaults)\n    92→3. Fallback: \"full-access\"\n    93→```\n    94→\n    95→```python\n    96→def resolve_profile(explicit: str | None, model: str, settings: dict) -> AccessProfile:\n    97→    if explicit:\n    98→        return settings[\"sandbox\"][\"profiles\"][explicit]\n    99→\n   100→    model_defaults = settings[\"sandbox\"].get(\"model_defaults\", {})\n   101→    if model in model_defaults:\n   102→        return settings[\"sandbox\"][\"profiles\"][model_defaults[model]]\n   103→\n   104→    return settings[\"sandbox\"][\"profiles\"][\"full-access\"]\n   105→```\n   106→\n   107→### Model Defaults\n   108→\n   109→Maps model names to profile names:\n   110→\n   111→```json\n   112→{\n   113→  \"sandbox\": {\n   114→    \"model_defaults\": {\n   115→      \"haiku\": \"feature-scoped\",\n   116→      \"sonnet\": \"full-access\",\n   117→      \"opus\": \"full-access\"\n   118→    }\n   119→  }\n   120→}\n   121→```\n   122→\n   123→Models not listed fall back to `full-access`.\n   124→\n   125→### Variable Substitution\n   126→\n   127→Profile mount paths can contain variables that are resolved at loop start time:\n   128→\n   129→| Variable | Resolved To | Example |\n   130→|----------|-------------|---------|\n   131→| `${FEATURE}` | Feature name / slug | `my-feature` |\n   132→| `${PROJECT_ROOT}` | Absolute project root path | `/workspace` (always this inside container) |\n   133→\n   134→### Mount Translation to Docker Volumes\n   135→\n   136→Each `MountSpec` is translated to a Docker bind mount:\n   137→\n   138→```python\n   139→def to_docker_mount(spec: MountSpec, project_root: Path, translator: PathTranslator) -> dict:\n   140→    host_path = project_root / spec.path  # Resolve relative to project\n   141→    docker_path = translator.translate(str(host_path))  # Platform translation\n   142→    container_path = f\"/workspace/{spec.path}\"  # Always under /workspace\n   143→\n   144→    return {\n   145→        \"host\": docker_path,\n   146→        \"container\": container_path,\n   147→        \"mode\": spec.mode,\n   148→    }\n   149→```\n   150→\n   151→**Special case for `\".\"`**: When path is `.`, mount the entire project root as `/workspace/`.\n   152→\n   153→### Validation Rules\n   154→\n   155→- A profile must have at least one mount\n   156→- Mount paths must be relative (no absolute paths or `..` traversal)\n   157→- Mount paths must resolve to locations within the project root\n   158→- If a mount path doesn't exist on the host at loop start time, it is skipped with a warning (not an error — the feature directory might not exist yet)\n   159→- Profile names must be alphanumeric + hyphens, no spaces\n   160→- `\"rw\"` and `\"ro\"` are the only valid modes\n   161→\n   162→### Network Policy\n   163→\n   164→Each profile can optionally override the global network policy:\n   165→\n   166→```json\n   167→{\n   168→  \"research-only\": {\n   169→    \"mounts\": [...],\n   170→    \"network\": false\n   171→  },\n   172→  \"full-access\": {\n   173→    \"mounts\": [...]\n   174→    // No \"network\" key: inherits global setting\n   175→  }\n   176→}\n   177→```\n   178→\n   179→Resolution: `profile.network ?? global_network_setting`\n   180→\n   181→**Constraint:** OpenCode sandbox loops always require network access (to reach `host.docker.internal`). If a profile disables network and the loop uses OpenCode, the loop will fail with a clear error: \"OpenCode sandbox loops require network access. Profile '{name}' has network disabled.\"\n   182→\n   183→## Edge Cases\n   184→\n   185→- **Mount path doesn't exist**: Skipped with warning. Agent sees the directory as missing inside the container.\n   186→- **Overlapping mounts**: If both `.` (full project) and `src/` are mounted, Docker handles this correctly.\n   187→- **`${FEATURE}` not provided**: If a profile uses `${FEATURE}` but the loop doesn't specify a feature name, error returned to caller.\n   188→- **Profile deleted while container running**: Container continues with current mounts. Container is per-loop so it's removed when loop finishes anyway.\n   189→- **Empty mount list**: Profile validation rejects this at settings save time.\n   190→- **`research-only` + OpenCode**: Fails with clear error (network required for OpenCode path).\n   191→\n   192→## Dependencies\n   193→\n   194→- Spec: [container-lifecycle](container-lifecycle.md) - Consumes profiles to create containers with correct mounts\n   195→- Spec: [settings](settings.md) - Profiles stored in `ralph.sandbox.profiles`\n   196→- Spec: [dashboard-ui](dashboard-ui.md) - Sandbox toggle only (no profile editor in this phase)\n   197→\n   198→## Testing Strategy\n   199→\n   200→- Unit tests for profile resolution (explicit > model default > fallback)\n   201→- Unit tests for variable substitution (`${FEATURE}`, `${PROJECT_ROOT}`)\n   202→- Unit tests for mount translation to Docker volumes\n   203→- Unit tests for validation rules (reject invalid paths, require at least one mount)\n   204→- Unit tests for network policy resolution (override vs inherit)\n   205→- Unit test: OpenCode + network-disabled profile fails with clear error\n   206→- Integration test: container with `full-access` profile can access all project files\n   207→- Integration test: container with `research-only` profile rejects writes\n   208→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6fe45d16-ab3a-4e41-9b98-035326f9b7c3","uuid":"fcc2b622-82d9-4b81-bbf7-339ea66764bc","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/.vista/features/docker-sandbox/specs/access-profiles.md","content":"# Spec: Access Profiles\n\n## Problem Statement\n\nWhile the default sandbox behavior mounts the full project root (giving agents complete project access including feature specs), some use cases benefit from restricting what the agent can see. A cheap model doing research might only need read-only access, while an expensive model needs full read-write. Named profiles provide this flexibility without changing the default full-access behavior.\n\n## Proposed Solution\n\nNamed **access profiles** stored in settings, each defining a set of directory mounts with access modes and an optional network policy override. The default profile is `full-access` (entire project root, read-write), which ensures agents can always reference feature specs, source code, and the full project context.\n\n> **Current phase:** Profiles are a configuration-level concept managed via `settings.json`. They are not exposed in the dashboard UI. The dashboard provides only a sandbox enable/disable toggle. Power users can define custom profiles by editing `settings.json` directly.\n\n### Profile Definition\n\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass MountSpec:\n    path: str        # Relative to project root, supports ${FEATURE} variable\n    mode: str        # \"rw\" or \"ro\"\n\n@dataclass\nclass AccessProfile:\n    name: str\n    mounts: list[MountSpec]\n    network: bool | None  # None = inherit global setting\n```\n\n### Built-In Profiles\n\n#### `full-access` (DEFAULT)\nFull project directory, read-write. The agent sees everything in the project including feature specs, architecture docs, source code, tests, and git history.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mounts\": [\n    { \"path\": \".\", \"mode\": \"rw\" }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n**Mounted as:** project root → `/workspace/`\n\nThis is the default for all loops. Agents can always access:\n- `.vista/features/{slug}/` — feature specs, PRDs, architecture docs\n- `.vista/ralph/{slug}/` — job directories, progress files\n- `src/`, `tests/`, etc. — full source tree\n- `.git/` — commit and push capability\n- `CLAUDE.md` — project instructions\n\n#### `feature-scoped`\nOnly the feature directory, source code, and git. Agent cannot see other features, configs outside src, etc.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mounts\": [\n    { \"path\": \".vista/features/${FEATURE}\", \"mode\": \"rw\" },\n    { \"path\": \".vista/ralph/${FEATURE}\", \"mode\": \"rw\" },\n    { \"path\": \"src\", \"mode\": \"rw\" },\n    { \"path\": \"tests\", \"mode\": \"rw\" },\n    { \"path\": \".git\", \"mode\": \"rw\" }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n**Mounted as:** Each path becomes a subdirectory under `/workspace/`. Only these subdirectories exist.\n\n**Variable substitution:** `${FEATURE}` is replaced with the feature/slug name at loop start time.\n\n#### `research-only`\nFull project, read-only. No writes, no network. For exploratory/analytical loops.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mounts\": [\n    { \"path\": \".\", \"mode\": \"ro\" }\n  ],\n  \"network\": false\n}\n```\n\n**Note:** `research-only` with `network: false` will NOT work for OpenCode loops, since those require network access to reach `host.docker.internal`. It works for Claude Code loops only (Claude Code runs natively in the container with `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` mounted).\n\n### Profile Resolution\n\nWhen a ralph loop starts, the profile is resolved through this priority chain:\n\n```\n1. Explicit override (user/LLM specifies profile in ralph_start)\n   ↓ (if not specified)\n2. Model default (from sandbox.model_defaults)\n   ↓ (if model not in defaults)\n3. Fallback: \"full-access\"\n```\n\n```python\ndef resolve_profile(explicit: str | None, model: str, settings: dict) -> AccessProfile:\n    if explicit:\n        return settings[\"sandbox\"][\"profiles\"][explicit]\n\n    model_defaults = settings[\"sandbox\"].get(\"model_defaults\", {})\n    if model in model_defaults:\n        return settings[\"sandbox\"][\"profiles\"][model_defaults[model]]\n\n    return settings[\"sandbox\"][\"profiles\"][\"full-access\"]\n```\n\n### Model Defaults\n\nMaps model names to profile names:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"sandbox\": {\n    \"model_defaults\": {\n      \"haiku\": \"feature-scoped\",\n      \"sonnet\": \"full-access\",\n      \"opus\": \"full-access\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nModels not listed fall back to `full-access`.\n\n### Variable Substitution\n\nProfile mount paths can contain variables that are resolved at loop start time:\n\n| Variable | Resolved To | Example |\n|----------|-------------|---------|\n| `${FEATURE}` | Feature name / slug | `my-feature` |\n| `${PROJECT_ROOT}` | Absolute project root path | `/workspace` (always this inside container) |\n\n### Mount Translation to Docker Volumes\n\nEach `MountSpec` is translated to a Docker bind mount:\n\n```python\ndef to_docker_mount(spec: MountSpec, project_root: Path, translator: PathTranslator) -> dict:\n    host_path = project_root / spec.path  # Resolve relative to project\n    docker_path = translator.translate(str(host_path))  # Platform translation\n    container_path = f\"/workspace/{spec.path}\"  # Always under /workspace\n\n    return {\n        \"host\": docker_path,\n        \"container\": container_path,\n        \"mode\": spec.mode,\n    }\n```\n\n**Special case for `\".\"`**: When path is `.`, mount the entire project root as `/workspace/`.\n\n### Validation Rules\n\n- A profile must have at least one mount\n- Mount paths must be relative (no absolute paths or `..` traversal)\n- Mount paths must resolve to locations within the project root\n- If a mount path doesn't exist on the host at loop start time, it is skipped with a warning (not an error — the feature directory might not exist yet)\n- Profile names must be alphanumeric + hyphens, no spaces\n- `\"rw\"` and `\"ro\"` are the only valid modes\n\n### Network Policy\n\nEach profile can optionally override the global network policy:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"research-only\": {\n    \"mounts\": [...],\n    \"network\": false\n  },\n  \"full-access\": {\n    \"mounts\": [...]\n    // No \"network\" key: inherits global setting\n  }\n}\n```\n\nResolution: `profile.network ?? global_network_setting`\n\n**Constraint:** OpenCode sandbox loops always require network access (to reach `host.docker.internal`). If a profile disables network and the loop uses OpenCode, the loop will fail with a clear error: \"OpenCode sandbox loops require network access. Profile '{name}' has network disabled.\"\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- **Mount path doesn't exist**: Skipped with warning. Agent sees the directory as missing inside the container.\n- **Overlapping mounts**: If both `.` (full project) and `src/` are mounted, Docker handles this correctly.\n- **`${FEATURE}` not provided**: If a profile uses `${FEATURE}` but the loop doesn't specify a feature name, error returned to caller.\n- **Profile deleted while container running**: Container continues with current mounts. Container is per-loop so it's removed when loop finishes anyway.\n- **Empty mount list**: Profile validation rejects this at settings save time.\n- **`research-only` + OpenCode**: Fails with clear error (network required for OpenCode path).\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- Spec: [container-lifecycle](container-lifecycle.md) - Consumes profiles to create containers with correct mounts\n- Spec: [settings](settings.md) - Profiles stored in `ralph.sandbox.profiles`\n- Spec: [dashboard-ui](dashboard-ui.md) - Sandbox toggle only (no profile editor in this phase)\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n- Unit tests for profile resolution (explicit > model default > fallback)\n- Unit tests for variable substitution (`${FEATURE}`, `${PROJECT_ROOT}`)\n- Unit tests for mount translation to Docker volumes\n- Unit tests for validation rules (reject invalid paths, require at least one mount)\n- Unit tests for network policy resolution (override vs inherit)\n- Unit test: OpenCode + network-disabled profile fails with clear error\n- Integration test: container with `full-access` profile can access all project files\n- Integration test: container with `research-only` profile rejects writes\n","numLines":208,"startLine":1,"totalLines":208}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01VpJJWqjAVvuWCq1PYwLBux","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JityzDs2e13BUjXLcRaC9N","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/.vista/features/docker-sandbox/specs/ralph-mcp-integration.md"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":217,"cache_read_input_tokens":48904,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":217},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6fe45d16-ab3a-4e41-9b98-035326f9b7c3","uuid":"b1785b29-8ab3-48bf-b07b-1d6ccb572399"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JityzDs2e13BUjXLcRaC9N","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Spec: Ralph MCP Tool Integration\n     2→\n     3→## Problem Statement\n     4→\n     5→The `ralph-mcp-tool` feature exposes MCP tools for programmatic loop orchestration: `ralph_providers`, `ralph_start`, `ralph_status`, `ralph_summary`, `ralph_stop`. When sandbox mode is enabled, `ralph_start` must route loop execution through `ContainerManager` instead of spawning a local subprocess — transparently, without changing the MCP tool interface.\n     6→\n     7→## Integration Point: `RalphService.create_job()`\n     8→\n     9→`RalphService` is the single entry point for loop execution. Only the job creation and execution path needs a sandbox branch.\n    10→\n    11→### Current Flow (no sandbox)\n    12→\n    13→```\n    14→ralph_start MCP tool\n    15→  → RalphService.create_job(provider, model, mode, feature, ...)\n    16→    → Generate loop.ps1 from LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE\n    17→    → subprocess.Popen([\"powershell\", \"-File\", \"loop.ps1\"], cwd=project_root)\n    18→    → Track PID in job.json\n    19→    → Return job_id\n    20→```\n    21→\n    22→### Sandbox Flow — Claude Code\n    23→\n    24→```\n    25→ralph_start MCP tool (provider=claude)\n    26→  → RalphService.create_job(provider, model, mode, feature, ...)\n    27→    → check settings.ralph.sandbox.enabled\n    28→    → Generate loop.sh from LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE (always bash in container)\n    29→    → Gather credentials (claude_auth + git_ssh + git_config)\n    30→    → ContainerManager.create_loop_container(\n    31→          job_id, \"claude\", project_root, credentials, image\n    32→      )\n    33→    → ContainerManager.exec_in_container(\n    34→          container_name=\"vista-ralph-{job_id}\",\n    35→          command=[\"bash\", \"/workspace/.vista/ralph/{slug}/{job_id}/loop.sh\"],\n    36→          workdir=\"/workspace\",\n    37→          stdout_handle=output_log\n    38→      )\n    39→    → Track exec host PID + container name in job.json\n    40→    → Return job_id\n    41→```\n    42→\n    43→Inside the container, `loop.sh` runs `claude -p` natively — identical to current behavior but sandboxed.\n    44→\n    45→### Sandbox Flow — OpenCode\n    46→\n    47→```\n    48→ralph_start MCP tool (provider=opencode)\n    49→  → RalphService.create_job(provider, model, mode, feature, ...)\n    50→    → check settings.ralph.sandbox.enabled\n    51→    → Ensure opencode serve is running on host\n    52→    → Create opencode serve session (scoped to project root)\n    53→    → Generate loop.sh from OPENCODE_SANDBOX_LOOP_TEMPLATE\n    54→    → Gather credentials (git_ssh + git_config only — no AI creds)\n    55→    → ContainerManager.create_loop_container(\n    56→          job_id, \"opencode\", project_root, credentials, image\n    57→      )\n    58→    → ContainerManager.exec_in_container(\n    59→          container_name=\"vista-ralph-{job_id}\",\n    60→          command=[\"bash\", \"/workspace/.vista/ralph/{slug}/{job_id}/loop.sh\"],\n    61→          workdir=\"/workspace\",\n    62→          env={\n    63→              \"VISTA_HOST\": \"host.docker.internal\",\n    64→              \"VISTA_PORT\": str(vista_port),\n    65→              \"OPENCODE_SESSION\": session_id,\n    66→              \"MODEL\": model,\n    67→          },\n    68→          stdout_handle=output_log\n    69→      )\n    70→    → Track exec host PID + container name + session_id in job.json\n    71→    → Return job_id\n    72→```\n    73→\n    74→Inside the container, `loop.sh` uses `curl` to call the Vista proxy endpoint instead of invoking `opencode run`.\n    75→\n    76→### Loop Script Templates\n    77→\n    78→**Claude Code sandbox loop (bash):**\n    79→\n    80→Uses the existing `LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE` with `shell=\"sh\"` — the Claude invocation block already supports bash:\n    81→\n    82→```bash\n    83→printf \"%s\" \"$PROMPT_CONTENT\" | claude -p \\\n    84→    --dangerously-skip-permissions \\\n    85→    --output-format=stream-json \\\n    86→    --model \"$MODEL\" \\\n    87→    --verbose\n    88→```\n    89→\n    90→No changes needed to the Claude invocation. The template generates bash instead of PowerShell when running in sandbox mode.\n    91→\n    92→**OpenCode sandbox loop (bash) — new template:**\n    93→\n    94→```bash\n    95→# OpenCode Sandbox Loop - calls Vista proxy instead of opencode CLI\n    96→# Auto-generated by ralph service\n    97→\n    98→FEATURE_DIR=\"{feature_dir}\"\n    99→PROJECT_ROOT=\"/workspace\"\n   100→MODE=\"{mode}\"\n   101→MODEL=\"$MODEL\"\n   102→MAX_ITERATIONS={max_iterations}\n   103→VISTA_API=\"http://$VISTA_HOST:$VISTA_PORT/api/sandbox/opencode/$OPENCODE_SESSION\"\n   104→\n   105→PROMPT_FILE=\"$FEATURE_DIR/PROMPT_$MODE.md\"\n   106→PROGRESS_FILE=\"$FEATURE_DIR/progress.txt\"\n   107→TASK_FILE=\"$FEATURE_DIR/task.md\"\n   108→\n   109→CURRENT_BRANCH=$(git branch --show-current)\n   110→\n   111→echo \"━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\"\n   112→echo \"Feature:  {feature_name}\"\n   113→echo \"Provider: OpenCode (via Vista proxy)\"\n   114→echo \"Mode:     $MODE\"\n   115→echo \"Model:    $MODEL\"\n   116→echo \"Branch:   $CURRENT_BRANCH\"\n   117→echo \"━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\"\n   118→\n   119→if [ ! -f \"$PROMPT_FILE\" ]; then\n   120→    echo \"Error: $PROMPT_FILE not found\"\n   121→    exit 1\n   122→fi\n   123→\n   124→ITERATION=0\n   125→\n   126→while true; do\n   127→    if [ \"$MAX_ITERATIONS\" -gt 0 ] && [ \"$ITERATION\" -ge \"$MAX_ITERATIONS\" ]; then\n   128→        echo \"Reached max iterations: $MAX_ITERATIONS\"\n   129→        break\n   130→    fi\n   131→\n   132→    ITERATION=$((ITERATION + 1))\n   133→    echo \"\"\n   134→    echo \"======================== ITERATION $ITERATION ========================\"\n   135→    echo \"Started: $(date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M')\"\n   136→\n   137→    # Build prompt with task + progress context\n   138→    PROMPT_CONTENT=$(cat \"$PROMPT_FILE\")\n   139→    if [ -f \"$TASK_FILE\" ]; then\n   140→        TASK_CONTENT=$(cat \"$TASK_FILE\")\n   141→        PROMPT_CONTENT=\"$PROMPT_CONTENT\n   142→\n   143→## Task\n   144→$TASK_CONTENT\"\n   145→    fi\n   146→    if [ -f \"$PROGRESS_FILE\" ]; then\n   147→        PROGRESS_CONTENT=$(cat \"$PROGRESS_FILE\")\n   148→        PROMPT_CONTENT=\"$PROMPT_CONTENT\n   149→\n   150→## Current Progress\n   151→$PROGRESS_CONTENT\"\n   152→    fi\n   153→\n   154→    # Send prompt to OpenCode via Vista proxy\n   155→    RESPONSE=$(curl -s -X POST \"$VISTA_API/message\" \\\n   156→        -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n   157→        -d \"$(jq -n --arg prompt \"$PROMPT_CONTENT\" --arg model \"$MODEL\" \\\n   158→            '{prompt: $prompt, model: $model}')\")\n   159→\n   160→    if [ $? -ne 0 ]; then\n   161→        echo \"Failed to reach Vista proxy\"\n   162→        exit 1\n   163→    fi\n   164→\n   165→    # Push changes after each iteration\n   166→    git push origin \"$CURRENT_BRANCH\" 2>/dev/null || \\\n   167→        git push -u origin \"$CURRENT_BRANCH\"\n   168→\n   169→    echo \"\"\n   170→    echo \"[$(date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M')] ITERATION $ITERATION complete\"\n   171→\n   172→    # Check completion (build mode)\n   173→    if [ \"$MODE\" = \"build\" ] && [ -f \"$PROGRESS_FILE\" ]; then\n   174→        if grep -q \"ALL PHASES COMPLETE\" \"$PROGRESS_FILE\"; then\n   175→            echo \"All phases complete! Stopping loop.\"\n   176→            break\n   177→        fi\n   178→    fi\n   179→done\n   180→\n   181→echo \"\"\n   182→echo \"━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\"\n   183→echo \"Loop finished after $ITERATION iteration(s)\"\n   184→echo \"━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\"\n   185→```\n   186→\n   187→### Vista Proxy Endpoint\n   188→\n   189→Vista exposes an endpoint that forwards to `opencode serve`:\n   190→\n   191→```python\n   192→# vista/server/routes/sandbox.py\n   193→\n   194→@router.post(\"/api/sandbox/opencode/{session_id}/message\")\n   195→async def opencode_proxy_message(session_id: str, request: Request):\n   196→    \"\"\"Forward a message to the opencode serve session.\n   197→\n   198→    1. Validate session_id exists\n   199→    2. Forward request body to opencode serve API\n   200→    3. Stream response back to caller (container)\n   201→    4. opencode serve handles AI reasoning + file operations on host\n   202→    5. File changes visible in container via bind mount\n   203→    \"\"\"\n   204→```\n   205→\n   206→## Impact on Each MCP Tool\n   207→\n   208→| MCP Tool | Change Required | Notes |\n   209→|----------|----------------|-------|\n   210→| `ralph_providers` | None | Discovers providers from host CLI — sandbox irrelevant |\n   211→| `ralph_start` | **Yes** — sandbox branch in `create_job()` | Routes to container + serve based on provider |\n   212→| `ralph_status` | Minor | Check container status in addition to PID |\n   213→| `ralph_summary` | None | Reads artifacts from job directory on host (mounted into container) |\n   214→| `ralph_stop` | Minor | Kill exec PID + remove container + close serve session |\n   215→\n   216→### `ralph_stop` with Sandbox\n   217→\n   218→```python\n   219→async def stop_job(self, job_id: str):\n   220→    job = self._load_job(job_id)\n   221→\n   222→    if job.get(\"sandbox\"):\n   223→        # Kill the exec process (terminates loop script in container)\n   224→        self._kill_pid(job[\"pid\"])\n   225→        # Close opencode serve session (if OpenCode loop)\n   226→        if job.get(\"opencode_session\"):\n   227→            await self.opencode_serve_manager.close_session(job_id)\n   228→        # Remove the container\n   229→        await self.container_manager.remove_container(f\"vista-ralph-{job_id}\")\n   230→    else:\n   231→        # Current behavior: kill local subprocess\n   232→        self._kill_pid(job[\"pid\"])\n   233→```\n   234→\n   235→## Job Metadata Extension\n   236→\n   237→When sandbox is active, `job.json` records additional fields:\n   238→\n   239→```json\n   240→{\n   241→  \"job_id\": \"a1b2c3d4\",\n   242→  \"slug\": \"my-feature\",\n   243→  \"mode\": \"build\",\n   244→  \"status\": \"running\",\n   245→  \"provider\": \"opencode\",\n   246→  \"model\": \"claude-sonnet-4\",\n   247→  \"pid\": 12345,\n   248→  \"sandbox\": true,\n   249→  \"container\": \"vista-ralph-a1b2c3d4\",\n   250→  \"opencode_session\": \"sess_xyz789\"\n   251→}\n   252→```\n   253→\n   254→For Claude Code loops, `opencode_session` is absent. When sandbox is disabled, `sandbox` is `false` and `container`/`opencode_session` are absent.\n   255→\n   256→## Loop Script Template Selection\n   257→\n   258→```python\n   259→def _get_loop_template(self, provider: Provider, sandbox_enabled: bool) -> str:\n   260→    if not sandbox_enabled:\n   261→        # Current behavior: platform-specific (ps1 or sh)\n   262→        return LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE  # PowerShell on Windows, bash on Linux/macOS\n   263→\n   264→    if provider.name == \"claude\":\n   265→        # Claude Code runs natively inside Linux container\n   266→        return LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE  # Use bash variant (shell=\"sh\")\n   267→\n   268→    if provider.name == \"opencode\":\n   269→        # OpenCode calls Vista proxy from inside container\n   270→        return OPENCODE_SANDBOX_LOOP_TEMPLATE  # New template\n   271→\n   272→    raise ValueError(f\"Unknown provider for sandbox: {provider.name}\")\n   273→```\n   274→\n   275→## Project Root Mounting — Agent Access\n   276→\n   277→The container always mounts the full project root at `/workspace/`:\n   278→\n   279→```\n   280→/workspace/\n   281→  ├── .vista/\n   282→  │   ├── features/\n   283→  │   │   └── {slug}/              ← feature specs, PRDs, arch docs\n   284→  │   │       ├── specs/\n   285→  │   │       ├── task.md\n   286→  │   │       └── PROMPT_build.md\n   287→  │   └── ralph/\n   288→  │       └── {slug}/\n   289→  │           └── {job_id}/        ← job directory\n   290→  │               ├── job.json\n   291→  │               ├── loop.sh\n   292→  │               ├── output.log\n   293→  │               └── progress.txt\n   294→  ├── src/                         ← source code\n   295→  ├── tests/                       ← test files\n   296→  ├── .git/                        ← git repo (commit + push)\n   297→  ├── CLAUDE.md                    ← project instructions\n   298→  └── ...                          ← everything else in project\n   299→```\n   300→\n   301→This ensures:\n   302→- Agents can read feature specs to understand requirements\n   303→- Agents can read/write source code and tests\n   304→- Agents can commit and push (`.git/` + SSH keys mounted)\n   305→- Progress tracking files are in the job directory\n   306→- `CLAUDE.md` and other project config is visible\n   307→\n   308→## Settings Namespace\n   309→\n   310→Both features share the `ralph` settings namespace:\n   311→\n   312→```json\n   313→{\n   314→  \"ralph\": {\n   315→    \"defaults\": { \"...\" : \"...\" },\n   316→    \"providers\": { \"...\" : \"...\" },\n   317→    \"summarizer\": { \"...\" : \"...\" },\n   318→    \"sandbox\": {\n   319→      \"enabled\": false,\n   320→      \"image\": \"vista-ralph:latest\",\n   321→      \"network\": true,\n   322→      \"opencode_serve_port\": 4096,\n   323→      \"credentials\": { \"...\" : \"...\" },\n   324→      \"profiles\": { \"...\" : \"...\" },\n   325→      \"model_defaults\": { \"...\" : \"...\" }\n   326→    }\n   327→  }\n   328→}\n   329→```\n   330→\n   331→## Implementation Order\n   332→\n   333→1. **ralph-mcp-tool** — implement `RalphService` with local subprocess spawning (done/in-progress)\n   334→2. **docker-sandbox phase 1** — `ContainerManager` + Claude Code sandbox path\n   335→3. **docker-sandbox phase 2** — `OpenCodeServeManager` + proxy endpoint + OpenCode sandbox path\n   336→\n   337→## Dependencies\n   338→\n   339→- Spec: [container-lifecycle](container-lifecycle.md) — `ContainerManager` and `OpenCodeServeManager` APIs\n   340→- Spec: [credential-management](credential-management.md) — credential gathering per provider\n   341→- Spec: [settings](settings.md) — `ralph.sandbox` settings schema\n   342→- Feature: `ralph-mcp-tool` — `RalphService`, MCP tool definitions, job management\n   343→\n   344→## Testing Strategy\n   345→\n   346→- Unit test: `create_job()` routes to `ContainerManager` when `sandbox.enabled = true`\n   347→- Unit test: `create_job()` uses local subprocess when `sandbox.enabled = false`\n   348→- Unit test: Claude Code loops use bash loop template with native `claude -p`\n   349→- Unit test: OpenCode loops use proxy loop template with `curl` calls\n   350→- Unit test: job.json includes sandbox metadata when sandbox active\n   351→- Integration test: full `ralph_start` → `ralph_status` → `ralph_stop` cycle with sandbox (Claude path)\n   352→- Integration test: full cycle with sandbox (OpenCode path via serve proxy)\n   353→- Integration test: `ralph_summary` reads artifacts produced inside container\n   354→- Integration test: `ralph_stop` kills exec, closes session, removes container\n   355→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6fe45d16-ab3a-4e41-9b98-035326f9b7c3","uuid":"127399a6-d414-4123-b9bc-d4cd74769822","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/.vista/features/docker-sandbox/specs/ralph-mcp-integration.md","content":"# Spec: Ralph MCP Tool Integration\n\n## Problem Statement\n\nThe `ralph-mcp-tool` feature exposes MCP tools for programmatic loop orchestration: `ralph_providers`, `ralph_start`, `ralph_status`, `ralph_summary`, `ralph_stop`. When sandbox mode is enabled, `ralph_start` must route loop execution through `ContainerManager` instead of spawning a local subprocess — transparently, without changing the MCP tool interface.\n\n## Integration Point: `RalphService.create_job()`\n\n`RalphService` is the single entry point for loop execution. Only the job creation and execution path needs a sandbox branch.\n\n### Current Flow (no sandbox)\n\n```\nralph_start MCP tool\n  → RalphService.create_job(provider, model, mode, feature, ...)\n    → Generate loop.ps1 from LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE\n    → subprocess.Popen([\"powershell\", \"-File\", \"loop.ps1\"], cwd=project_root)\n    → Track PID in job.json\n    → Return job_id\n```\n\n### Sandbox Flow — Claude Code\n\n```\nralph_start MCP tool (provider=claude)\n  → RalphService.create_job(provider, model, mode, feature, ...)\n    → check settings.ralph.sandbox.enabled\n    → Generate loop.sh from LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE (always bash in container)\n    → Gather credentials (claude_auth + git_ssh + git_config)\n    → ContainerManager.create_loop_container(\n          job_id, \"claude\", project_root, credentials, image\n      )\n    → ContainerManager.exec_in_container(\n          container_name=\"vista-ralph-{job_id}\",\n          command=[\"bash\", \"/workspace/.vista/ralph/{slug}/{job_id}/loop.sh\"],\n          workdir=\"/workspace\",\n          stdout_handle=output_log\n      )\n    → Track exec host PID + container name in job.json\n    → Return job_id\n```\n\nInside the container, `loop.sh` runs `claude -p` natively — identical to current behavior but sandboxed.\n\n### Sandbox Flow — OpenCode\n\n```\nralph_start MCP tool (provider=opencode)\n  → RalphService.create_job(provider, model, mode, feature, ...)\n    → check settings.ralph.sandbox.enabled\n    → Ensure opencode serve is running on host\n    → Create opencode serve session (scoped to project root)\n    → Generate loop.sh from OPENCODE_SANDBOX_LOOP_TEMPLATE\n    → Gather credentials (git_ssh + git_config only — no AI creds)\n    → ContainerManager.create_loop_container(\n          job_id, \"opencode\", project_root, credentials, image\n      )\n    → ContainerManager.exec_in_container(\n          container_name=\"vista-ralph-{job_id}\",\n          command=[\"bash\", \"/workspace/.vista/ralph/{slug}/{job_id}/loop.sh\"],\n          workdir=\"/workspace\",\n          env={\n              \"VISTA_HOST\": \"host.docker.internal\",\n              \"VISTA_PORT\": str(vista_port),\n              \"OPENCODE_SESSION\": session_id,\n              \"MODEL\": model,\n          },\n          stdout_handle=output_log\n      )\n    → Track exec host PID + container name + session_id in job.json\n    → Return job_id\n```\n\nInside the container, `loop.sh` uses `curl` to call the Vista proxy endpoint instead of invoking `opencode run`.\n\n### Loop Script Templates\n\n**Claude Code sandbox loop (bash):**\n\nUses the existing `LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE` with `shell=\"sh\"` — the Claude invocation block already supports bash:\n\n```bash\nprintf \"%s\" \"$PROMPT_CONTENT\" | claude -p \\\n    --dangerously-skip-permissions \\\n    --output-format=stream-json \\\n    --model \"$MODEL\" \\\n    --verbose\n```\n\nNo changes needed to the Claude invocation. The template generates bash instead of PowerShell when running in sandbox mode.\n\n**OpenCode sandbox loop (bash) — new template:**\n\n```bash\n# OpenCode Sandbox Loop - calls Vista proxy instead of opencode CLI\n# Auto-generated by ralph service\n\nFEATURE_DIR=\"{feature_dir}\"\nPROJECT_ROOT=\"/workspace\"\nMODE=\"{mode}\"\nMODEL=\"$MODEL\"\nMAX_ITERATIONS={max_iterations}\nVISTA_API=\"http://$VISTA_HOST:$VISTA_PORT/api/sandbox/opencode/$OPENCODE_SESSION\"\n\nPROMPT_FILE=\"$FEATURE_DIR/PROMPT_$MODE.md\"\nPROGRESS_FILE=\"$FEATURE_DIR/progress.txt\"\nTASK_FILE=\"$FEATURE_DIR/task.md\"\n\nCURRENT_BRANCH=$(git branch --show-current)\n\necho \"━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\"\necho \"Feature:  {feature_name}\"\necho \"Provider: OpenCode (via Vista proxy)\"\necho \"Mode:     $MODE\"\necho \"Model:    $MODEL\"\necho \"Branch:   $CURRENT_BRANCH\"\necho \"━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\"\n\nif [ ! -f \"$PROMPT_FILE\" ]; then\n    echo \"Error: $PROMPT_FILE not found\"\n    exit 1\nfi\n\nITERATION=0\n\nwhile true; do\n    if [ \"$MAX_ITERATIONS\" -gt 0 ] && [ \"$ITERATION\" -ge \"$MAX_ITERATIONS\" ]; then\n        echo \"Reached max iterations: $MAX_ITERATIONS\"\n        break\n    fi\n\n    ITERATION=$((ITERATION + 1))\n    echo \"\"\n    echo \"======================== ITERATION $ITERATION ========================\"\n    echo \"Started: $(date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M')\"\n\n    # Build prompt with task + progress context\n    PROMPT_CONTENT=$(cat \"$PROMPT_FILE\")\n    if [ -f \"$TASK_FILE\" ]; then\n        TASK_CONTENT=$(cat \"$TASK_FILE\")\n        PROMPT_CONTENT=\"$PROMPT_CONTENT\n\n## Task\n$TASK_CONTENT\"\n    fi\n    if [ -f \"$PROGRESS_FILE\" ]; then\n        PROGRESS_CONTENT=$(cat \"$PROGRESS_FILE\")\n        PROMPT_CONTENT=\"$PROMPT_CONTENT\n\n## Current Progress\n$PROGRESS_CONTENT\"\n    fi\n\n    # Send prompt to OpenCode via Vista proxy\n    RESPONSE=$(curl -s -X POST \"$VISTA_API/message\" \\\n        -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n        -d \"$(jq -n --arg prompt \"$PROMPT_CONTENT\" --arg model \"$MODEL\" \\\n            '{prompt: $prompt, model: $model}')\")\n\n    if [ $? -ne 0 ]; then\n        echo \"Failed to reach Vista proxy\"\n        exit 1\n    fi\n\n    # Push changes after each iteration\n    git push origin \"$CURRENT_BRANCH\" 2>/dev/null || \\\n        git push -u origin \"$CURRENT_BRANCH\"\n\n    echo \"\"\n    echo \"[$(date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M')] ITERATION $ITERATION complete\"\n\n    # Check completion (build mode)\n    if [ \"$MODE\" = \"build\" ] && [ -f \"$PROGRESS_FILE\" ]; then\n        if grep -q \"ALL PHASES COMPLETE\" \"$PROGRESS_FILE\"; then\n            echo \"All phases complete! Stopping loop.\"\n            break\n        fi\n    fi\ndone\n\necho \"\"\necho \"━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\"\necho \"Loop finished after $ITERATION iteration(s)\"\necho \"━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\"\n```\n\n### Vista Proxy Endpoint\n\nVista exposes an endpoint that forwards to `opencode serve`:\n\n```python\n# vista/server/routes/sandbox.py\n\n@router.post(\"/api/sandbox/opencode/{session_id}/message\")\nasync def opencode_proxy_message(session_id: str, request: Request):\n    \"\"\"Forward a message to the opencode serve session.\n\n    1. Validate session_id exists\n    2. Forward request body to opencode serve API\n    3. Stream response back to caller (container)\n    4. opencode serve handles AI reasoning + file operations on host\n    5. File changes visible in container via bind mount\n    \"\"\"\n```\n\n## Impact on Each MCP Tool\n\n| MCP Tool | Change Required | Notes |\n|----------|----------------|-------|\n| `ralph_providers` | None | Discovers providers from host CLI — sandbox irrelevant |\n| `ralph_start` | **Yes** — sandbox branch in `create_job()` | Routes to container + serve based on provider |\n| `ralph_status` | Minor | Check container status in addition to PID |\n| `ralph_summary` | None | Reads artifacts from job directory on host (mounted into container) |\n| `ralph_stop` | Minor | Kill exec PID + remove container + close serve session |\n\n### `ralph_stop` with Sandbox\n\n```python\nasync def stop_job(self, job_id: str):\n    job = self._load_job(job_id)\n\n    if job.get(\"sandbox\"):\n        # Kill the exec process (terminates loop script in container)\n        self._kill_pid(job[\"pid\"])\n        # Close opencode serve session (if OpenCode loop)\n        if job.get(\"opencode_session\"):\n            await self.opencode_serve_manager.close_session(job_id)\n        # Remove the container\n        await self.container_manager.remove_container(f\"vista-ralph-{job_id}\")\n    else:\n        # Current behavior: kill local subprocess\n        self._kill_pid(job[\"pid\"])\n```\n\n## Job Metadata Extension\n\nWhen sandbox is active, `job.json` records additional fields:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"job_id\": \"a1b2c3d4\",\n  \"slug\": \"my-feature\",\n  \"mode\": \"build\",\n  \"status\": \"running\",\n  \"provider\": \"opencode\",\n  \"model\": \"claude-sonnet-4\",\n  \"pid\": 12345,\n  \"sandbox\": true,\n  \"container\": \"vista-ralph-a1b2c3d4\",\n  \"opencode_session\": \"sess_xyz789\"\n}\n```\n\nFor Claude Code loops, `opencode_session` is absent. When sandbox is disabled, `sandbox` is `false` and `container`/`opencode_session` are absent.\n\n## Loop Script Template Selection\n\n```python\ndef _get_loop_template(self, provider: Provider, sandbox_enabled: bool) -> str:\n    if not sandbox_enabled:\n        # Current behavior: platform-specific (ps1 or sh)\n        return LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE  # PowerShell on Windows, bash on Linux/macOS\n\n    if provider.name == \"claude\":\n        # Claude Code runs natively inside Linux container\n        return LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE  # Use bash variant (shell=\"sh\")\n\n    if provider.name == \"opencode\":\n        # OpenCode calls Vista proxy from inside container\n        return OPENCODE_SANDBOX_LOOP_TEMPLATE  # New template\n\n    raise ValueError(f\"Unknown provider for sandbox: {provider.name}\")\n```\n\n## Project Root Mounting — Agent Access\n\nThe container always mounts the full project root at `/workspace/`:\n\n```\n/workspace/\n  ├── .vista/\n  │   ├── features/\n  │   │   └── {slug}/              ← feature specs, PRDs, arch docs\n  │   │       ├── specs/\n  │   │       ├── task.md\n  │   │       └── PROMPT_build.md\n  │   └── ralph/\n  │       └── {slug}/\n  │           └── {job_id}/        ← job directory\n  │               ├── job.json\n  │               ├── loop.sh\n  │               ├── output.log\n  │               └── progress.txt\n  ├── src/                         ← source code\n  ├── tests/                       ← test files\n  ├── .git/                        ← git repo (commit + push)\n  ├── CLAUDE.md                    ← project instructions\n  └── ...                          ← everything else in project\n```\n\nThis ensures:\n- Agents can read feature specs to understand requirements\n- Agents can read/write source code and tests\n- Agents can commit and push (`.git/` + SSH keys mounted)\n- Progress tracking files are in the job directory\n- `CLAUDE.md` and other project config is visible\n\n## Settings Namespace\n\nBoth features share the `ralph` settings namespace:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"ralph\": {\n    \"defaults\": { \"...\" : \"...\" },\n    \"providers\": { \"...\" : \"...\" },\n    \"summarizer\": { \"...\" : \"...\" },\n    \"sandbox\": {\n      \"enabled\": false,\n      \"image\": \"vista-ralph:latest\",\n      \"network\": true,\n      \"opencode_serve_port\": 4096,\n      \"credentials\": { \"...\" : \"...\" },\n      \"profiles\": { \"...\" : \"...\" },\n      \"model_defaults\": { \"...\" : \"...\" }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Implementation Order\n\n1. **ralph-mcp-tool** — implement `RalphService` with local subprocess spawning (done/in-progress)\n2. **docker-sandbox phase 1** — `ContainerManager` + Claude Code sandbox path\n3. **docker-sandbox phase 2** — `OpenCodeServeManager` + proxy endpoint + OpenCode sandbox path\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- Spec: [container-lifecycle](container-lifecycle.md) — `ContainerManager` and `OpenCodeServeManager` APIs\n- Spec: [credential-management](credential-management.md) — credential gathering per provider\n- Spec: [settings](settings.md) — `ralph.sandbox` settings schema\n- Feature: `ralph-mcp-tool` — `RalphService`, MCP tool definitions, job management\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n- Unit test: `create_job()` routes to `ContainerManager` when `sandbox.enabled = true`\n- Unit test: `create_job()` uses local subprocess when `sandbox.enabled = false`\n- Unit test: Claude Code loops use bash loop template with native `claude -p`\n- Unit test: OpenCode loops use proxy loop template with `curl` calls\n- Unit test: job.json includes sandbox metadata when sandbox active\n- Integration test: full `ralph_start` → `ralph_status` → `ralph_stop` cycle with sandbox (Claude path)\n- Integration test: full cycle with sandbox (OpenCode path via serve proxy)\n- Integration test: `ralph_summary` reads artifacts produced inside container\n- Integration test: `ralph_stop` kills exec, closes session, removes container\n","numLines":355,"startLine":1,"totalLines":355}}}
