{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DF3cJ5tTbAcTW5NSicwHmY","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Spec: Credential Management\n     2→\n     3→## Problem Statement\n     4→\n     5→Docker containers need host credentials to function: Claude Code needs OAuth tokens and API keys, git needs SSH keys and identity config. The challenge is mounting these automatically without user intervention, handling platform differences (Windows vs Linux vs macOS), and validating that mounted credentials actually work inside the container.\n     6→\n     7→With the split execution model, OpenCode loops do NOT need AI credentials in the container — `opencode serve` runs on the host with native auth. This dramatically simplifies the credential story.\n     8→\n     9→## Proposed Solution\n    10→\n    11→A **credential provider** pattern where each provider encapsulates the logic to detect, mount, and validate a specific credential type. Providers are scoped to what's actually needed in the container — git/SSH credentials (both paths) and Claude auth (Claude Code path only).\n    12→\n    13→### What Goes in the Container vs What Stays on Host\n    14→\n    15→| Credential | Claude Code Loops | OpenCode Loops | Why |\n    16→|---|---|---|---|\n    17→| `~/.claude/` (OAuth + session) | Mounted (rw) | Not needed | Claude Code runs inside container |\n    18→| `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` | Forwarded as env var | Not needed | Claude Code may use API key auth |\n    19→| `~/.ssh/` | Mounted (ro) | Mounted (ro) | Both paths: git push/pull from container |\n    20→| `~/.gitconfig` | Mounted (ro) | Mounted (ro) | Both paths: git identity for commits |\n    21→| `~/.config/gh/` | Mounted (ro) | Mounted (ro) | Both paths: `gh` CLI for PR creation |\n    22→| AI provider keys (OpenAI, etc.) | N/A | Stays on host | `opencode serve` handles on host |\n    23→\n    24→### Credential Provider Interface\n    25→\n    26→```python\n    27→class CredentialProvider:\n    28→    name: str                    # e.g., \"claude_auth\"\n    29→    display_name: str            # e.g., \"Claude Code Auth\"\n    30→    description: str             # e.g., \"OAuth tokens and session state for Claude Code\"\n    31→    applies_to: list[str]        # [\"claude\"] or [\"claude\", \"opencode\"] or [\"*\"]\n    32→\n    33→    def detect(self) -> CredentialDetection:\n    34→        \"\"\"Check if this credential exists on the host.\n    35→        Returns detection result with source location and method.\"\"\"\n    36→\n    37→    def get_docker_config(self) -> DockerCredentialConfig:\n    38→        \"\"\"Generate Docker mount/env configuration for this credential.\n    39→        Only called if credential is detected and enabled.\"\"\"\n    40→\n    41→    def get_validation_command(self) -> str:\n    42→        \"\"\"Return a shell command to run inside the container to verify\n    43→        the credential is accessible and functional.\"\"\"\n    44→```\n    45→\n    46→### Built-In Providers\n    47→\n    48→#### ClaudeAuthProvider\n    49→- **Applies to**: Claude Code loops only\n    50→- **Detects**: `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` env var, then `~/.claude/` directory\n    51→- **Docker config**:\n    52→  - If env var: passes as `-e ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...`\n    53→  - Config dir: mounts `~/.claude/` → `/home/{user}/.claude/` (read-write)\n    54→  - **Must be read-write**: Claude Code writes session state, token cache, and settings to this directory. Read-only mount causes errors.\n    55→- **Validation**: `claude --version` (confirms CLI + auth)\n    56→- **Platform notes**:\n    57→  - Windows: `C:\\Users\\{user}\\.claude\\`\n    58→  - Linux/macOS: `~/.claude/`\n    59→\n    60→#### GitSshProvider\n    61→- **Applies to**: All loops (`[\"*\"]`)\n    62→- **Detects**: `~/.ssh/` directory with key files (`id_rsa`, `id_ed25519`, etc.)\n    63→- **Docker config**: mounts `~/.ssh/` → `/home/{user}/.ssh/` (read-only)\n    64→- **Validation**: `ssh -T git@github.com` (or configured remote host)\n    65→- **Platform notes**:\n    66→  - Windows: `C:\\Users\\{user}\\.ssh\\`\n    67→  - Linux/macOS: `~/.ssh/`\n    68→\n    69→#### GitConfigProvider\n    70→- **Applies to**: All loops (`[\"*\"]`)\n    71→- **Detects**: `~/.gitconfig` file\n    72→- **Docker config**: mounts `~/.gitconfig` → `/home/{user}/.gitconfig` (read-only)\n    73→- **Validation**: `git config user.name && git config user.email`\n    74→- **Platform notes**:\n    75→  - Windows: `C:\\Users\\{user}\\.gitconfig`\n    76→  - Linux/macOS: `~/.gitconfig`\n    77→\n    78→#### GitHubCliProvider\n    79→- **Applies to**: All loops (`[\"*\"]`)\n    80→- **Detects**: `~/.config/gh/` directory (Linux/macOS) or `%APPDATA%\\GitHub CLI\\` (Windows)\n    81→- **Docker config**: mounts config dir → `/home/{user}/.config/gh/` (read-only)\n    82→- **Validation**: `gh auth status`\n    83→\n    84→#### CustomMountProvider\n    85→- **User-defined** mounts from settings\n    86→- **Detects**: checks if the host path exists\n    87→- **Docker config**: mounts as specified (user provides host path, container path, mode)\n    88→- **Validation**: `test -r {container_path}` (simple readability check)\n    89→\n    90→### Detection Result\n    91→\n    92→```python\n    93→@dataclass\n    94→class CredentialDetection:\n    95→    found: bool\n    96→    method: str           # \"env_var\", \"config_dir\", \"config_file\", \"not_found\"\n    97→    source_path: str      # Host path or env var name\n    98→    display_info: str     # Human-readable: \"Found via env var ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\"\n    99→```\n   100→\n   101→### Docker Credential Config\n   102→\n   103→```python\n   104→@dataclass\n   105→class DockerCredentialConfig:\n   106→    env_vars: dict[str, str]           # -e KEY=VALUE\n   107→    mounts: list[DockerMount]          # -v host:container:mode\n   108→\n   109→@dataclass\n   110→class DockerMount:\n   111→    host_path: str       # Absolute path on host (pre-translation)\n   112→    container_path: str  # Path inside container\n   113→    mode: str            # \"ro\" or \"rw\"\n   114→```\n   115→\n   116→### Path Translation\n   117→\n   118→Each provider uses a `PathTranslator` that auto-converts host paths to Docker-compatible mount paths:\n   119→\n   120→```python\n   121→class PathTranslator:\n   122→    def translate(self, host_path: str) -> str:\n   123→        \"\"\"Convert host path to Docker bind mount path.\n   124→\n   125→        Windows: C:\\\\Users\\\\Grove\\\\.ssh → /c/Users/Grove/.ssh\n   126→        WSL:     /mnt/c/Users/Grove/.ssh (no change needed)\n   127→        Linux:   /home/user/.ssh (no change needed)\n   128→        macOS:   /Users/user/.ssh (no change needed)\n   129→        \"\"\"\n   130→```\n   131→\n   132→### UID/GID Matching\n   133→\n   134→Critical for bind mount file permissions. The container user must match the host user's UID/GID:\n   135→\n   136→```python\n   137→def get_host_uid_gid() -> tuple[int, int]:\n   138→    \"\"\"Get the current user's UID and GID.\n   139→\n   140→    Windows/WSL2: Docker Desktop handles translation (use defaults 1000:1000)\n   141→    Linux: os.getuid(), os.getgid()\n   142→    macOS: os.getuid(), os.getgid()\n   143→    \"\"\"\n   144→```\n   145→\n   146→The claudebox Dockerfile already accepts `USER_ID` and `GROUP_ID` build args. Vista passes the host user's IDs when building the image.\n   147→\n   148→### Settings Schema\n   149→\n   150→```json\n   151→{\n   152→  \"ralph\": {\n   153→    \"sandbox\": {\n   154→      \"credentials\": {\n   155→        \"claude_auth\": true,\n   156→        \"git_ssh\": true,\n   157→        \"git_config\": true,\n   158→        \"github_cli\": false,\n   159→        \"custom\": []\n   160→      }\n   161→    }\n   162→  }\n   163→}\n   164→```\n   165→\n   166→- `true` = enabled (provider will detect and mount)\n   167→- `false` = disabled (credential not shared, even if detected)\n   168→- Custom entries are always evaluated if present\n   169→- Providers with `applies_to` that don't match the current loop provider are skipped automatically\n   170→\n   171→### Credential Gathering at Loop Start\n   172→\n   173→```python\n   174→def gather_credentials(provider_name: str, settings: dict) -> list[DockerCredentialConfig]:\n   175→    \"\"\"Collect Docker credential configs for a loop.\n   176→\n   177→    1. Iterate all built-in providers\n   178→    2. Skip providers where applies_to doesn't match provider_name\n   179→    3. Skip providers disabled in settings\n   180→    4. Run detect() on remaining providers\n   181→    5. For detected providers, call get_docker_config()\n   182→    6. Return list of configs to apply to container\n   183→    \"\"\"\n   184→```\n   185→\n   186→### Credential Validation Flow\n   187→\n   188→Runs automatically at Vista startup when `sandbox.enabled = true`, and available via internal API (`POST /api/sandbox/credentials/validate`):\n   189→\n   190→1. Vista collects all enabled providers\n   191→2. Each enabled provider runs `detect()` — results logged (found/not found)\n   192→3. Vista creates a temporary container with credential mounts from all detected+enabled providers\n   193→4. For each provider, runs `get_validation_command()` inside the container\n   194→5. Collects pass/fail results\n   195→6. Logs structured report to Vista server output (and returns via API if called programmatically)\n   196→7. Tears down temporary container\n   197→\n   198→## Edge Cases\n   199→\n   200→- **`~/.claude/` mounted read-only**: Claude Code writes session state here. Must be read-write or Claude Code will error. This differs from claudebox which uses a copy-per-project pattern — for ralph loops, direct rw mount is simpler.\n   201→- **Credential detected but mount fails**: Docker may reject certain paths (permissions, symlinks). Validation catches this.\n   202→- **Env var vs file for same credential**: Provider prefers env var if both exist (simpler Docker config).\n   203→- **SSH agent forwarding**: Not supported in v1. Only file-based SSH keys are mounted.\n   204→- **Windows Credential Manager**: Git credentials stored in Windows Credential Manager are not directly mountable. Users need SSH keys or `.git-credentials` file instead.\n   205→- **Docker not running**: All detection still works (detection is host-side). Mounting and validation fail with clear \"Docker not running\" error.\n   206→- **OpenCode loop with claude_auth enabled**: Provider is skipped because `applies_to: [\"claude\"]` doesn't match. No error.\n   207→\n   208→## Dependencies\n   209→\n   210→- `vista/server/config.py` - Settings loading for credential toggle states\n   211→- Spec: [container-lifecycle](container-lifecycle.md) - Creates containers with credential mounts\n   212→- Spec: [dashboard-ui](dashboard-ui.md) - Sandbox toggle (no credential UI in this phase)\n   213→\n   214→## Testing Strategy\n   215→\n   216→- Unit tests per provider: detection logic with mocked filesystem/env\n   217→- Unit tests for path translation: Windows, Linux, macOS paths\n   218→- Unit tests for Docker config generation: correct `-v` and `-e` flags\n   219→- Unit tests for `applies_to` filtering (Claude-only creds skipped for OpenCode loops)\n   220→- Unit tests for UID/GID detection per platform\n   221→- Integration test: full validation flow with real Docker container\n   222→- Platform-specific tests: Windows path detection, Linux path detection\n   223→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14b921d9-eeaf-453d-9533-337d6f497996","uuid":"9eb30864-b662-4523-8878-54313f8c9655","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/.vista/features/docker-sandbox/specs/credential-management.md","content":"# Spec: Credential Management\n\n## Problem Statement\n\nDocker containers need host credentials to function: Claude Code needs OAuth tokens and API keys, git needs SSH keys and identity config. The challenge is mounting these automatically without user intervention, handling platform differences (Windows vs Linux vs macOS), and validating that mounted credentials actually work inside the container.\n\nWith the split execution model, OpenCode loops do NOT need AI credentials in the container — `opencode serve` runs on the host with native auth. This dramatically simplifies the credential story.\n\n## Proposed Solution\n\nA **credential provider** pattern where each provider encapsulates the logic to detect, mount, and validate a specific credential type. Providers are scoped to what's actually needed in the container — git/SSH credentials (both paths) and Claude auth (Claude Code path only).\n\n### What Goes in the Container vs What Stays on Host\n\n| Credential | Claude Code Loops | OpenCode Loops | Why |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `~/.claude/` (OAuth + session) | Mounted (rw) | Not needed | Claude Code runs inside container |\n| `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` | Forwarded as env var | Not needed | Claude Code may use API key auth |\n| `~/.ssh/` | Mounted (ro) | Mounted (ro) | Both paths: git push/pull from container |\n| `~/.gitconfig` | Mounted (ro) | Mounted (ro) | Both paths: git identity for commits |\n| `~/.config/gh/` | Mounted (ro) | Mounted (ro) | Both paths: `gh` CLI for PR creation |\n| AI provider keys (OpenAI, etc.) | N/A | Stays on host | `opencode serve` handles on host |\n\n### Credential Provider Interface\n\n```python\nclass CredentialProvider:\n    name: str                    # e.g., \"claude_auth\"\n    display_name: str            # e.g., \"Claude Code Auth\"\n    description: str             # e.g., \"OAuth tokens and session state for Claude Code\"\n    applies_to: list[str]        # [\"claude\"] or [\"claude\", \"opencode\"] or [\"*\"]\n\n    def detect(self) -> CredentialDetection:\n        \"\"\"Check if this credential exists on the host.\n        Returns detection result with source location and method.\"\"\"\n\n    def get_docker_config(self) -> DockerCredentialConfig:\n        \"\"\"Generate Docker mount/env configuration for this credential.\n        Only called if credential is detected and enabled.\"\"\"\n\n    def get_validation_command(self) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Return a shell command to run inside the container to verify\n        the credential is accessible and functional.\"\"\"\n```\n\n### Built-In Providers\n\n#### ClaudeAuthProvider\n- **Applies to**: Claude Code loops only\n- **Detects**: `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` env var, then `~/.claude/` directory\n- **Docker config**:\n  - If env var: passes as `-e ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...`\n  - Config dir: mounts `~/.claude/` → `/home/{user}/.claude/` (read-write)\n  - **Must be read-write**: Claude Code writes session state, token cache, and settings to this directory. Read-only mount causes errors.\n- **Validation**: `claude --version` (confirms CLI + auth)\n- **Platform notes**:\n  - Windows: `C:\\Users\\{user}\\.claude\\`\n  - Linux/macOS: `~/.claude/`\n\n#### GitSshProvider\n- **Applies to**: All loops (`[\"*\"]`)\n- **Detects**: `~/.ssh/` directory with key files (`id_rsa`, `id_ed25519`, etc.)\n- **Docker config**: mounts `~/.ssh/` → `/home/{user}/.ssh/` (read-only)\n- **Validation**: `ssh -T git@github.com` (or configured remote host)\n- **Platform notes**:\n  - Windows: `C:\\Users\\{user}\\.ssh\\`\n  - Linux/macOS: `~/.ssh/`\n\n#### GitConfigProvider\n- **Applies to**: All loops (`[\"*\"]`)\n- **Detects**: `~/.gitconfig` file\n- **Docker config**: mounts `~/.gitconfig` → `/home/{user}/.gitconfig` (read-only)\n- **Validation**: `git config user.name && git config user.email`\n- **Platform notes**:\n  - Windows: `C:\\Users\\{user}\\.gitconfig`\n  - Linux/macOS: `~/.gitconfig`\n\n#### GitHubCliProvider\n- **Applies to**: All loops (`[\"*\"]`)\n- **Detects**: `~/.config/gh/` directory (Linux/macOS) or `%APPDATA%\\GitHub CLI\\` (Windows)\n- **Docker config**: mounts config dir → `/home/{user}/.config/gh/` (read-only)\n- **Validation**: `gh auth status`\n\n#### CustomMountProvider\n- **User-defined** mounts from settings\n- **Detects**: checks if the host path exists\n- **Docker config**: mounts as specified (user provides host path, container path, mode)\n- **Validation**: `test -r {container_path}` (simple readability check)\n\n### Detection Result\n\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass CredentialDetection:\n    found: bool\n    method: str           # \"env_var\", \"config_dir\", \"config_file\", \"not_found\"\n    source_path: str      # Host path or env var name\n    display_info: str     # Human-readable: \"Found via env var ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\"\n```\n\n### Docker Credential Config\n\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass DockerCredentialConfig:\n    env_vars: dict[str, str]           # -e KEY=VALUE\n    mounts: list[DockerMount]          # -v host:container:mode\n\n@dataclass\nclass DockerMount:\n    host_path: str       # Absolute path on host (pre-translation)\n    container_path: str  # Path inside container\n    mode: str            # \"ro\" or \"rw\"\n```\n\n### Path Translation\n\nEach provider uses a `PathTranslator` that auto-converts host paths to Docker-compatible mount paths:\n\n```python\nclass PathTranslator:\n    def translate(self, host_path: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Convert host path to Docker bind mount path.\n\n        Windows: C:\\\\Users\\\\Grove\\\\.ssh → /c/Users/Grove/.ssh\n        WSL:     /mnt/c/Users/Grove/.ssh (no change needed)\n        Linux:   /home/user/.ssh (no change needed)\n        macOS:   /Users/user/.ssh (no change needed)\n        \"\"\"\n```\n\n### UID/GID Matching\n\nCritical for bind mount file permissions. The container user must match the host user's UID/GID:\n\n```python\ndef get_host_uid_gid() -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"Get the current user's UID and GID.\n\n    Windows/WSL2: Docker Desktop handles translation (use defaults 1000:1000)\n    Linux: os.getuid(), os.getgid()\n    macOS: os.getuid(), os.getgid()\n    \"\"\"\n```\n\nThe claudebox Dockerfile already accepts `USER_ID` and `GROUP_ID` build args. Vista passes the host user's IDs when building the image.\n\n### Settings Schema\n\n```json\n{\n  \"ralph\": {\n    \"sandbox\": {\n      \"credentials\": {\n        \"claude_auth\": true,\n        \"git_ssh\": true,\n        \"git_config\": true,\n        \"github_cli\": false,\n        \"custom\": []\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n- `true` = enabled (provider will detect and mount)\n- `false` = disabled (credential not shared, even if detected)\n- Custom entries are always evaluated if present\n- Providers with `applies_to` that don't match the current loop provider are skipped automatically\n\n### Credential Gathering at Loop Start\n\n```python\ndef gather_credentials(provider_name: str, settings: dict) -> list[DockerCredentialConfig]:\n    \"\"\"Collect Docker credential configs for a loop.\n\n    1. Iterate all built-in providers\n    2. Skip providers where applies_to doesn't match provider_name\n    3. Skip providers disabled in settings\n    4. Run detect() on remaining providers\n    5. For detected providers, call get_docker_config()\n    6. Return list of configs to apply to container\n    \"\"\"\n```\n\n### Credential Validation Flow\n\nRuns automatically at Vista startup when `sandbox.enabled = true`, and available via internal API (`POST /api/sandbox/credentials/validate`):\n\n1. Vista collects all enabled providers\n2. Each enabled provider runs `detect()` — results logged (found/not found)\n3. Vista creates a temporary container with credential mounts from all detected+enabled providers\n4. For each provider, runs `get_validation_command()` inside the container\n5. Collects pass/fail results\n6. Logs structured report to Vista server output (and returns via API if called programmatically)\n7. Tears down temporary container\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- **`~/.claude/` mounted read-only**: Claude Code writes session state here. Must be read-write or Claude Code will error. This differs from claudebox which uses a copy-per-project pattern — for ralph loops, direct rw mount is simpler.\n- **Credential detected but mount fails**: Docker may reject certain paths (permissions, symlinks). Validation catches this.\n- **Env var vs file for same credential**: Provider prefers env var if both exist (simpler Docker config).\n- **SSH agent forwarding**: Not supported in v1. Only file-based SSH keys are mounted.\n- **Windows Credential Manager**: Git credentials stored in Windows Credential Manager are not directly mountable. Users need SSH keys or `.git-credentials` file instead.\n- **Docker not running**: All detection still works (detection is host-side). Mounting and validation fail with clear \"Docker not running\" error.\n- **OpenCode loop with claude_auth enabled**: Provider is skipped because `applies_to: [\"claude\"]` doesn't match. No error.\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- `vista/server/config.py` - Settings loading for credential toggle states\n- Spec: [container-lifecycle](container-lifecycle.md) - Creates containers with credential mounts\n- Spec: [dashboard-ui](dashboard-ui.md) - Sandbox toggle (no credential UI in this phase)\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n- Unit tests per provider: detection logic with mocked filesystem/env\n- Unit tests for path translation: Windows, Linux, macOS paths\n- Unit tests for Docker config generation: correct `-v` and `-e` flags\n- Unit tests for `applies_to` filtering (Claude-only creds skipped for OpenCode loops)\n- Unit tests for UID/GID detection per platform\n- Integration test: full validation flow with real Docker container\n- Platform-specific tests: Windows path detection, Linux path detection\n","numLines":223,"startLine":1,"totalLines":223}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01FaXqEV9VkM1anppfLkXivr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HLpnrog2TJ8MBe1EXJyyRs","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/.vista/features/docker-sandbox/specs/dashboard-ui.md"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4724,"cache_read_input_tokens":44307,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4724},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14b921d9-eeaf-453d-9533-337d6f497996","uuid":"1ab3f85a-e7dd-4064-a9e9-b163201ce75a"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HLpnrog2TJ8MBe1EXJyyRs","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Spec: Dashboard UI for Sandbox Settings\n     2→\n     3→## Problem Statement\n     4→\n     5→Users need a simple way to enable or disable Docker sandboxing for ralph loops. The dashboard should surface a single toggle and provide clear inline feedback when something is wrong (e.g., Docker not installed or not running). Advanced sandbox configuration (credentials, profiles, model defaults, container controls, opencode serve management) is handled via `settings.json` — not the dashboard — in this phase.\n     6→\n     7→## Proposed Solution\n     8→\n     9→A single **toggle control** in the Vista dashboard's Ralph settings area, bound to `ralph.sandbox.enabled`. Optionally, inline status text next to the toggle communicates readiness or errors.\n    10→\n    11→### UI Layout\n    12→\n    13→```\n    14→┌─ Ralph Settings ───────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n    15→│                                                                 │\n    16→│  ...existing ralph settings (provider, model, iterations)...    │\n    17→│                                                                 │\n    18→│  Docker Sandbox  [toggle: OFF]                                  │\n    19→│                                                                 │\n    20→│  ─── When toggled ON: ─────────────────────────────────────── │\n    21→│                                                                 │\n    22→│  Docker Sandbox  [toggle: ON]   ● Docker running                │\n    23→│                                                                 │\n    24→│  ─── Or, if Docker is unavailable: ───────────────────────── │\n    25→│                                                                 │\n    26→│  Docker Sandbox  [toggle: ON]   ✕ Docker not running            │\n    27→│                                    Install Docker Desktop and   │\n    28→│                                    ensure it is running.        │\n    29→│                                                                 │\n    30→│  ─── Or, if image not built: ─────────────────────────────── │\n    31→│                                                                 │\n    32→│  Docker Sandbox  [toggle: ON]   ● Building image...             │\n    33→│                                                                 │\n    34→└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n    35→```\n    36→\n    37→### Behavior\n    38→\n    39→#### Toggle\n    40→\n    41→- Reads and writes `ralph.sandbox.enabled` in `settings.json`\n    42→- Default state: OFF\n    43→- Toggling ON triggers an immediate Docker availability check\n    44→- Toggling OFF requires no validation — loops revert to direct subprocess execution\n    45→\n    46→#### Inline Status Text\n    47→\n    48→Displayed next to the toggle only when sandbox is enabled. Shows one of:\n    49→\n    50→| Condition | Status Text | Style |\n    51→|-----------|-------------|-------|\n    52→| Docker running + image built | `Docker running` | Green dot |\n    53→| Docker running + image not built | `Building image...` | Amber dot (auto-builds on first enable) |\n    54→| Docker installed but not running | `Docker not running` | Red dot + guidance text |\n    55→| Docker not installed | `Docker Desktop required` | Red dot + install guidance |\n    56→\n    57→Status is checked:\n    58→1. On page load (if toggle is ON)\n    59→2. Immediately when toggle is switched ON\n    60→3. No polling — manual page refresh for updated status\n    61→\n    62→#### What Is NOT in the Dashboard\n    63→\n    64→The following are configured via `settings.json` only (not surfaced in the dashboard in this phase):\n    65→\n    66→- Credential toggles and custom mounts (`sandbox.credentials.*`)\n    67→- Access profiles (`sandbox.profiles.*`)\n    68→- Model-to-profile defaults (`sandbox.model_defaults`)\n    69→- Image name override (`sandbox.image`)\n    70→- Network policy (`sandbox.network`)\n    71→- OpenCode serve port and auto-start (`sandbox.opencode_serve.*`)\n    72→- Container listing, start/stop controls\n    73→- Credential validation (\"Test Credentials\")\n    74→- Image rebuild button\n    75→\n    76→These features are fully functional via the settings file and internal API, but are deferred from the dashboard UI to keep the initial experience minimal.\n    77→\n    78→### API Endpoints\n    79→\n    80→```\n    81→GET  /api/sandbox/status\n    82→  Returns: { docker_available, docker_running, image_built, image_name }\n    83→  Used by: Dashboard toggle to show inline status\n    84→\n    85→PUT  /api/sandbox/settings\n    86→  Body: { \"enabled\": true|false }\n    87→  Returns: validation result\n    88→  Used by: Dashboard toggle to persist state\n    89→```\n    90→\n    91→All other sandbox API endpoints (credential validation, container listing, serve management, image build) exist as internal APIs for programmatic use but are not called by the dashboard in this phase.\n    92→\n    93→### Detection on Page Load\n    94→\n    95→When the Ralph settings section loads:\n    96→\n    97→1. Read current `sandbox.enabled` state → set toggle position\n    98→2. If enabled, call `GET /api/sandbox/status` → display inline status text\n    99→3. If disabled, no status check needed\n   100→\n   101→### Save Flow\n   102→\n   103→1. User flips the toggle\n   104→2. Frontend sends `PUT /api/sandbox/settings` with `{ \"enabled\": true }` or `{ \"enabled\": false }`\n   105→3. Backend writes to `settings.json`\n   106→4. If enabling: also calls status check and displays result inline\n   107→5. If disabling: clears inline status text\n   108→\n   109→## Edge Cases\n   110→\n   111→- **Docker not installed**: Toggle can be switched ON, but inline status shows \"Docker Desktop required\" with install guidance. Loops will fail at container creation time with a clear error.\n   112→- **Docker not running**: Toggle can be switched ON, but inline status shows \"Docker not running.\" User must start Docker Desktop themselves.\n   113→- **Settings file locked**: Save fails with generic \"Could not write settings\" error.\n   114→- **Image auto-build on first enable**: When sandbox is first enabled and no image exists, Vista queues an image build. Status shows \"Building image...\" until complete.\n   115→\n   116→## Dependencies\n   117→\n   118→- `vista/server/routes/` — Sandbox status endpoint\n   119→- `vista/server/views/` — Toggle control in Ralph settings area\n   120→- Spec: [settings](settings.md) — Reads/writes `ralph.sandbox.enabled`\n   121→\n   122→## Testing Strategy\n   123→\n   124→- API test: `GET /api/sandbox/status` returns correct Docker and image state\n   125→- API test: `PUT /api/sandbox/settings` with `enabled: true` and `enabled: false`\n   126→- Frontend test: toggle renders correct state from settings\n   127→- Frontend test: inline status text appears when enabled, hidden when disabled\n   128→- Frontend test: error states display actionable guidance\n   129→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14b921d9-eeaf-453d-9533-337d6f497996","uuid":"348bdc8d-255e-46b4-b609-2a9a739a762c","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/.vista/features/docker-sandbox/specs/dashboard-ui.md","content":"# Spec: Dashboard UI for Sandbox Settings\n\n## Problem Statement\n\nUsers need a simple way to enable or disable Docker sandboxing for ralph loops. The dashboard should surface a single toggle and provide clear inline feedback when something is wrong (e.g., Docker not installed or not running). Advanced sandbox configuration (credentials, profiles, model defaults, container controls, opencode serve management) is handled via `settings.json` — not the dashboard — in this phase.\n\n## Proposed Solution\n\nA single **toggle control** in the Vista dashboard's Ralph settings area, bound to `ralph.sandbox.enabled`. Optionally, inline status text next to the toggle communicates readiness or errors.\n\n### UI Layout\n\n```\n┌─ Ralph Settings ───────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                                                                 │\n│  ...existing ralph settings (provider, model, iterations)...    │\n│                                                                 │\n│  Docker Sandbox  [toggle: OFF]                                  │\n│                                                                 │\n│  ─── When toggled ON: ─────────────────────────────────────── │\n│                                                                 │\n│  Docker Sandbox  [toggle: ON]   ● Docker running                │\n│                                                                 │\n│  ─── Or, if Docker is unavailable: ───────────────────────── │\n│                                                                 │\n│  Docker Sandbox  [toggle: ON]   ✕ Docker not running            │\n│                                    Install Docker Desktop and   │\n│                                    ensure it is running.        │\n│                                                                 │\n│  ─── Or, if image not built: ─────────────────────────────── │\n│                                                                 │\n│  Docker Sandbox  [toggle: ON]   ● Building image...             │\n│                                                                 │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Behavior\n\n#### Toggle\n\n- Reads and writes `ralph.sandbox.enabled` in `settings.json`\n- Default state: OFF\n- Toggling ON triggers an immediate Docker availability check\n- Toggling OFF requires no validation — loops revert to direct subprocess execution\n\n#### Inline Status Text\n\nDisplayed next to the toggle only when sandbox is enabled. Shows one of:\n\n| Condition | Status Text | Style |\n|-----------|-------------|-------|\n| Docker running + image built | `Docker running` | Green dot |\n| Docker running + image not built | `Building image...` | Amber dot (auto-builds on first enable) |\n| Docker installed but not running | `Docker not running` | Red dot + guidance text |\n| Docker not installed | `Docker Desktop required` | Red dot + install guidance |\n\nStatus is checked:\n1. On page load (if toggle is ON)\n2. Immediately when toggle is switched ON\n3. No polling — manual page refresh for updated status\n\n#### What Is NOT in the Dashboard\n\nThe following are configured via `settings.json` only (not surfaced in the dashboard in this phase):\n\n- Credential toggles and custom mounts (`sandbox.credentials.*`)\n- Access profiles (`sandbox.profiles.*`)\n- Model-to-profile defaults (`sandbox.model_defaults`)\n- Image name override (`sandbox.image`)\n- Network policy (`sandbox.network`)\n- OpenCode serve port and auto-start (`sandbox.opencode_serve.*`)\n- Container listing, start/stop controls\n- Credential validation (\"Test Credentials\")\n- Image rebuild button\n\nThese features are fully functional via the settings file and internal API, but are deferred from the dashboard UI to keep the initial experience minimal.\n\n### API Endpoints\n\n```\nGET  /api/sandbox/status\n  Returns: { docker_available, docker_running, image_built, image_name }\n  Used by: Dashboard toggle to show inline status\n\nPUT  /api/sandbox/settings\n  Body: { \"enabled\": true|false }\n  Returns: validation result\n  Used by: Dashboard toggle to persist state\n```\n\nAll other sandbox API endpoints (credential validation, container listing, serve management, image build) exist as internal APIs for programmatic use but are not called by the dashboard in this phase.\n\n### Detection on Page Load\n\nWhen the Ralph settings section loads:\n\n1. Read current `sandbox.enabled` state → set toggle position\n2. If enabled, call `GET /api/sandbox/status` → display inline status text\n3. If disabled, no status check needed\n\n### Save Flow\n\n1. User flips the toggle\n2. Frontend sends `PUT /api/sandbox/settings` with `{ \"enabled\": true }` or `{ \"enabled\": false }`\n3. Backend writes to `settings.json`\n4. If enabling: also calls status check and displays result inline\n5. If disabling: clears inline status text\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- **Docker not installed**: Toggle can be switched ON, but inline status shows \"Docker Desktop required\" with install guidance. Loops will fail at container creation time with a clear error.\n- **Docker not running**: Toggle can be switched ON, but inline status shows \"Docker not running.\" User must start Docker Desktop themselves.\n- **Settings file locked**: Save fails with generic \"Could not write settings\" error.\n- **Image auto-build on first enable**: When sandbox is first enabled and no image exists, Vista queues an image build. Status shows \"Building image...\" until complete.\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- `vista/server/routes/` — Sandbox status endpoint\n- `vista/server/views/` — Toggle control in Ralph settings area\n- Spec: [settings](settings.md) — Reads/writes `ralph.sandbox.enabled`\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n- API test: `GET /api/sandbox/status` returns correct Docker and image state\n- API test: `PUT /api/sandbox/settings` with `enabled: true` and `enabled: false`\n- Frontend test: toggle renders correct state from settings\n- Frontend test: inline status text appears when enabled, hidden when disabled\n- Frontend test: error states display actionable guidance\n","numLines":129,"startLine":1,"totalLines":129}}}
