{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C7p7BqEJBhv75FgdGexWXa","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Spec: Ralph MCP Tool Integration\n     2→\n     3→## Problem Statement\n     4→\n     5→The `ralph-mcp-tool` feature exposes MCP tools for programmatic loop orchestration: `ralph_providers`, `ralph_start`, `ralph_status`, `ralph_summary`, `ralph_stop`. When sandbox mode is enabled, `ralph_start` must route loop execution through `ContainerManager` instead of spawning a local subprocess — transparently, without changing the MCP tool interface.\n     6→\n     7→## Integration Point: `RalphService.create_job()`\n     8→\n     9→`RalphService` is the single entry point for loop execution. Only the job creation and execution path needs a sandbox branch.\n    10→\n    11→### Current Flow (no sandbox)\n    12→\n    13→```\n    14→ralph_start MCP tool\n    15→  → RalphService.create_job(provider, model, mode, feature, ...)\n    16→    → Generate loop.ps1 from LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE\n    17→    → subprocess.Popen([\"powershell\", \"-File\", \"loop.ps1\"], cwd=project_root)\n    18→    → Track PID in job.json\n    19→    → Return job_id\n    20→```\n    21→\n    22→### Sandbox Flow — Claude Code\n    23→\n    24→```\n    25→ralph_start MCP tool (provider=claude)\n    26→  → RalphService.create_job(provider, model, mode, feature, ...)\n    27→    → check settings.ralph.sandbox.enabled\n    28→    → Generate loop.sh from LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE (always bash in container)\n    29→    → Gather credentials (claude_auth + git_ssh + git_config)\n    30→    → ContainerManager.create_loop_container(\n    31→          job_id, \"claude\", project_root, credentials, image\n    32→      )\n    33→    → ContainerManager.exec_in_container(\n    34→          container_name=\"vista-ralph-{job_id}\",\n    35→          command=[\"bash\", \"/workspace/.vista/ralph/{slug}/{job_id}/loop.sh\"],\n    36→          workdir=\"/workspace\",\n    37→          stdout_handle=output_log\n    38→      )\n    39→    → Track exec host PID + container name in job.json\n    40→    → Return job_id\n    41→```\n    42→\n    43→Inside the container, `loop.sh` runs `claude -p` natively — identical to current behavior but sandboxed.\n    44→\n    45→### Sandbox Flow — OpenCode\n    46→\n    47→```\n    48→ralph_start MCP tool (provider=opencode)\n    49→  → RalphService.create_job(provider, model, mode, feature, ...)\n    50→    → check settings.ralph.sandbox.enabled\n    51→    → Ensure opencode serve is running on host\n    52→    → Create opencode serve session (scoped to project root)\n    53→    → Generate loop.sh from OPENCODE_SANDBOX_LOOP_TEMPLATE\n    54→    → Gather credentials (git_ssh + git_config only — no AI creds)\n    55→    → ContainerManager.create_loop_container(\n    56→          job_id, \"opencode\", project_root, credentials, image\n    57→      )\n    58→    → ContainerManager.exec_in_container(\n    59→          container_name=\"vista-ralph-{job_id}\",\n    60→          command=[\"bash\", \"/workspace/.vista/ralph/{slug}/{job_id}/loop.sh\"],\n    61→          workdir=\"/workspace\",\n    62→          env={\n    63→              \"VISTA_HOST\": \"host.docker.internal\",\n    64→              \"VISTA_PORT\": str(vista_port),\n    65→              \"OPENCODE_SESSION\": session_id,\n    66→              \"MODEL\": model,\n    67→          },\n    68→          stdout_handle=output_log\n    69→      )\n    70→    → Track exec host PID + container name + session_id in job.json\n    71→    → Return job_id\n    72→```\n    73→\n    74→Inside the container, `loop.sh` uses `curl` to call the Vista proxy endpoint instead of invoking `opencode run`.\n    75→\n    76→### Loop Script Templates\n    77→\n    78→**Claude Code sandbox loop (bash):**\n    79→\n    80→Uses the existing `LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE` with `shell=\"sh\"` — the Claude invocation block already supports bash:\n    81→\n    82→```bash\n    83→printf \"%s\" \"$PROMPT_CONTENT\" | claude -p \\\n    84→    --dangerously-skip-permissions \\\n    85→    --output-format=stream-json \\\n    86→    --model \"$MODEL\" \\\n    87→    --verbose\n    88→```\n    89→\n    90→No changes needed to the Claude invocation. The template generates bash instead of PowerShell when running in sandbox mode.\n    91→\n    92→**OpenCode sandbox loop (bash) — new template:**\n    93→\n    94→```bash\n    95→# OpenCode Sandbox Loop - calls Vista proxy instead of opencode CLI\n    96→# Auto-generated by ralph service\n    97→\n    98→FEATURE_DIR=\"{feature_dir}\"\n    99→PROJECT_ROOT=\"/workspace\"\n   100→MODE=\"{mode}\"\n   101→MODEL=\"$MODEL\"\n   102→MAX_ITERATIONS={max_iterations}\n   103→VISTA_API=\"http://$VISTA_HOST:$VISTA_PORT/api/sandbox/opencode/$OPENCODE_SESSION\"\n   104→\n   105→PROMPT_FILE=\"$FEATURE_DIR/PROMPT_$MODE.md\"\n   106→PROGRESS_FILE=\"$FEATURE_DIR/progress.txt\"\n   107→TASK_FILE=\"$FEATURE_DIR/task.md\"\n   108→\n   109→CURRENT_BRANCH=$(git branch --show-current)\n   110→\n   111→echo \"━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\"\n   112→echo \"Feature:  {feature_name}\"\n   113→echo \"Provider: OpenCode (via Vista proxy)\"\n   114→echo \"Mode:     $MODE\"\n   115→echo \"Model:    $MODEL\"\n   116→echo \"Branch:   $CURRENT_BRANCH\"\n   117→echo \"━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\"\n   118→\n   119→if [ ! -f \"$PROMPT_FILE\" ]; then\n   120→    echo \"Error: $PROMPT_FILE not found\"\n   121→    exit 1\n   122→fi\n   123→\n   124→ITERATION=0\n   125→\n   126→while true; do\n   127→    if [ \"$MAX_ITERATIONS\" -gt 0 ] && [ \"$ITERATION\" -ge \"$MAX_ITERATIONS\" ]; then\n   128→        echo \"Reached max iterations: $MAX_ITERATIONS\"\n   129→        break\n   130→    fi\n   131→\n   132→    ITERATION=$((ITERATION + 1))\n   133→    echo \"\"\n   134→    echo \"======================== ITERATION $ITERATION ========================\"\n   135→    echo \"Started: $(date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M')\"\n   136→\n   137→    # Build prompt with task + progress context\n   138→    PROMPT_CONTENT=$(cat \"$PROMPT_FILE\")\n   139→    if [ -f \"$TASK_FILE\" ]; then\n   140→        TASK_CONTENT=$(cat \"$TASK_FILE\")\n   141→        PROMPT_CONTENT=\"$PROMPT_CONTENT\n   142→\n   143→## Task\n   144→$TASK_CONTENT\"\n   145→    fi\n   146→    if [ -f \"$PROGRESS_FILE\" ]; then\n   147→        PROGRESS_CONTENT=$(cat \"$PROGRESS_FILE\")\n   148→        PROMPT_CONTENT=\"$PROMPT_CONTENT\n   149→\n   150→## Current Progress\n   151→$PROGRESS_CONTENT\"\n   152→    fi\n   153→\n   154→    # Send prompt to OpenCode via Vista proxy\n   155→    RESPONSE=$(curl -s -X POST \"$VISTA_API/message\" \\\n   156→        -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n   157→        -d \"$(jq -n --arg prompt \"$PROMPT_CONTENT\" --arg model \"$MODEL\" \\\n   158→            '{prompt: $prompt, model: $model}')\")\n   159→\n   160→    if [ $? -ne 0 ]; then\n   161→        echo \"Failed to reach Vista proxy\"\n   162→        exit 1\n   163→    fi\n   164→\n   165→    # Push changes after each iteration\n   166→    git push origin \"$CURRENT_BRANCH\" 2>/dev/null || \\\n   167→        git push -u origin \"$CURRENT_BRANCH\"\n   168→\n   169→    echo \"\"\n   170→    echo \"[$(date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M')] ITERATION $ITERATION complete\"\n   171→\n   172→    # Check completion (build mode)\n   173→    if [ \"$MODE\" = \"build\" ] && [ -f \"$PROGRESS_FILE\" ]; then\n   174→        if grep -q \"ALL PHASES COMPLETE\" \"$PROGRESS_FILE\"; then\n   175→            echo \"All phases complete! Stopping loop.\"\n   176→            break\n   177→        fi\n   178→    fi\n   179→done\n   180→\n   181→echo \"\"\n   182→echo \"━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\"\n   183→echo \"Loop finished after $ITERATION iteration(s)\"\n   184→echo \"━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\"\n   185→```\n   186→\n   187→### Vista Proxy Endpoint\n   188→\n   189→Vista exposes an endpoint that forwards to `opencode serve`:\n   190→\n   191→```python\n   192→# vista/server/routes/sandbox.py\n   193→\n   194→@router.post(\"/api/sandbox/opencode/{session_id}/message\")\n   195→async def opencode_proxy_message(session_id: str, request: Request):\n   196→    \"\"\"Forward a message to the opencode serve session.\n   197→\n   198→    1. Validate session_id exists\n   199→    2. Forward request body to opencode serve API\n   200→    3. Stream response back to caller (container)\n   201→    4. opencode serve handles AI reasoning + file operations on host\n   202→    5. File changes visible in container via bind mount\n   203→    \"\"\"\n   204→```\n   205→\n   206→## Impact on Each MCP Tool\n   207→\n   208→| MCP Tool | Change Required | Notes |\n   209→|----------|----------------|-------|\n   210→| `ralph_providers` | None | Discovers providers from host CLI — sandbox irrelevant |\n   211→| `ralph_start` | **Yes** — sandbox branch in `create_job()` | Routes to container + serve based on provider |\n   212→| `ralph_status` | Minor | Check container status in addition to PID |\n   213→| `ralph_summary` | None | Reads artifacts from job directory on host (mounted into container) |\n   214→| `ralph_stop` | Minor | Kill exec PID + remove container + close serve session |\n   215→\n   216→### `ralph_stop` with Sandbox\n   217→\n   218→```python\n   219→async def stop_job(self, job_id: str):\n   220→    job = self._load_job(job_id)\n   221→\n   222→    if job.get(\"sandbox\"):\n   223→        # Kill the exec process (terminates loop script in container)\n   224→        self._kill_pid(job[\"pid\"])\n   225→        # Close opencode serve session (if OpenCode loop)\n   226→        if job.get(\"opencode_session\"):\n   227→            await self.opencode_serve_manager.close_session(job_id)\n   228→        # Remove the container\n   229→        await self.container_manager.remove_container(f\"vista-ralph-{job_id}\")\n   230→    else:\n   231→        # Current behavior: kill local subprocess\n   232→        self._kill_pid(job[\"pid\"])\n   233→```\n   234→\n   235→## Job Metadata Extension\n   236→\n   237→When sandbox is active, `job.json` records additional fields:\n   238→\n   239→```json\n   240→{\n   241→  \"job_id\": \"a1b2c3d4\",\n   242→  \"slug\": \"my-feature\",\n   243→  \"mode\": \"build\",\n   244→  \"status\": \"running\",\n   245→  \"provider\": \"opencode\",\n   246→  \"model\": \"claude-sonnet-4\",\n   247→  \"pid\": 12345,\n   248→  \"sandbox\": true,\n   249→  \"container\": \"vista-ralph-a1b2c3d4\",\n   250→  \"opencode_session\": \"sess_xyz789\"\n   251→}\n   252→```\n   253→\n   254→For Claude Code loops, `opencode_session` is absent. When sandbox is disabled, `sandbox` is `false` and `container`/`opencode_session` are absent.\n   255→\n   256→## Loop Script Template Selection\n   257→\n   258→```python\n   259→def _get_loop_template(self, provider: Provider, sandbox_enabled: bool) -> str:\n   260→    if not sandbox_enabled:\n   261→        # Current behavior: platform-specific (ps1 or sh)\n   262→        return LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE  # PowerShell on Windows, bash on Linux/macOS\n   263→\n   264→    if provider.name == \"claude\":\n   265→        # Claude Code runs natively inside Linux container\n   266→        return LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE  # Use bash variant (shell=\"sh\")\n   267→\n   268→    if provider.name == \"opencode\":\n   269→        # OpenCode calls Vista proxy from inside container\n   270→        return OPENCODE_SANDBOX_LOOP_TEMPLATE  # New template\n   271→\n   272→    raise ValueError(f\"Unknown provider for sandbox: {provider.name}\")\n   273→```\n   274→\n   275→## Project Root Mounting — Agent Access\n   276→\n   277→The container always mounts the full project root at `/workspace/`:\n   278→\n   279→```\n   280→/workspace/\n   281→  ├── .vista/\n   282→  │   ├── features/\n   283→  │   │   └── {slug}/              ← feature specs, PRDs, arch docs\n   284→  │   │       ├── specs/\n   285→  │   │       ├── task.md\n   286→  │   │       └── PROMPT_build.md\n   287→  │   └── ralph/\n   288→  │       └── {slug}/\n   289→  │           └── {job_id}/        ← job directory\n   290→  │               ├── job.json\n   291→  │               ├── loop.sh\n   292→  │               ├── output.log\n   293→  │               └── progress.txt\n   294→  ├── src/                         ← source code\n   295→  ├── tests/                       ← test files\n   296→  ├── .git/                        ← git repo (commit + push)\n   297→  ├── CLAUDE.md                    ← project instructions\n   298→  └── ...                          ← everything else in project\n   299→```\n   300→\n   301→This ensures:\n   302→- Agents can read feature specs to understand requirements\n   303→- Agents can read/write source code and tests\n   304→- Agents can commit and push (`.git/` + SSH keys mounted)\n   305→- Progress tracking files are in the job directory\n   306→- `CLAUDE.md` and other project config is visible\n   307→\n   308→## Settings Namespace\n   309→\n   310→Both features share the `ralph` settings namespace:\n   311→\n   312→```json\n   313→{\n   314→  \"ralph\": {\n   315→    \"defaults\": { \"...\" : \"...\" },\n   316→    \"providers\": { \"...\" : \"...\" },\n   317→    \"summarizer\": { \"...\" : \"...\" },\n   318→    \"sandbox\": {\n   319→      \"enabled\": false,\n   320→      \"image\": \"vista-ralph:latest\",\n   321→      \"network\": true,\n   322→      \"opencode_serve_port\": 4096,\n   323→      \"credentials\": { \"...\" : \"...\" },\n   324→      \"profiles\": { \"...\" : \"...\" },\n   325→      \"model_defaults\": { \"...\" : \"...\" }\n   326→    }\n   327→  }\n   328→}\n   329→```\n   330→\n   331→## Implementation Order\n   332→\n   333→1. **ralph-mcp-tool** — implement `RalphService` with local subprocess spawning (done/in-progress)\n   334→2. **docker-sandbox phase 1** — `ContainerManager` + Claude Code sandbox path\n   335→3. **docker-sandbox phase 2** — `OpenCodeServeManager` + proxy endpoint + OpenCode sandbox path\n   336→\n   337→## Dependencies\n   338→\n   339→- Spec: [container-lifecycle](container-lifecycle.md) — `ContainerManager` and `OpenCodeServeManager` APIs\n   340→- Spec: [credential-management](credential-management.md) — credential gathering per provider\n   341→- Spec: [settings](settings.md) — `ralph.sandbox` settings schema\n   342→- Feature: `ralph-mcp-tool` — `RalphService`, MCP tool definitions, job management\n   343→\n   344→## Testing Strategy\n   345→\n   346→- Unit test: `create_job()` routes to `ContainerManager` when `sandbox.enabled = true`\n   347→- Unit test: `create_job()` uses local subprocess when `sandbox.enabled = false`\n   348→- Unit test: Claude Code loops use bash loop template with native `claude -p`\n   349→- Unit test: OpenCode loops use proxy loop template with `curl` calls\n   350→- Unit test: job.json includes sandbox metadata when sandbox active\n   351→- Integration test: full `ralph_start` → `ralph_status` → `ralph_stop` cycle with sandbox (Claude path)\n   352→- Integration test: full cycle with sandbox (OpenCode path via serve proxy)\n   353→- Integration test: `ralph_summary` reads artifacts produced inside container\n   354→- Integration test: `ralph_stop` kills exec, closes session, removes container\n   355→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14b921d9-eeaf-453d-9533-337d6f497996","uuid":"6708d5bd-c6fc-4289-9d51-585469a035be","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/.vista/features/docker-sandbox/specs/ralph-mcp-integration.md","content":"# Spec: Ralph MCP Tool Integration\n\n## Problem Statement\n\nThe `ralph-mcp-tool` feature exposes MCP tools for programmatic loop orchestration: `ralph_providers`, `ralph_start`, `ralph_status`, `ralph_summary`, `ralph_stop`. When sandbox mode is enabled, `ralph_start` must route loop execution through `ContainerManager` instead of spawning a local subprocess — transparently, without changing the MCP tool interface.\n\n## Integration Point: `RalphService.create_job()`\n\n`RalphService` is the single entry point for loop execution. Only the job creation and execution path needs a sandbox branch.\n\n### Current Flow (no sandbox)\n\n```\nralph_start MCP tool\n  → RalphService.create_job(provider, model, mode, feature, ...)\n    → Generate loop.ps1 from LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE\n    → subprocess.Popen([\"powershell\", \"-File\", \"loop.ps1\"], cwd=project_root)\n    → Track PID in job.json\n    → Return job_id\n```\n\n### Sandbox Flow — Claude Code\n\n```\nralph_start MCP tool (provider=claude)\n  → RalphService.create_job(provider, model, mode, feature, ...)\n    → check settings.ralph.sandbox.enabled\n    → Generate loop.sh from LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE (always bash in container)\n    → Gather credentials (claude_auth + git_ssh + git_config)\n    → ContainerManager.create_loop_container(\n          job_id, \"claude\", project_root, credentials, image\n      )\n    → ContainerManager.exec_in_container(\n          container_name=\"vista-ralph-{job_id}\",\n          command=[\"bash\", \"/workspace/.vista/ralph/{slug}/{job_id}/loop.sh\"],\n          workdir=\"/workspace\",\n          stdout_handle=output_log\n      )\n    → Track exec host PID + container name in job.json\n    → Return job_id\n```\n\nInside the container, `loop.sh` runs `claude -p` natively — identical to current behavior but sandboxed.\n\n### Sandbox Flow — OpenCode\n\n```\nralph_start MCP tool (provider=opencode)\n  → RalphService.create_job(provider, model, mode, feature, ...)\n    → check settings.ralph.sandbox.enabled\n    → Ensure opencode serve is running on host\n    → Create opencode serve session (scoped to project root)\n    → Generate loop.sh from OPENCODE_SANDBOX_LOOP_TEMPLATE\n    → Gather credentials (git_ssh + git_config only — no AI creds)\n    → ContainerManager.create_loop_container(\n          job_id, \"opencode\", project_root, credentials, image\n      )\n    → ContainerManager.exec_in_container(\n          container_name=\"vista-ralph-{job_id}\",\n          command=[\"bash\", \"/workspace/.vista/ralph/{slug}/{job_id}/loop.sh\"],\n          workdir=\"/workspace\",\n          env={\n              \"VISTA_HOST\": \"host.docker.internal\",\n              \"VISTA_PORT\": str(vista_port),\n              \"OPENCODE_SESSION\": session_id,\n              \"MODEL\": model,\n          },\n          stdout_handle=output_log\n      )\n    → Track exec host PID + container name + session_id in job.json\n    → Return job_id\n```\n\nInside the container, `loop.sh` uses `curl` to call the Vista proxy endpoint instead of invoking `opencode run`.\n\n### Loop Script Templates\n\n**Claude Code sandbox loop (bash):**\n\nUses the existing `LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE` with `shell=\"sh\"` — the Claude invocation block already supports bash:\n\n```bash\nprintf \"%s\" \"$PROMPT_CONTENT\" | claude -p \\\n    --dangerously-skip-permissions \\\n    --output-format=stream-json \\\n    --model \"$MODEL\" \\\n    --verbose\n```\n\nNo changes needed to the Claude invocation. The template generates bash instead of PowerShell when running in sandbox mode.\n\n**OpenCode sandbox loop (bash) — new template:**\n\n```bash\n# OpenCode Sandbox Loop - calls Vista proxy instead of opencode CLI\n# Auto-generated by ralph service\n\nFEATURE_DIR=\"{feature_dir}\"\nPROJECT_ROOT=\"/workspace\"\nMODE=\"{mode}\"\nMODEL=\"$MODEL\"\nMAX_ITERATIONS={max_iterations}\nVISTA_API=\"http://$VISTA_HOST:$VISTA_PORT/api/sandbox/opencode/$OPENCODE_SESSION\"\n\nPROMPT_FILE=\"$FEATURE_DIR/PROMPT_$MODE.md\"\nPROGRESS_FILE=\"$FEATURE_DIR/progress.txt\"\nTASK_FILE=\"$FEATURE_DIR/task.md\"\n\nCURRENT_BRANCH=$(git branch --show-current)\n\necho \"━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\"\necho \"Feature:  {feature_name}\"\necho \"Provider: OpenCode (via Vista proxy)\"\necho \"Mode:     $MODE\"\necho \"Model:    $MODEL\"\necho \"Branch:   $CURRENT_BRANCH\"\necho \"━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\"\n\nif [ ! -f \"$PROMPT_FILE\" ]; then\n    echo \"Error: $PROMPT_FILE not found\"\n    exit 1\nfi\n\nITERATION=0\n\nwhile true; do\n    if [ \"$MAX_ITERATIONS\" -gt 0 ] && [ \"$ITERATION\" -ge \"$MAX_ITERATIONS\" ]; then\n        echo \"Reached max iterations: $MAX_ITERATIONS\"\n        break\n    fi\n\n    ITERATION=$((ITERATION + 1))\n    echo \"\"\n    echo \"======================== ITERATION $ITERATION ========================\"\n    echo \"Started: $(date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M')\"\n\n    # Build prompt with task + progress context\n    PROMPT_CONTENT=$(cat \"$PROMPT_FILE\")\n    if [ -f \"$TASK_FILE\" ]; then\n        TASK_CONTENT=$(cat \"$TASK_FILE\")\n        PROMPT_CONTENT=\"$PROMPT_CONTENT\n\n## Task\n$TASK_CONTENT\"\n    fi\n    if [ -f \"$PROGRESS_FILE\" ]; then\n        PROGRESS_CONTENT=$(cat \"$PROGRESS_FILE\")\n        PROMPT_CONTENT=\"$PROMPT_CONTENT\n\n## Current Progress\n$PROGRESS_CONTENT\"\n    fi\n\n    # Send prompt to OpenCode via Vista proxy\n    RESPONSE=$(curl -s -X POST \"$VISTA_API/message\" \\\n        -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n        -d \"$(jq -n --arg prompt \"$PROMPT_CONTENT\" --arg model \"$MODEL\" \\\n            '{prompt: $prompt, model: $model}')\")\n\n    if [ $? -ne 0 ]; then\n        echo \"Failed to reach Vista proxy\"\n        exit 1\n    fi\n\n    # Push changes after each iteration\n    git push origin \"$CURRENT_BRANCH\" 2>/dev/null || \\\n        git push -u origin \"$CURRENT_BRANCH\"\n\n    echo \"\"\n    echo \"[$(date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M')] ITERATION $ITERATION complete\"\n\n    # Check completion (build mode)\n    if [ \"$MODE\" = \"build\" ] && [ -f \"$PROGRESS_FILE\" ]; then\n        if grep -q \"ALL PHASES COMPLETE\" \"$PROGRESS_FILE\"; then\n            echo \"All phases complete! Stopping loop.\"\n            break\n        fi\n    fi\ndone\n\necho \"\"\necho \"━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\"\necho \"Loop finished after $ITERATION iteration(s)\"\necho \"━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\"\n```\n\n### Vista Proxy Endpoint\n\nVista exposes an endpoint that forwards to `opencode serve`:\n\n```python\n# vista/server/routes/sandbox.py\n\n@router.post(\"/api/sandbox/opencode/{session_id}/message\")\nasync def opencode_proxy_message(session_id: str, request: Request):\n    \"\"\"Forward a message to the opencode serve session.\n\n    1. Validate session_id exists\n    2. Forward request body to opencode serve API\n    3. Stream response back to caller (container)\n    4. opencode serve handles AI reasoning + file operations on host\n    5. File changes visible in container via bind mount\n    \"\"\"\n```\n\n## Impact on Each MCP Tool\n\n| MCP Tool | Change Required | Notes |\n|----------|----------------|-------|\n| `ralph_providers` | None | Discovers providers from host CLI — sandbox irrelevant |\n| `ralph_start` | **Yes** — sandbox branch in `create_job()` | Routes to container + serve based on provider |\n| `ralph_status` | Minor | Check container status in addition to PID |\n| `ralph_summary` | None | Reads artifacts from job directory on host (mounted into container) |\n| `ralph_stop` | Minor | Kill exec PID + remove container + close serve session |\n\n### `ralph_stop` with Sandbox\n\n```python\nasync def stop_job(self, job_id: str):\n    job = self._load_job(job_id)\n\n    if job.get(\"sandbox\"):\n        # Kill the exec process (terminates loop script in container)\n        self._kill_pid(job[\"pid\"])\n        # Close opencode serve session (if OpenCode loop)\n        if job.get(\"opencode_session\"):\n            await self.opencode_serve_manager.close_session(job_id)\n        # Remove the container\n        await self.container_manager.remove_container(f\"vista-ralph-{job_id}\")\n    else:\n        # Current behavior: kill local subprocess\n        self._kill_pid(job[\"pid\"])\n```\n\n## Job Metadata Extension\n\nWhen sandbox is active, `job.json` records additional fields:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"job_id\": \"a1b2c3d4\",\n  \"slug\": \"my-feature\",\n  \"mode\": \"build\",\n  \"status\": \"running\",\n  \"provider\": \"opencode\",\n  \"model\": \"claude-sonnet-4\",\n  \"pid\": 12345,\n  \"sandbox\": true,\n  \"container\": \"vista-ralph-a1b2c3d4\",\n  \"opencode_session\": \"sess_xyz789\"\n}\n```\n\nFor Claude Code loops, `opencode_session` is absent. When sandbox is disabled, `sandbox` is `false` and `container`/`opencode_session` are absent.\n\n## Loop Script Template Selection\n\n```python\ndef _get_loop_template(self, provider: Provider, sandbox_enabled: bool) -> str:\n    if not sandbox_enabled:\n        # Current behavior: platform-specific (ps1 or sh)\n        return LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE  # PowerShell on Windows, bash on Linux/macOS\n\n    if provider.name == \"claude\":\n        # Claude Code runs natively inside Linux container\n        return LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE  # Use bash variant (shell=\"sh\")\n\n    if provider.name == \"opencode\":\n        # OpenCode calls Vista proxy from inside container\n        return OPENCODE_SANDBOX_LOOP_TEMPLATE  # New template\n\n    raise ValueError(f\"Unknown provider for sandbox: {provider.name}\")\n```\n\n## Project Root Mounting — Agent Access\n\nThe container always mounts the full project root at `/workspace/`:\n\n```\n/workspace/\n  ├── .vista/\n  │   ├── features/\n  │   │   └── {slug}/              ← feature specs, PRDs, arch docs\n  │   │       ├── specs/\n  │   │       ├── task.md\n  │   │       └── PROMPT_build.md\n  │   └── ralph/\n  │       └── {slug}/\n  │           └── {job_id}/        ← job directory\n  │               ├── job.json\n  │               ├── loop.sh\n  │               ├── output.log\n  │               └── progress.txt\n  ├── src/                         ← source code\n  ├── tests/                       ← test files\n  ├── .git/                        ← git repo (commit + push)\n  ├── CLAUDE.md                    ← project instructions\n  └── ...                          ← everything else in project\n```\n\nThis ensures:\n- Agents can read feature specs to understand requirements\n- Agents can read/write source code and tests\n- Agents can commit and push (`.git/` + SSH keys mounted)\n- Progress tracking files are in the job directory\n- `CLAUDE.md` and other project config is visible\n\n## Settings Namespace\n\nBoth features share the `ralph` settings namespace:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"ralph\": {\n    \"defaults\": { \"...\" : \"...\" },\n    \"providers\": { \"...\" : \"...\" },\n    \"summarizer\": { \"...\" : \"...\" },\n    \"sandbox\": {\n      \"enabled\": false,\n      \"image\": \"vista-ralph:latest\",\n      \"network\": true,\n      \"opencode_serve_port\": 4096,\n      \"credentials\": { \"...\" : \"...\" },\n      \"profiles\": { \"...\" : \"...\" },\n      \"model_defaults\": { \"...\" : \"...\" }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Implementation Order\n\n1. **ralph-mcp-tool** — implement `RalphService` with local subprocess spawning (done/in-progress)\n2. **docker-sandbox phase 1** — `ContainerManager` + Claude Code sandbox path\n3. **docker-sandbox phase 2** — `OpenCodeServeManager` + proxy endpoint + OpenCode sandbox path\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- Spec: [container-lifecycle](container-lifecycle.md) — `ContainerManager` and `OpenCodeServeManager` APIs\n- Spec: [credential-management](credential-management.md) — credential gathering per provider\n- Spec: [settings](settings.md) — `ralph.sandbox` settings schema\n- Feature: `ralph-mcp-tool` — `RalphService`, MCP tool definitions, job management\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n- Unit test: `create_job()` routes to `ContainerManager` when `sandbox.enabled = true`\n- Unit test: `create_job()` uses local subprocess when `sandbox.enabled = false`\n- Unit test: Claude Code loops use bash loop template with native `claude -p`\n- Unit test: OpenCode loops use proxy loop template with `curl` calls\n- Unit test: job.json includes sandbox metadata when sandbox active\n- Integration test: full `ralph_start` → `ralph_status` → `ralph_stop` cycle with sandbox (Claude path)\n- Integration test: full cycle with sandbox (OpenCode path via serve proxy)\n- Integration test: `ralph_summary` reads artifacts produced inside container\n- Integration test: `ralph_stop` kills exec, closes session, removes container\n","numLines":355,"startLine":1,"totalLines":355}}}
