{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018pkxWYb6HjDHRDvuLdk598","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Spec: Sandbox Settings\n     2→\n     3→## Problem Statement\n     4→\n     5→The Docker sandbox feature introduces new configuration: credential toggles, access profiles, image selection, network policy, model defaults, and OpenCode serve management. This must integrate cleanly into the existing `vista/settings.json` structure without breaking existing settings or requiring migration.\n     6→\n     7→## Proposed Solution\n     8→\n     9→Add a `sandbox` section under the existing `ralph` key in `vista/settings.json`. When `sandbox` is absent or `enabled` is `false`, all sandbox functionality is disabled and loops run as direct subprocesses (current behavior).\n    10→\n    11→### Full Settings Schema\n    12→\n    13→```json\n    14→{\n    15→  \"server\": {\n    16→    \"auto_start\": true,\n    17→    \"auto_open_browser\": true,\n    18→    \"host\": \"127.0.0.1\",\n    19→    \"port\": 3456\n    20→  },\n    21→  \"providers\": {\n    22→    \"claude\": { \"enabled\": true, \"display_name\": \"Claude Code\" },\n    23→    \"opencode\": { \"enabled\": true, \"display_name\": \"OpenCode\" }\n    24→  },\n    25→  \"ralph\": {\n    26→    \"defaults\": {\n    27→      \"provider\": \"claude\",\n    28→      \"model\": \"sonnet\",\n    29→      \"iterations\": 3\n    30→    },\n    31→    \"summarizer\": {\n    32→      \"provider\": \"claude\",\n    33→      \"model\": \"haiku\"\n    34→    },\n    35→    \"providers\": { \"...\" : \"...\" },\n    36→    \"sandbox\": {\n    37→      \"enabled\": false,\n    38→      \"image\": \"vista-ralph:latest\",\n    39→      \"network\": true,\n    40→      \"opencode_serve\": {\n    41→        \"port\": 4096,\n    42→        \"auto_start\": true\n    43→      },\n    44→      \"credentials\": {\n    45→        \"claude_auth\": true,\n    46→        \"git_ssh\": true,\n    47→        \"git_config\": true,\n    48→        \"github_cli\": false,\n    49→        \"custom\": []\n    50→      },\n    51→      \"profiles\": {\n    52→        \"full-access\": {\n    53→          \"mounts\": [\n    54→            { \"path\": \".\", \"mode\": \"rw\" }\n    55→          ]\n    56→        },\n    57→        \"feature-scoped\": {\n    58→          \"mounts\": [\n    59→            { \"path\": \".vista/features/${FEATURE}\", \"mode\": \"rw\" },\n    60→            { \"path\": \".vista/ralph/${FEATURE}\", \"mode\": \"rw\" },\n    61→            { \"path\": \"src\", \"mode\": \"rw\" },\n    62→            { \"path\": \"tests\", \"mode\": \"rw\" },\n    63→            { \"path\": \".git\", \"mode\": \"rw\" }\n    64→          ]\n    65→        },\n    66→        \"research-only\": {\n    67→          \"mounts\": [\n    68→            { \"path\": \".\", \"mode\": \"ro\" }\n    69→          ],\n    70→          \"network\": false\n    71→        }\n    72→      },\n    73→      \"model_defaults\": {\n    74→        \"haiku\": \"feature-scoped\",\n    75→        \"sonnet\": \"full-access\",\n    76→        \"opus\": \"full-access\"\n    77→      }\n    78→    }\n    79→  }\n    80→}\n    81→```\n    82→\n    83→### Field Reference\n    84→\n    85→| Field | Type | Default | Description |\n    86→|-------|------|---------|-------------|\n    87→| `sandbox.enabled` | bool | `false` | Master toggle. `false` = loops run as direct subprocesses. |\n    88→| `sandbox.image` | string | `\"vista-ralph:latest\"` | Docker image to use. Modified claudebox image. |\n    89→| `sandbox.network` | bool | `true` | Global network policy. `true` = containers have network access. |\n    90→| `sandbox.opencode_serve.port` | int | `4096` | Port for host-side `opencode serve` instance. |\n    91→| `sandbox.opencode_serve.auto_start` | bool | `true` | Auto-start `opencode serve` when first OpenCode sandbox loop runs. |\n    92→| `sandbox.credentials.claude_auth` | bool | `true` | Mount Claude Code auth (`~/.claude/` + `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`). Applied to Claude Code loops only. |\n    93→| `sandbox.credentials.git_ssh` | bool | `true` | Mount SSH keys for Git. Applied to all loops. |\n    94→| `sandbox.credentials.git_config` | bool | `true` | Mount `.gitconfig`. Applied to all loops. |\n    95→| `sandbox.credentials.github_cli` | bool | `false` | Mount GitHub CLI auth. Applied to all loops. |\n    96→| `sandbox.credentials.custom` | array | `[]` | User-defined mounts. |\n    97→| `sandbox.credentials.custom[].name` | string | required | Display name for the custom credential. |\n    98→| `sandbox.credentials.custom[].host_path` | string | required | Path on host. `~` expanded. |\n    99→| `sandbox.credentials.custom[].container_path` | string | required | Path inside container. |\n   100→| `sandbox.credentials.custom[].mode` | string | `\"ro\"` | `\"ro\"` or `\"rw\"`. |\n   101→| `sandbox.profiles` | object | built-ins | Named access profiles. Keys are profile names. |\n   102→| `sandbox.profiles.{name}.mounts` | array | required | List of mount specs. |\n   103→| `sandbox.profiles.{name}.mounts[].path` | string | required | Path relative to project root. Supports `${FEATURE}`. |\n   104→| `sandbox.profiles.{name}.mounts[].mode` | string | required | `\"rw\"` or `\"ro\"`. |\n   105→| `sandbox.profiles.{name}.network` | bool\\|undefined | inherit | Override global network policy. Omit to inherit. |\n   106→| `sandbox.model_defaults` | object | `{}` | Maps model names to profile names. |\n   107→\n   108→### UI Exposure (Current Phase)\n   109→\n   110→Only `sandbox.enabled` is exposed in the Vista dashboard as a toggle control. All other sandbox settings are configurable by editing `settings.json` directly. This keeps the dashboard minimal while preserving full configurability for power users and automation.\n   111→\n   112→| Field | Exposure | Notes |\n   113→|-------|----------|-------|\n   114→| `sandbox.enabled` | Dashboard toggle | Only field surfaced in dashboard UI |\n   115→| All other fields | `settings.json` only | Edit directly; validated on load |\n   116→\n   117→### Defaults Behavior\n   118→\n   119→When `sandbox` section is missing entirely:\n   120→\n   121→```python\n   122→DEFAULT_SANDBOX = {\n   123→    \"enabled\": False,\n   124→    \"image\": \"vista-ralph:latest\",\n   125→    \"network\": True,\n   126→    \"opencode_serve\": {\n   127→        \"port\": 4096,\n   128→        \"auto_start\": True,\n   129→    },\n   130→    \"credentials\": {\n   131→        \"claude_auth\": True,\n   132→        \"git_ssh\": True,\n   133→        \"git_config\": True,\n   134→        \"github_cli\": False,\n   135→        \"custom\": [],\n   136→    },\n   137→    \"profiles\": {\n   138→        \"full-access\": {\"mounts\": [{\"path\": \".\", \"mode\": \"rw\"}]},\n   139→        \"feature-scoped\": {\"mounts\": [\n   140→            {\"path\": \".vista/features/${FEATURE}\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n   141→            {\"path\": \".vista/ralph/${FEATURE}\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n   142→            {\"path\": \"src\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n   143→            {\"path\": \"tests\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n   144→            {\"path\": \".git\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n   145→        ]},\n   146→        \"research-only\": {\"mounts\": [{\"path\": \".\", \"mode\": \"ro\"}], \"network\": False},\n   147→    },\n   148→    \"model_defaults\": {},\n   149→}\n   150→```\n   151→\n   152→### Settings Loading\n   153→\n   154→Extend existing `vista/server/config.py`:\n   155→\n   156→```python\n   157→def get_sandbox_settings() -> dict:\n   158→    \"\"\"Load sandbox settings with defaults applied.\n   159→\n   160→    Returns fully-populated sandbox config dict.\n   161→    Missing keys are filled from DEFAULT_SANDBOX.\n   162→    \"\"\"\n   163→\n   164→def is_sandbox_enabled() -> bool:\n   165→    \"\"\"Quick check: is sandbox.enabled == true?\"\"\"\n   166→\n   167→def get_sandbox_profile(name: str) -> AccessProfile | None:\n   168→    \"\"\"Load a specific profile by name. Returns None if not found.\"\"\"\n   169→\n   170→def get_sandbox_credentials() -> dict:\n   171→    \"\"\"Load credential toggle states + custom mounts.\"\"\"\n   172→\n   173→def get_opencode_serve_settings() -> dict:\n   174→    \"\"\"Load opencode serve config (port, auto_start).\"\"\"\n   175→```\n   176→\n   177→### Settings Write-Back\n   178→\n   179→The dashboard writes only the `sandbox.enabled` toggle. All other sandbox settings are managed by editing `settings.json` directly. A general-purpose write-back function is available for internal API use:\n   180→\n   181→```python\n   182→def save_sandbox_settings(sandbox_config: dict) -> None:\n   183→    \"\"\"Write sandbox settings back to settings.json.\n   184→\n   185→    1. Read full settings.json\n   186→    2. Validate sandbox_config against schema\n   187→    3. Set settings[\"ralph\"][\"sandbox\"] = sandbox_config\n   188→    4. Write back with json.dumps(indent=2)\n   189→\n   190→    Preserves all other settings sections.\n   191→    \"\"\"\n   192→```\n   193→\n   194→### Validation\n   195→\n   196→On load and on save, validate:\n   197→\n   198→- `enabled` is boolean\n   199→- `image` is string\n   200→- `network` is boolean\n   201→- `opencode_serve.port` is integer 1024-65535\n   202→- `opencode_serve.auto_start` is boolean\n   203→- Each credential toggle is boolean\n   204→- Custom mounts have all required fields (`name`, `host_path`, `container_path`)\n   205→- Each profile has at least one mount\n   206→- Mount paths are relative, no `..` traversal\n   207→- Mount modes are `\"rw\"` or `\"ro\"`\n   208→- Profile names are alphanumeric + hyphens\n   209→- `model_defaults` values reference existing profile names\n   210→\n   211→Invalid config on load: log warning, apply defaults for invalid fields. Don't crash.\n   212→Invalid config on save: reject with validation errors returned to dashboard.\n   213→\n   214→## Edge Cases\n   215→\n   216→- **No `ralph` section at all**: Sandbox defaults are applied. `enabled` is `false`. No change in behavior.\n   217→- **`ralph` section exists but no `sandbox` key**: Same as above — defaults applied.\n   218→- **User deletes a profile that's referenced by `model_defaults`**: Validation warning on load. Model falls back to `full-access` at runtime.\n   219→- **User sets `image` to a non-existent image**: Container creation fails at runtime with clear error. Settings save succeeds (no Docker check at save time).\n   220→- **Port conflict for `opencode_serve`**: If configured port is in use, `OpenCodeServeManager` logs error and tries next available port.\n   221→- **Concurrent save from dashboard + MCP tool call**: Acceptable race. Next operation reads latest file.\n   222→\n   223→## Dependencies\n   224→\n   225→- `vista/server/config.py` (existing) - Extend with sandbox loading\n   226→- `vista/settings.json` (existing) - Extended with `sandbox` section\n   227→- Spec: [credential-management](credential-management.md) - Consumes credential toggles\n   228→- Spec: [access-profiles](access-profiles.md) - Consumes profile definitions\n   229→- Spec: [dashboard-ui](dashboard-ui.md) - Toggle for `sandbox.enabled` and inline status display\n   230→\n   231→## Testing Strategy\n   232→\n   233→- Unit tests for defaults application (missing section, partial section, empty section)\n   234→- Unit tests for validation (invalid modes, missing fields, path traversal rejection)\n   235→- Unit tests for settings write-back (preserves other sections, atomic)\n   236→- Unit tests for opencode_serve settings validation (port range)\n   237→- Integration test: modify settings → restart → settings loaded correctly\n   238→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14b921d9-eeaf-453d-9533-337d6f497996","uuid":"8999ea63-4d82-447f-a32a-4d6cc3907e48","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/.vista/features/docker-sandbox/specs/settings.md","content":"# Spec: Sandbox Settings\n\n## Problem Statement\n\nThe Docker sandbox feature introduces new configuration: credential toggles, access profiles, image selection, network policy, model defaults, and OpenCode serve management. This must integrate cleanly into the existing `vista/settings.json` structure without breaking existing settings or requiring migration.\n\n## Proposed Solution\n\nAdd a `sandbox` section under the existing `ralph` key in `vista/settings.json`. When `sandbox` is absent or `enabled` is `false`, all sandbox functionality is disabled and loops run as direct subprocesses (current behavior).\n\n### Full Settings Schema\n\n```json\n{\n  \"server\": {\n    \"auto_start\": true,\n    \"auto_open_browser\": true,\n    \"host\": \"127.0.0.1\",\n    \"port\": 3456\n  },\n  \"providers\": {\n    \"claude\": { \"enabled\": true, \"display_name\": \"Claude Code\" },\n    \"opencode\": { \"enabled\": true, \"display_name\": \"OpenCode\" }\n  },\n  \"ralph\": {\n    \"defaults\": {\n      \"provider\": \"claude\",\n      \"model\": \"sonnet\",\n      \"iterations\": 3\n    },\n    \"summarizer\": {\n      \"provider\": \"claude\",\n      \"model\": \"haiku\"\n    },\n    \"providers\": { \"...\" : \"...\" },\n    \"sandbox\": {\n      \"enabled\": false,\n      \"image\": \"vista-ralph:latest\",\n      \"network\": true,\n      \"opencode_serve\": {\n        \"port\": 4096,\n        \"auto_start\": true\n      },\n      \"credentials\": {\n        \"claude_auth\": true,\n        \"git_ssh\": true,\n        \"git_config\": true,\n        \"github_cli\": false,\n        \"custom\": []\n      },\n      \"profiles\": {\n        \"full-access\": {\n          \"mounts\": [\n            { \"path\": \".\", \"mode\": \"rw\" }\n          ]\n        },\n        \"feature-scoped\": {\n          \"mounts\": [\n            { \"path\": \".vista/features/${FEATURE}\", \"mode\": \"rw\" },\n            { \"path\": \".vista/ralph/${FEATURE}\", \"mode\": \"rw\" },\n            { \"path\": \"src\", \"mode\": \"rw\" },\n            { \"path\": \"tests\", \"mode\": \"rw\" },\n            { \"path\": \".git\", \"mode\": \"rw\" }\n          ]\n        },\n        \"research-only\": {\n          \"mounts\": [\n            { \"path\": \".\", \"mode\": \"ro\" }\n          ],\n          \"network\": false\n        }\n      },\n      \"model_defaults\": {\n        \"haiku\": \"feature-scoped\",\n        \"sonnet\": \"full-access\",\n        \"opus\": \"full-access\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Field Reference\n\n| Field | Type | Default | Description |\n|-------|------|---------|-------------|\n| `sandbox.enabled` | bool | `false` | Master toggle. `false` = loops run as direct subprocesses. |\n| `sandbox.image` | string | `\"vista-ralph:latest\"` | Docker image to use. Modified claudebox image. |\n| `sandbox.network` | bool | `true` | Global network policy. `true` = containers have network access. |\n| `sandbox.opencode_serve.port` | int | `4096` | Port for host-side `opencode serve` instance. |\n| `sandbox.opencode_serve.auto_start` | bool | `true` | Auto-start `opencode serve` when first OpenCode sandbox loop runs. |\n| `sandbox.credentials.claude_auth` | bool | `true` | Mount Claude Code auth (`~/.claude/` + `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`). Applied to Claude Code loops only. |\n| `sandbox.credentials.git_ssh` | bool | `true` | Mount SSH keys for Git. Applied to all loops. |\n| `sandbox.credentials.git_config` | bool | `true` | Mount `.gitconfig`. Applied to all loops. |\n| `sandbox.credentials.github_cli` | bool | `false` | Mount GitHub CLI auth. Applied to all loops. |\n| `sandbox.credentials.custom` | array | `[]` | User-defined mounts. |\n| `sandbox.credentials.custom[].name` | string | required | Display name for the custom credential. |\n| `sandbox.credentials.custom[].host_path` | string | required | Path on host. `~` expanded. |\n| `sandbox.credentials.custom[].container_path` | string | required | Path inside container. |\n| `sandbox.credentials.custom[].mode` | string | `\"ro\"` | `\"ro\"` or `\"rw\"`. |\n| `sandbox.profiles` | object | built-ins | Named access profiles. Keys are profile names. |\n| `sandbox.profiles.{name}.mounts` | array | required | List of mount specs. |\n| `sandbox.profiles.{name}.mounts[].path` | string | required | Path relative to project root. Supports `${FEATURE}`. |\n| `sandbox.profiles.{name}.mounts[].mode` | string | required | `\"rw\"` or `\"ro\"`. |\n| `sandbox.profiles.{name}.network` | bool\\|undefined | inherit | Override global network policy. Omit to inherit. |\n| `sandbox.model_defaults` | object | `{}` | Maps model names to profile names. |\n\n### UI Exposure (Current Phase)\n\nOnly `sandbox.enabled` is exposed in the Vista dashboard as a toggle control. All other sandbox settings are configurable by editing `settings.json` directly. This keeps the dashboard minimal while preserving full configurability for power users and automation.\n\n| Field | Exposure | Notes |\n|-------|----------|-------|\n| `sandbox.enabled` | Dashboard toggle | Only field surfaced in dashboard UI |\n| All other fields | `settings.json` only | Edit directly; validated on load |\n\n### Defaults Behavior\n\nWhen `sandbox` section is missing entirely:\n\n```python\nDEFAULT_SANDBOX = {\n    \"enabled\": False,\n    \"image\": \"vista-ralph:latest\",\n    \"network\": True,\n    \"opencode_serve\": {\n        \"port\": 4096,\n        \"auto_start\": True,\n    },\n    \"credentials\": {\n        \"claude_auth\": True,\n        \"git_ssh\": True,\n        \"git_config\": True,\n        \"github_cli\": False,\n        \"custom\": [],\n    },\n    \"profiles\": {\n        \"full-access\": {\"mounts\": [{\"path\": \".\", \"mode\": \"rw\"}]},\n        \"feature-scoped\": {\"mounts\": [\n            {\"path\": \".vista/features/${FEATURE}\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n            {\"path\": \".vista/ralph/${FEATURE}\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n            {\"path\": \"src\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n            {\"path\": \"tests\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n            {\"path\": \".git\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n        ]},\n        \"research-only\": {\"mounts\": [{\"path\": \".\", \"mode\": \"ro\"}], \"network\": False},\n    },\n    \"model_defaults\": {},\n}\n```\n\n### Settings Loading\n\nExtend existing `vista/server/config.py`:\n\n```python\ndef get_sandbox_settings() -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Load sandbox settings with defaults applied.\n\n    Returns fully-populated sandbox config dict.\n    Missing keys are filled from DEFAULT_SANDBOX.\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef is_sandbox_enabled() -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Quick check: is sandbox.enabled == true?\"\"\"\n\ndef get_sandbox_profile(name: str) -> AccessProfile | None:\n    \"\"\"Load a specific profile by name. Returns None if not found.\"\"\"\n\ndef get_sandbox_credentials() -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Load credential toggle states + custom mounts.\"\"\"\n\ndef get_opencode_serve_settings() -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Load opencode serve config (port, auto_start).\"\"\"\n```\n\n### Settings Write-Back\n\nThe dashboard writes only the `sandbox.enabled` toggle. All other sandbox settings are managed by editing `settings.json` directly. A general-purpose write-back function is available for internal API use:\n\n```python\ndef save_sandbox_settings(sandbox_config: dict) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Write sandbox settings back to settings.json.\n\n    1. Read full settings.json\n    2. Validate sandbox_config against schema\n    3. Set settings[\"ralph\"][\"sandbox\"] = sandbox_config\n    4. Write back with json.dumps(indent=2)\n\n    Preserves all other settings sections.\n    \"\"\"\n```\n\n### Validation\n\nOn load and on save, validate:\n\n- `enabled` is boolean\n- `image` is string\n- `network` is boolean\n- `opencode_serve.port` is integer 1024-65535\n- `opencode_serve.auto_start` is boolean\n- Each credential toggle is boolean\n- Custom mounts have all required fields (`name`, `host_path`, `container_path`)\n- Each profile has at least one mount\n- Mount paths are relative, no `..` traversal\n- Mount modes are `\"rw\"` or `\"ro\"`\n- Profile names are alphanumeric + hyphens\n- `model_defaults` values reference existing profile names\n\nInvalid config on load: log warning, apply defaults for invalid fields. Don't crash.\nInvalid config on save: reject with validation errors returned to dashboard.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- **No `ralph` section at all**: Sandbox defaults are applied. `enabled` is `false`. No change in behavior.\n- **`ralph` section exists but no `sandbox` key**: Same as above — defaults applied.\n- **User deletes a profile that's referenced by `model_defaults`**: Validation warning on load. Model falls back to `full-access` at runtime.\n- **User sets `image` to a non-existent image**: Container creation fails at runtime with clear error. Settings save succeeds (no Docker check at save time).\n- **Port conflict for `opencode_serve`**: If configured port is in use, `OpenCodeServeManager` logs error and tries next available port.\n- **Concurrent save from dashboard + MCP tool call**: Acceptable race. Next operation reads latest file.\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- `vista/server/config.py` (existing) - Extend with sandbox loading\n- `vista/settings.json` (existing) - Extended with `sandbox` section\n- Spec: [credential-management](credential-management.md) - Consumes credential toggles\n- Spec: [access-profiles](access-profiles.md) - Consumes profile definitions\n- Spec: [dashboard-ui](dashboard-ui.md) - Toggle for `sandbox.enabled` and inline status display\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n- Unit tests for defaults application (missing section, partial section, empty section)\n- Unit tests for validation (invalid modes, missing fields, path traversal rejection)\n- Unit tests for settings write-back (preserves other sections, atomic)\n- Unit tests for opencode_serve settings validation (port range)\n- Integration test: modify settings → restart → settings loaded correctly\n","numLines":238,"startLine":1,"totalLines":238}}}
