{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SczPVD4G56yi1W94CTFVfY","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have enough information. Let me create a comprehensive overview document:\n\n## Vista Codebase Architecture Overview\n\nBased on my exploration of the vista codebase, here's a comprehensive overview organized by component:\n\n---\n\n## **1. CORE ARCHITECTURE**\n\n### **Absolute Path**\nC:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista\n\n### **Tech Stack**\n- **Framework**: FastAPI web dashboard + FastMCP for Claude Code MCP integration\n- **Loop Execution**: PowerShell (Windows) / Bash (Linux/macOS) scripts\n- **Process Management**: subprocess with PID tracking and signal handling\n- **Data Storage**: JSON files (no database)\n- **Testing**: pytest with mocking\n- **Python Version**: 3.11+\n\n---\n\n## **2. PROJECT STRUCTURE**\n\n```\nvista/\n├── server/                          # FastAPI web server + services\n│   ├── app.py                      # Main FastAPI app (v1.3.6) with lifespan\n│   ├── config.py                   # Configuration management\n│   ├── data/\n│   │   ├── projects.json           # Registry of projects (JSON store)\n│   │   └── sessions/               # Chat session storage\n│   ├── models/                     # Data models\n│   │   ├── project.py              # Project dataclass\n│   │   ├── loop_state.py           # LoopInstance state tracking\n│   │   └── chat_session.py\n│   ├── services/                   # Business logic services\n│   │   ├── ralph_service.py        # Ralph job lifecycle (CRITICAL)\n│   │   ├── provider_service.py     # Provider abstraction (Claude/OpenCode)\n│   │   ├── output_parser.py        # Parse loop script output\n│   │   ├── loop_service.py         # Web loop execution (mirrors ralph.py)\n│   │   ├── project_service.py      # Project CRUD\n│   │   ├── progress_service.py     # Progress tracking\n│   │   ├── chat_service.py         # Chat management\n│   │   ├── summarizer_service.py   # Output summarization\n│   │   └── [other services]\n│   ├── routes/                     # API endpoints\n│   │   ├── ralph.py                # Ralph job API (start/stop/status)\n│   │   ├── ralph_settings.py       # Ralph settings management\n│   │   ├── loops.py                # Loop control endpoints\n│   │   ├── providers.py            # Provider discovery\n│   │   ├── projects.py             # Project management\n│   │   └── [other routes]\n│   └── views/                      # HTML/static assets\n│       ├── dashboard.html\n│       ├── project.html\n│       ├── ralph_jobs.html\n│       └── static/\n├── portable/                        # Standalone loop runner\n│   ├── ralph.py                    # CLI tool for running loops\n│   ├── ralph.ps1 / ralph.sh        # Shell wrappers\n│   └── templates/\n│       ├── PROMPT_plan_adhoc.md    # Plan mode prompt template\n│       ├── PROMPT_build_adhoc.md   # Build mode prompt template\n│       ├── AGENTS.md               # Agent role definitions\n│       └── progress_template.txt   # Progress tracking template\n├── mcp_server.py                   # MCP entry point for Claude Code\n├── tests/                          # pytest test suite\n├── skills/                         # Custom MCP skills\n├── .claude-plugin/                 # Plugin metadata\n└── settings.json                   # Global settings (providers, ralph config)\n```\n\n---\n\n## **3. CORE SERVICES**\n\n### **3.1 RalphService** (C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/vista/server/services/ralph_service.py)\n\n**Purpose**: Manage ralph loop job lifecycle (create, execute, monitor, stop)\n\n**Key Classes/Methods**:\n- `RalphService` (singleton: `ralph_service`)\n  - `create_job()` - Create a new ralph job, write task/prompt files, launch subprocess\n  - `get_job_status()` - Get current job status, parse output.log for activity, detect completion\n  - `stop_job()` - Terminate running job with SIGTERM/SIGKILL\n  - `list_jobs()` - List all jobs in project\n  - `_job_dir()` - Resolve job directory path\n  - `_read_activity()` - Parse output.log (dispatches to Claude/OpenCode parsers)\n  - `_completed_successfully()` - Check for normal completion markers\n  - `_is_process_running()` - PID-based process check (Windows/Unix)\n\n**Job Directory Structure**:\n```\n.vista/ralph/{slug}-{job_id[:8]}/\n├── job.json                        # Job metadata (status, provider, model, etc.)\n├── task.md                         # Task description (read by agent)\n├── PROMPT_plan.md / PROMPT_build.md\n├── loop.ps1 / loop.sh              # Generated shell script\n├── output.log                      # Raw subprocess stdout (for dashboard)\n└── progress.txt                    # Inter-loop agent context (not displayed)\n```\n\n**Key Design**:\n- Jobs are persisted on disk (not in-memory)\n- `output.log` is the ONLY source for dashboard activity (not `progress.txt`)\n- Parser dispatches based on provider (Claude = stream-json, OpenCode = plaintext)\n- PID validation to prevent stopping wrong processes\n- Clears runtime artifacts (output.log, progress.txt, loop script) on job creation\n\n---\n\n### **3.2 ProviderService** (C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/vista/server/services/provider_service.py)\n\n**Purpose**: Abstract CLI providers (Claude Code, OpenCode) with model discovery and invocation commands\n\n**Key Classes**:\n- `Provider` (base class)\n  - `get_models()` - Discover available models\n  - `get_invocation()` - Return shell code snippet to invoke provider\n  - `get_chat_cmd()` - Return CLI command for chat\n  - `get_summarizer_command()` - Return command for summarization\n  - `parse_stream_event()` - Parse streaming output\n\n- `ClaudeProvider(Provider)`\n  - Models: `[\"opus\", \"sonnet\", \"haiku\"]` (hardcoded)\n  - Invocation: `claude -p --dangerously-skip-permissions --output-format=stream-json --model $MODEL`\n  - Supports streaming with stream-json output format\n\n- `OpenCodeProvider(Provider)`\n  - Models: Discovered via `opencode models` CLI (dynamic)\n  - Invocation: `opencode run --model $MODEL`\n\n**Key Functions**:\n- `get_enabled_providers()` - Load from settings.json, return Provider instances\n- `get_provider_by_name()` - Lookup provider by name\n- `get_ralph_providers()` - Return providers with model filtering/metadata for ralph MCP tools\n- `_find_command()` - Search PATH and common install locations\n\n**Settings Structure** (from settings.json):\n```json\n\"providers\": {\n  \"claude\": { \"enabled\": true, \"display_name\": \"Claude Code\" },\n  \"opencode\": { \"enabled\": true, \"display_name\": \"OpenCode\" }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### **3.3 OutputParser** (C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/vista/server/services/output_parser.py)\n\n**Purpose**: Parse loop script output into human-readable activity for dashboard\n\n**Key Functions**:\n- `parse_stream_json_activity()` - Parse Claude's stream-json output\n  - Extracts assistant text, tool calls, iteration markers\n  - Returns `(activity_lines, current_iteration)`\n  \n- `parse_plaintext_activity()` - Parse OpenCode plaintext output\n  - Handles ANSI codes, arrow-prefixed tool calls\n  - Skips boilerplate/PowerShell noise\n  - Returns `(activity_lines, current_iteration)`\n\n**Output Patterns Recognized**:\n- Iteration markers: `=== ITERATION 3 ===`\n- Completion: `Loop finished after 3 iteration(s)`, `All phases complete`, `Reached max iterations`\n- Tool calls: `> Tool: Read  file.txt`, `> Tool: Bash  command`\n- Model output: Assistant text blocks\n\n---\n\n### **3.4 ProjectService** (C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/vista/server/services/project_service.py)\n\n**Purpose**: CRUD for project registry\n\n**Key Methods**:\n- `get_all()` - Load all projects from projects.json\n- `register()` - Add new project with path validation\n- `unregister()` - Remove project by ID\n- `scan_features()` - List features in `.vista/features/`\n- `scan_features_detailed()` - Rich metadata (which files exist, spec count, etc.)\n\n**Project Model** (models/project.py):\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass Project:\n    id: str              # UUID[:8]\n    name: str            # Directory name\n    path: str            # Absolute path\n    created_at: str      # ISO datetime\n    last_accessed: str\n```\n\n---\n\n### **3.5 LoopService** (C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/vista/server/services/loop_service.py)\n\n**Purpose**: Execute loops via web (mirrors portable/ralph.py for web context)\n\n**Key Methods**:\n- `start_loop()` - Create feature dir, generate loop script, launch subprocess\n- `stop_loop()` - Terminate running loop\n- `get_state()` - Get current loop state\n- `get_all_states()` - State for all projects\n\n**Uses identical LOOP_PS1_TEMPLATE and LOOP_SH_TEMPLATE as ralph.py** for consistent behavior\n\n---\n\n## **4. MCP INTEGRATION**\n\n### **Main Entry Point**\n**File**: C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/vista/mcp_server.py\n\n**Key Functions**:\n- `ralph_start()` - Start a ralph job (MCP tool)\n- `ralph_stop()` - Stop a running job (MCP tool)\n- `ralph_status()` - Get job status (MCP tool)\n- `ralph_summary()` - Generate AI summary of job progress (MCP tool)\n- `spawn_teammate()` - Spawn new team member (Claude Teams integration)\n- Dashboard runs as daemon thread on HTTP (no stdio involvement)\n\n**FastMCP Integration**:\n- Uses fastmcp 3.x for proper Context/ToolError handling\n- Supports Claude Code + OpenCode backends\n- Interactive tmux support for teammate spawning\n\n---\n\n## **5. ROUTES & API ENDPOINTS**\n\n### **5.1 Ralph Routes** (routes/ralph.py)\n- `GET /api/ralph/jobs` - List all jobs\n- `GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}` - Get job status\n- `GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/progress` - Get parsed activity (last 50 lines)\n- `GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/output` - Get raw output.log tail\n- `GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/artifacts` - List artifact files\n- `GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/artifacts/{filename}` - Download artifact\n- `POST /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/stop` - Stop a job\n\n### **5.2 Other Routes**\n- `routes/providers.py` - Provider discovery, model listing\n- `routes/projects.py` - Project registration/management\n- `routes/loops.py` - Web loop execution\n- `routes/chat.py`, `routes/chat_sessions.py` - Chat functionality\n- `routes/plans.py` - Plan generation\n- `routes/ralph_settings.py` - Ralph settings API\n\n---\n\n## **6. CONFIGURATION**\n\n### **Configuration Layers** (config.py)\n1. **Defaults** (hardcoded)\n2. **settings.json** (persistent)\n3. **Environment variables** (override, e.g., `VISTA_SETTINGS_FILE`, `RALPH_SERVER_PORT`)\n\n### **Server Defaults**:\n```python\n{\n    \"auto_start\": True,\n    \"auto_open_browser\": True,\n    \"host\": \"127.0.0.1\",\n    \"port\": 3456,\n}\n```\n\n### **Ralph Defaults**:\n```python\n{\n    \"defaults\": {\n        \"provider\": \"claude\",\n        \"model\": \"sonnet\",\n        \"iterations\": 3,\n    },\n    \"summarizer\": {\n        \"provider\": \"claude\",\n        \"model\": \"haiku\",\n    },\n    \"providers\": {...}\n}\n```\n\n### **Settings File Locations**:\n- Default: `~/.vista/settings.json` (persistent, user home)\n- Legacy: `vista/settings.json` (plugin root, migrated to default)\n- Override: `VISTA_SETTINGS_FILE` environment variable\n\n---\n\n## **7. PORTABLE LOOP RUNNER**\n\n### **File**: vista/portable/ralph.py\n\n**Purpose**: Standalone CLI for running loops (used when ralph.py is invoked directly, not via web)\n\n**Key Functions**:\n- Prompts user for feature, mode, iterations, model\n- Uses same **LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE** as server\n- Copies prompt template to feature directory\n- Launches loop script\n- Cleans up generated files\n\n**LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE** (shared with server):\n- PowerShell (Windows) and Bash (Linux/macOS)\n- Bakes in absolute paths (no relative resolution)\n- Composes prompt: base PROMPT_{mode}.md + task.md + progress.txt\n- Invokes provider CLI (claude or opencode)\n- Pushes changes after each iteration\n- Detects completion (`ALL PHASES COMPLETE` for build mode)\n\n---\n\n## **8. PROMPT TEMPLATES**\n\n### **File Locations**: vista/portable/templates/\n\n**For Adhoc Ralph Jobs** (created dynamically):\n- `PROMPT_plan_adhoc.md` - Plan mode template for ralph_start\n- `PROMPT_build_adhoc.md` - Build mode template for ralph_start\n\n**Variable Substitution**:\n- `{{FEATURE_NAME}}` → slug (job name)\n- `{{FEATURE_DIR}}` → job directory path\n- `{{PROJECT_NAME}}` → project root directory name\n\n**Template Content Example**:\n```markdown\n**CRITICAL: This is a PLAN iteration. You MUST write a detailed plan.**\n\nPROJECT: {{PROJECT_NAME}}\nJOB: {{FEATURE_NAME}}\nJOB_DIR: {{FEATURE_DIR}}\n\n## Step 1-2: Understand task, inspect codebase\n## Step 3: Plan the work\n## Output: Write to {{FEATURE_DIR}}/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md\n```\n\n---\n\n## **9. DATA MODELS**\n\n### **Project** (models/project.py)\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass Project:\n    id: str = UUID[:8]\n    name: str\n    path: str  # Absolute\n    created_at: str  # ISO\n    last_accessed: str\n```\n\n### **LoopInstance** (models/loop_state.py)\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass LoopInstance:\n    project_id: str\n    feature_name: str\n    mode: str  # \"plan\" or \"build\"\n    model: str\n    provider: str  # \"claude\" or \"opencode\"\n    provider_display_name: str\n    status: str  # \"idle\", \"starting\", \"running\", \"stopped\", \"completed\", \"failed\"\n    pid: Optional[int]\n    iteration: int\n    max_iterations: int\n    start_time: Optional[str]  # ISO\n    end_time: Optional[str]\n    error: Optional[str]\n    output_lines: deque[str]  # Last 2000 lines\n    last_ralph_control: Optional[dict]  # {\"status\": \"done\", ...}\n    progress_summary: Optional[str]\n    recent_actions: deque[dict]  # Last 20 actions\n```\n\n### **Job Metadata** (job.json in .vista/ralph/{slug}-{id}/)\n```json\n{\n    \"job_id\": \"uuid\",\n    \"slug\": \"feature-name\",\n    \"mode\": \"plan\" or \"build\",\n    \"status\": \"running\" | \"completed\" | \"failed\" | \"stopped\",\n    \"provider\": \"claude\" or \"opencode\",\n    \"model\": \"sonnet\",\n    \"iterations\": 3,\n    \"current_iteration\": 0,\n    \"pid\": 12345,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-12T...\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-12T...\",\n    \"completed_at\": null,\n    \"error\": null\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## **10. TESTING**\n\n### **Test Files**: vista/tests/\n\n- `test_ralph_service.py` - Job creation, status detection, completion markers\n- `test_output_parser.py` - Parse stream-json and plaintext\n- `test_api.py` - FastAPI endpoint tests\n- `test_project_service.py` - Project CRUD\n- `test_config.py` - Configuration loading/merging\n- `integration/test_ralph_lifecycle.py` - End-to-end job lifecycle\n- `integration/test_mcp_tools.py` - MCP tool functionality\n\n**Test Pattern**: Use pytest with mocking (subprocess.Popen, config paths)\n\n**Run Tests**:\n```bash\npython -m pytest vista/tests -q  # From vista/ directory\n```\n\n---\n\n## **11. DOCKERFILE SANDBOX FEATURE**\n\n### **Reference Architecture**: .vista/features/docker-sandbox/\n\n**Specification Files**:\n- `domain-requirements.md` - Feature requirements\n- `specs/` - Detailed specifications:\n  - `access-profiles.md` - Permission scoping\n  - `container-lifecycle.md` - Container management\n  - `credential-management.md` - Secret handling\n  - `dashboard-ui.md` - UI components\n  - `settings.md` - Configuration schema\n- `arch/` - Architecture diagrams (Mermaid, DrawIO)\n- `reference/claudebox/` - Reference implementation\n\n**Key Concepts**:\n- Container lifecycle management for isolated execution\n- Credential & secret management\n- Access profiles for permission control\n- Dashboard UI for sandbox management\n- Settings integration with vista config system\n\n---\n\n## **12. KEY PATTERNS & CONVENTIONS**\n\n### **File Naming**:\n- Loop scripts: `loop.ps1` (Windows) / `loop.sh` (Bash)\n- Prompts: `PROMPT_{mode}.md` or `PROMPT_{mode}_adhoc.md`\n- Progress: `progress.txt` (inter-loop context only)\n- Output: `output.log` (displayed on dashboard)\n- Job metadata: `job.json`\n\n### **Paths**:\n- **Absolute paths used throughout** (no relative resolution needed)\n- Feature dir: `.vista/features/{feature_name}/`\n- Ralph jobs: `.vista/ralph/{slug}-{job_id[:8]}/`\n- Projects registry: `server/data/projects.json`\n\n### **Provider Invocation**:\nPowerShell:\n```powershell\n$PromptContent | claude -p --dangerously-skip-permissions --output-format=stream-json --model $Model\n```\n\nBash:\n```bash\nprintf \"%s\" \"$PROMPT_CONTENT\" | claude -p --dangerously-skip-permissions --output-format=stream-json --model \"$MODEL\"\n```\n\n### **Process Management**:\n- Windows: CREATE_NO_WINDOW | CREATE_NEW_PROCESS_GROUP (no console window)\n- Unix: signal(SIGTERM) then signal(SIGKILL) if needed\n- PID validation before stopping to prevent accidents\n\n### **Completion Detection**:\n- Loop markers: \"Loop finished after X iteration(s)\", \"Reached max iterations\", \"All phases complete\"\n- Model activity: Check for actual model output in output.log\n- Iteration number: Extracted from output.log OR progress.txt (whichever is higher)\n\n---\n\n## **13. EXTERNAL DEPENDENCIES**\n\n**Key Imports**:\n- `fastapi` - Web framework\n- `fastmcp` - MCP server\n- `uvicorn` - ASGI server (runs as daemon thread)\n- `claude_teams` - Team spawning, messaging\n- Standard: `subprocess`, `json`, `pathlib`, `dataclasses`, `asyncio`\n\n---\n\n## **14. CRITICAL FILES FOR DOCKER SANDBOX FEATURE**\n\nBased on the docker-sandbox feature specs, you'll likely need to modify/add:\n\n1. **Core Services** (new sandbox service):\n   - `vista/server/services/sandbox_service.py` - Container lifecycle\n   - `vista/server/services/credential_service.py` - Secret management\n   - `vista/server/services/access_profile_service.py` - Permission control\n\n2. **Routes** (new sandbox routes):\n   - `vista/server/routes/sandbox.py` - Container management endpoints\n   - `vista/server/routes/credentials.py` - Secret management endpoints\n\n3. **Models** (new data models):\n   - `vista/server/models/sandbox.py` - Container state\n   - `vista/server/models/credential.py` - Credential metadata\n\n4. **Configuration**:\n   - Extend `vista/server/config.py` with sandbox defaults\n   - Update `vista/settings.json` with sandbox settings schema\n\n5. **Integration Points**:\n   - Modify `RalphService.create_job()` to support sandbox execution\n   - Extend `LoopService` for sandboxed loops\n   - Update provider invocation to support containerized execution\n\n6. **Database/Persistence**:\n   - Consider adding SQLite/JSON store for credential encryption\n   - Extend job.json schema with sandbox metadata\n\n---\n\nThis comprehensive overview should give you a solid understanding of the vista architecture for planning the Docker sandbox feature. All file paths are absolute from the vista project root."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a7d3eba (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 81462\ntool_uses: 25\nduration_ms: 93039</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14b921d9-eeaf-453d-9533-337d6f497996","uuid":"b86322ce-0f7b-446c-b058-0b8fcd6175f5","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need a comprehensive overview of the vista codebase structure. Please explore:\n\n1. `vista/server/` - all services, routes, config files, app.py\n2. `vista/server/services/` - all service files, especially ralph_service.py, provider_service.py, output_parser.py\n3. `vista/server/routes/` - all route files\n4. `vista/portable/` - loop script templates, prompt templates\n5. `vista/server/config.py` or similar settings/config files\n6. `vista/settings.json` - current settings structure\n7. `vista/tests/` - existing test files\n\nFor each file found, give me the file path and a brief description of what it contains (key classes, functions, important patterns). I need to understand the current architecture to plan new Docker sandbox features.\n\nThe project root is: C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista","agentId":"a7d3eba","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have enough information. Let me create a comprehensive overview document:\n\n## Vista Codebase Architecture Overview\n\nBased on my exploration of the vista codebase, here's a comprehensive overview organized by component:\n\n---\n\n## **1. CORE ARCHITECTURE**\n\n### **Absolute Path**\nC:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista\n\n### **Tech Stack**\n- **Framework**: FastAPI web dashboard + FastMCP for Claude Code MCP integration\n- **Loop Execution**: PowerShell (Windows) / Bash (Linux/macOS) scripts\n- **Process Management**: subprocess with PID tracking and signal handling\n- **Data Storage**: JSON files (no database)\n- **Testing**: pytest with mocking\n- **Python Version**: 3.11+\n\n---\n\n## **2. PROJECT STRUCTURE**\n\n```\nvista/\n├── server/                          # FastAPI web server + services\n│   ├── app.py                      # Main FastAPI app (v1.3.6) with lifespan\n│   ├── config.py                   # Configuration management\n│   ├── data/\n│   │   ├── projects.json           # Registry of projects (JSON store)\n│   │   └── sessions/               # Chat session storage\n│   ├── models/                     # Data models\n│   │   ├── project.py              # Project dataclass\n│   │   ├── loop_state.py           # LoopInstance state tracking\n│   │   └── chat_session.py\n│   ├── services/                   # Business logic services\n│   │   ├── ralph_service.py        # Ralph job lifecycle (CRITICAL)\n│   │   ├── provider_service.py     # Provider abstraction (Claude/OpenCode)\n│   │   ├── output_parser.py        # Parse loop script output\n│   │   ├── loop_service.py         # Web loop execution (mirrors ralph.py)\n│   │   ├── project_service.py      # Project CRUD\n│   │   ├── progress_service.py     # Progress tracking\n│   │   ├── chat_service.py         # Chat management\n│   │   ├── summarizer_service.py   # Output summarization\n│   │   └── [other services]\n│   ├── routes/                     # API endpoints\n│   │   ├── ralph.py                # Ralph job API (start/stop/status)\n│   │   ├── ralph_settings.py       # Ralph settings management\n│   │   ├── loops.py                # Loop control endpoints\n│   │   ├── providers.py            # Provider discovery\n│   │   ├── projects.py             # Project management\n│   │   └── [other routes]\n│   └── views/                      # HTML/static assets\n│       ├── dashboard.html\n│       ├── project.html\n│       ├── ralph_jobs.html\n│       └── static/\n├── portable/                        # Standalone loop runner\n│   ├── ralph.py                    # CLI tool for running loops\n│   ├── ralph.ps1 / ralph.sh        # Shell wrappers\n│   └── templates/\n│       ├── PROMPT_plan_adhoc.md    # Plan mode prompt template\n│       ├── PROMPT_build_adhoc.md   # Build mode prompt template\n│       ├── AGENTS.md               # Agent role definitions\n│       └── progress_template.txt   # Progress tracking template\n├── mcp_server.py                   # MCP entry point for Claude Code\n├── tests/                          # pytest test suite\n├── skills/                         # Custom MCP skills\n├── .claude-plugin/                 # Plugin metadata\n└── settings.json                   # Global settings (providers, ralph config)\n```\n\n---\n\n## **3. CORE SERVICES**\n\n### **3.1 RalphService** (C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/vista/server/services/ralph_service.py)\n\n**Purpose**: Manage ralph loop job lifecycle (create, execute, monitor, stop)\n\n**Key Classes/Methods**:\n- `RalphService` (singleton: `ralph_service`)\n  - `create_job()` - Create a new ralph job, write task/prompt files, launch subprocess\n  - `get_job_status()` - Get current job status, parse output.log for activity, detect completion\n  - `stop_job()` - Terminate running job with SIGTERM/SIGKILL\n  - `list_jobs()` - List all jobs in project\n  - `_job_dir()` - Resolve job directory path\n  - `_read_activity()` - Parse output.log (dispatches to Claude/OpenCode parsers)\n  - `_completed_successfully()` - Check for normal completion markers\n  - `_is_process_running()` - PID-based process check (Windows/Unix)\n\n**Job Directory Structure**:\n```\n.vista/ralph/{slug}-{job_id[:8]}/\n├── job.json                        # Job metadata (status, provider, model, etc.)\n├── task.md                         # Task description (read by agent)\n├── PROMPT_plan.md / PROMPT_build.md\n├── loop.ps1 / loop.sh              # Generated shell script\n├── output.log                      # Raw subprocess stdout (for dashboard)\n└── progress.txt                    # Inter-loop agent context (not displayed)\n```\n\n**Key Design**:\n- Jobs are persisted on disk (not in-memory)\n- `output.log` is the ONLY source for dashboard activity (not `progress.txt`)\n- Parser dispatches based on provider (Claude = stream-json, OpenCode = plaintext)\n- PID validation to prevent stopping wrong processes\n- Clears runtime artifacts (output.log, progress.txt, loop script) on job creation\n\n---\n\n### **3.2 ProviderService** (C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/vista/server/services/provider_service.py)\n\n**Purpose**: Abstract CLI providers (Claude Code, OpenCode) with model discovery and invocation commands\n\n**Key Classes**:\n- `Provider` (base class)\n  - `get_models()` - Discover available models\n  - `get_invocation()` - Return shell code snippet to invoke provider\n  - `get_chat_cmd()` - Return CLI command for chat\n  - `get_summarizer_command()` - Return command for summarization\n  - `parse_stream_event()` - Parse streaming output\n\n- `ClaudeProvider(Provider)`\n  - Models: `[\"opus\", \"sonnet\", \"haiku\"]` (hardcoded)\n  - Invocation: `claude -p --dangerously-skip-permissions --output-format=stream-json --model $MODEL`\n  - Supports streaming with stream-json output format\n\n- `OpenCodeProvider(Provider)`\n  - Models: Discovered via `opencode models` CLI (dynamic)\n  - Invocation: `opencode run --model $MODEL`\n\n**Key Functions**:\n- `get_enabled_providers()` - Load from settings.json, return Provider instances\n- `get_provider_by_name()` - Lookup provider by name\n- `get_ralph_providers()` - Return providers with model filtering/metadata for ralph MCP tools\n- `_find_command()` - Search PATH and common install locations\n\n**Settings Structure** (from settings.json):\n```json\n\"providers\": {\n  \"claude\": { \"enabled\": true, \"display_name\": \"Claude Code\" },\n  \"opencode\": { \"enabled\": true, \"display_name\": \"OpenCode\" }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### **3.3 OutputParser** (C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/vista/server/services/output_parser.py)\n\n**Purpose**: Parse loop script output into human-readable activity for dashboard\n\n**Key Functions**:\n- `parse_stream_json_activity()` - Parse Claude's stream-json output\n  - Extracts assistant text, tool calls, iteration markers\n  - Returns `(activity_lines, current_iteration)`\n  \n- `parse_plaintext_activity()` - Parse OpenCode plaintext output\n  - Handles ANSI codes, arrow-prefixed tool calls\n  - Skips boilerplate/PowerShell noise\n  - Returns `(activity_lines, current_iteration)`\n\n**Output Patterns Recognized**:\n- Iteration markers: `=== ITERATION 3 ===`\n- Completion: `Loop finished after 3 iteration(s)`, `All phases complete`, `Reached max iterations`\n- Tool calls: `> Tool: Read  file.txt`, `> Tool: Bash  command`\n- Model output: Assistant text blocks\n\n---\n\n### **3.4 ProjectService** (C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/vista/server/services/project_service.py)\n\n**Purpose**: CRUD for project registry\n\n**Key Methods**:\n- `get_all()` - Load all projects from projects.json\n- `register()` - Add new project with path validation\n- `unregister()` - Remove project by ID\n- `scan_features()` - List features in `.vista/features/`\n- `scan_features_detailed()` - Rich metadata (which files exist, spec count, etc.)\n\n**Project Model** (models/project.py):\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass Project:\n    id: str              # UUID[:8]\n    name: str            # Directory name\n    path: str            # Absolute path\n    created_at: str      # ISO datetime\n    last_accessed: str\n```\n\n---\n\n### **3.5 LoopService** (C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/vista/server/services/loop_service.py)\n\n**Purpose**: Execute loops via web (mirrors portable/ralph.py for web context)\n\n**Key Methods**:\n- `start_loop()` - Create feature dir, generate loop script, launch subprocess\n- `stop_loop()` - Terminate running loop\n- `get_state()` - Get current loop state\n- `get_all_states()` - State for all projects\n\n**Uses identical LOOP_PS1_TEMPLATE and LOOP_SH_TEMPLATE as ralph.py** for consistent behavior\n\n---\n\n## **4. MCP INTEGRATION**\n\n### **Main Entry Point**\n**File**: C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/vista/mcp_server.py\n\n**Key Functions**:\n- `ralph_start()` - Start a ralph job (MCP tool)\n- `ralph_stop()` - Stop a running job (MCP tool)\n- `ralph_status()` - Get job status (MCP tool)\n- `ralph_summary()` - Generate AI summary of job progress (MCP tool)\n- `spawn_teammate()` - Spawn new team member (Claude Teams integration)\n- Dashboard runs as daemon thread on HTTP (no stdio involvement)\n\n**FastMCP Integration**:\n- Uses fastmcp 3.x for proper Context/ToolError handling\n- Supports Claude Code + OpenCode backends\n- Interactive tmux support for teammate spawning\n\n---\n\n## **5. ROUTES & API ENDPOINTS**\n\n### **5.1 Ralph Routes** (routes/ralph.py)\n- `GET /api/ralph/jobs` - List all jobs\n- `GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}` - Get job status\n- `GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/progress` - Get parsed activity (last 50 lines)\n- `GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/output` - Get raw output.log tail\n- `GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/artifacts` - List artifact files\n- `GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/artifacts/{filename}` - Download artifact\n- `POST /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/stop` - Stop a job\n\n### **5.2 Other Routes**\n- `routes/providers.py` - Provider discovery, model listing\n- `routes/projects.py` - Project registration/management\n- `routes/loops.py` - Web loop execution\n- `routes/chat.py`, `routes/chat_sessions.py` - Chat functionality\n- `routes/plans.py` - Plan generation\n- `routes/ralph_settings.py` - Ralph settings API\n\n---\n\n## **6. CONFIGURATION**\n\n### **Configuration Layers** (config.py)\n1. **Defaults** (hardcoded)\n2. **settings.json** (persistent)\n3. **Environment variables** (override, e.g., `VISTA_SETTINGS_FILE`, `RALPH_SERVER_PORT`)\n\n### **Server Defaults**:\n```python\n{\n    \"auto_start\": True,\n    \"auto_open_browser\": True,\n    \"host\": \"127.0.0.1\",\n    \"port\": 3456,\n}\n```\n\n### **Ralph Defaults**:\n```python\n{\n    \"defaults\": {\n        \"provider\": \"claude\",\n        \"model\": \"sonnet\",\n        \"iterations\": 3,\n    },\n    \"summarizer\": {\n        \"provider\": \"claude\",\n        \"model\": \"haiku\",\n    },\n    \"providers\": {...}\n}\n```\n\n### **Settings File Locations**:\n- Default: `~/.vista/settings.json` (persistent, user home)\n- Legacy: `vista/settings.json` (plugin root, migrated to default)\n- Override: `VISTA_SETTINGS_FILE` environment variable\n\n---\n\n## **7. PORTABLE LOOP RUNNER**\n\n### **File**: vista/portable/ralph.py\n\n**Purpose**: Standalone CLI for running loops (used when ralph.py is invoked directly, not via web)\n\n**Key Functions**:\n- Prompts user for feature, mode, iterations, model\n- Uses same **LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE** as server\n- Copies prompt template to feature directory\n- Launches loop script\n- Cleans up generated files\n\n**LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE** (shared with server):\n- PowerShell (Windows) and Bash (Linux/macOS)\n- Bakes in absolute paths (no relative resolution)\n- Composes prompt: base PROMPT_{mode}.md + task.md + progress.txt\n- Invokes provider CLI (claude or opencode)\n- Pushes changes after each iteration\n- Detects completion (`ALL PHASES COMPLETE` for build mode)\n\n---\n\n## **8. PROMPT TEMPLATES**\n\n### **File Locations**: vista/portable/templates/\n\n**For Adhoc Ralph Jobs** (created dynamically):\n- `PROMPT_plan_adhoc.md` - Plan mode template for ralph_start\n- `PROMPT_build_adhoc.md` - Build mode template for ralph_start\n\n**Variable Substitution**:\n- `{{FEATURE_NAME}}` → slug (job name)\n- `{{FEATURE_DIR}}` → job directory path\n- `{{PROJECT_NAME}}` → project root directory name\n\n**Template Content Example**:\n```markdown\n**CRITICAL: This is a PLAN iteration. You MUST write a detailed plan.**\n\nPROJECT: {{PROJECT_NAME}}\nJOB: {{FEATURE_NAME}}\nJOB_DIR: {{FEATURE_DIR}}\n\n## Step 1-2: Understand task, inspect codebase\n## Step 3: Plan the work\n## Output: Write to {{FEATURE_DIR}}/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md\n```\n\n---\n\n## **9. DATA MODELS**\n\n### **Project** (models/project.py)\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass Project:\n    id: str = UUID[:8]\n    name: str\n    path: str  # Absolute\n    created_at: str  # ISO\n    last_accessed: str\n```\n\n### **LoopInstance** (models/loop_state.py)\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass LoopInstance:\n    project_id: str\n    feature_name: str\n    mode: str  # \"plan\" or \"build\"\n    model: str\n    provider: str  # \"claude\" or \"opencode\"\n    provider_display_name: str\n    status: str  # \"idle\", \"starting\", \"running\", \"stopped\", \"completed\", \"failed\"\n    pid: Optional[int]\n    iteration: int\n    max_iterations: int\n    start_time: Optional[str]  # ISO\n    end_time: Optional[str]\n    error: Optional[str]\n    output_lines: deque[str]  # Last 2000 lines\n    last_ralph_control: Optional[dict]  # {\"status\": \"done\", ...}\n    progress_summary: Optional[str]\n    recent_actions: deque[dict]  # Last 20 actions\n```\n\n### **Job Metadata** (job.json in .vista/ralph/{slug}-{id}/)\n```json\n{\n    \"job_id\": \"uuid\",\n    \"slug\": \"feature-name\",\n    \"mode\": \"plan\" or \"build\",\n    \"status\": \"running\" | \"completed\" | \"failed\" | \"stopped\",\n    \"provider\": \"claude\" or \"opencode\",\n    \"model\": \"sonnet\",\n    \"iterations\": 3,\n    \"current_iteration\": 0,\n    \"pid\": 12345,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-12T...\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-12T...\",\n    \"completed_at\": null,\n    \"error\": null\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## **10. TESTING**\n\n### **Test Files**: vista/tests/\n\n- `test_ralph_service.py` - Job creation, status detection, completion markers\n- `test_output_parser.py` - Parse stream-json and plaintext\n- `test_api.py` - FastAPI endpoint tests\n- `test_project_service.py` - Project CRUD\n- `test_config.py` - Configuration loading/merging\n- `integration/test_ralph_lifecycle.py` - End-to-end job lifecycle\n- `integration/test_mcp_tools.py` - MCP tool functionality\n\n**Test Pattern**: Use pytest with mocking (subprocess.Popen, config paths)\n\n**Run Tests**:\n```bash\npython -m pytest vista/tests -q  # From vista/ directory\n```\n\n---\n\n## **11. DOCKERFILE SANDBOX FEATURE**\n\n### **Reference Architecture**: .vista/features/docker-sandbox/\n\n**Specification Files**:\n- `domain-requirements.md` - Feature requirements\n- `specs/` - Detailed specifications:\n  - `access-profiles.md` - Permission scoping\n  - `container-lifecycle.md` - Container management\n  - `credential-management.md` - Secret handling\n  - `dashboard-ui.md` - UI components\n  - `settings.md` - Configuration schema\n- `arch/` - Architecture diagrams (Mermaid, DrawIO)\n- `reference/claudebox/` - Reference implementation\n\n**Key Concepts**:\n- Container lifecycle management for isolated execution\n- Credential & secret management\n- Access profiles for permission control\n- Dashboard UI for sandbox management\n- Settings integration with vista config system\n\n---\n\n## **12. KEY PATTERNS & CONVENTIONS**\n\n### **File Naming**:\n- Loop scripts: `loop.ps1` (Windows) / `loop.sh` (Bash)\n- Prompts: `PROMPT_{mode}.md` or `PROMPT_{mode}_adhoc.md`\n- Progress: `progress.txt` (inter-loop context only)\n- Output: `output.log` (displayed on dashboard)\n- Job metadata: `job.json`\n\n### **Paths**:\n- **Absolute paths used throughout** (no relative resolution needed)\n- Feature dir: `.vista/features/{feature_name}/`\n- Ralph jobs: `.vista/ralph/{slug}-{job_id[:8]}/`\n- Projects registry: `server/data/projects.json`\n\n### **Provider Invocation**:\nPowerShell:\n```powershell\n$PromptContent | claude -p --dangerously-skip-permissions --output-format=stream-json --model $Model\n```\n\nBash:\n```bash\nprintf \"%s\" \"$PROMPT_CONTENT\" | claude -p --dangerously-skip-permissions --output-format=stream-json --model \"$MODEL\"\n```\n\n### **Process Management**:\n- Windows: CREATE_NO_WINDOW | CREATE_NEW_PROCESS_GROUP (no console window)\n- Unix: signal(SIGTERM) then signal(SIGKILL) if needed\n- PID validation before stopping to prevent accidents\n\n### **Completion Detection**:\n- Loop markers: \"Loop finished after X iteration(s)\", \"Reached max iterations\", \"All phases complete\"\n- Model activity: Check for actual model output in output.log\n- Iteration number: Extracted from output.log OR progress.txt (whichever is higher)\n\n---\n\n## **13. EXTERNAL DEPENDENCIES**\n\n**Key Imports**:\n- `fastapi` - Web framework\n- `fastmcp` - MCP server\n- `uvicorn` - ASGI server (runs as daemon thread)\n- `claude_teams` - Team spawning, messaging\n- Standard: `subprocess`, `json`, `pathlib`, `dataclasses`, `asyncio`\n\n---\n\n## **14. CRITICAL FILES FOR DOCKER SANDBOX FEATURE**\n\nBased on the docker-sandbox feature specs, you'll likely need to modify/add:\n\n1. **Core Services** (new sandbox service):\n   - `vista/server/services/sandbox_service.py` - Container lifecycle\n   - `vista/server/services/credential_service.py` - Secret management\n   - `vista/server/services/access_profile_service.py` - Permission control\n\n2. **Routes** (new sandbox routes):\n   - `vista/server/routes/sandbox.py` - Container management endpoints\n   - `vista/server/routes/credentials.py` - Secret management endpoints\n\n3. **Models** (new data models):\n   - `vista/server/models/sandbox.py` - Container state\n   - `vista/server/models/credential.py` - Credential metadata\n\n4. **Configuration**:\n   - Extend `vista/server/config.py` with sandbox defaults\n   - Update `vista/settings.json` with sandbox settings schema\n\n5. **Integration Points**:\n   - Modify `RalphService.create_job()` to support sandbox execution\n   - Extend `LoopService` for sandboxed loops\n   - Update provider invocation to support containerized execution\n\n6. **Database/Persistence**:\n   - Consider adding SQLite/JSON store for credential encryption\n   - Extend job.json schema with sandbox metadata\n\n---\n\nThis comprehensive overview should give you a solid understanding of the vista architecture for planning the Docker sandbox feature. All file paths are absolute from the vista project root."}],"totalDurationMs":93039,"totalTokens":81462,"totalToolUseCount":25,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":558,"cache_read_input_tokens":75434,"output_tokens":5470,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":558,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[]}}}
