{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01N4VTcqw6Eb1qiaBTENsS3R","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LbYHyYFyHFn6K1Eb6eDYGj","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/.vista/ralph/docker-sandbox-2bd3e57b/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","content":"# Implementation Plan: Docker Sandbox for Ralph Loops\n\n## Overview\n\nThis plan implements Docker-based sandboxing for Ralph loop execution, adding container isolation for both Claude Code and OpenCode providers. The sandbox wraps existing loop execution in per-loop Docker containers with credential mounting, while OpenCode loops use a host-side `opencode serve` proxy pattern.\n\n**Specs covered:**\n- `settings.md` — sandbox settings schema + defaults\n- `credential-management.md` — credential providers + path translation\n- `access-profiles.md` — named mount profiles\n- `container-lifecycle.md` — ContainerManager + OpenCodeServeManager\n- `ralph-mcp-integration.md` — RalphService sandbox branch + loop templates\n- `dashboard-ui.md` — sandbox toggle + inline status\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Settings & Configuration Foundation\n\n**Goal:** Extend `config.py` and settings schema with sandbox section so all subsequent phases can read configuration.\n\n### Step 1.1: Sandbox defaults in `config.py`\n\n**File:** `vista/server/config.py`\n\n- Add `_SANDBOX_DEFAULTS` dict matching the spec's `DEFAULT_SANDBOX`:\n  ```python\n  _SANDBOX_DEFAULTS = {\n      \"enabled\": False,\n      \"image\": \"vista-ralph:latest\",\n      \"network\": True,\n      \"opencode_serve\": {\"port\": 4096, \"auto_start\": True},\n      \"credentials\": {\n          \"claude_auth\": True,\n          \"git_ssh\": True,\n          \"git_config\": True,\n          \"github_cli\": False,\n          \"custom\": [],\n      },\n      \"profiles\": {\n          \"full-access\": {\"mounts\": [{\"path\": \".\", \"mode\": \"rw\"}]},\n          \"feature-scoped\": {\"mounts\": [\n              {\"path\": \".vista/features/${FEATURE}\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n              {\"path\": \".vista/ralph/${FEATURE}\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n              {\"path\": \"src\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n              {\"path\": \"tests\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n              {\"path\": \".git\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n          ]},\n          \"research-only\": {\"mounts\": [{\"path\": \".\", \"mode\": \"ro\"}], \"network\": False},\n      },\n      \"model_defaults\": {},\n  }\n  ```\n- Add functions:\n  - `get_sandbox_settings() -> dict` — merge `ralph.sandbox` from settings with `_SANDBOX_DEFAULTS`\n  - `is_sandbox_enabled() -> bool` — shortcut check\n  - `get_sandbox_profile(name: str) -> dict | None`\n  - `get_sandbox_credentials() -> dict`\n  - `get_opencode_serve_settings() -> dict`\n  - `save_sandbox_settings(sandbox_config: dict)` — write `ralph.sandbox` section\n\n### Step 1.2: Settings validation\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/sandbox_settings.py` (new)\n\n- Validation functions called on load and save:\n  - `validate_sandbox_settings(config: dict) -> list[str]` — returns list of validation errors\n  - Validates: boolean fields, port range (1024-65535), mount paths (relative, no `..`), mount modes (`rw`/`ro`), profile names (alphanumeric+hyphens), `model_defaults` references existing profiles\n  - On load: log warnings for invalid fields, apply defaults. Don't crash.\n  - On save: reject with validation errors.\n\n### Step 1.3: Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_sandbox_settings.py` (new)\n\n- Test defaults application (missing section, partial section, empty section)\n- Test validation (invalid modes, missing fields, path traversal rejection, port range)\n- Test write-back (preserves other sections)\n- Test `is_sandbox_enabled()` shortcut\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Credential Management\n\n**Goal:** Implement credential providers that detect, configure, and validate host credentials for Docker mounting.\n\n### Step 2.1: Data models\n\n**File:** `vista/server/models/sandbox.py` (new)\n\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass CredentialDetection:\n    found: bool\n    method: str           # \"env_var\", \"config_dir\", \"config_file\", \"not_found\"\n    source_path: str\n    display_info: str\n\n@dataclass\nclass DockerMount:\n    host_path: str\n    container_path: str\n    mode: str             # \"ro\" or \"rw\"\n\n@dataclass\nclass DockerCredentialConfig:\n    env_vars: dict[str, str]\n    mounts: list[DockerMount]\n\n@dataclass\nclass MountSpec:\n    path: str\n    mode: str\n\n@dataclass\nclass AccessProfile:\n    name: str\n    mounts: list[MountSpec]\n    network: bool | None  # None = inherit global\n\n@dataclass\nclass ContainerInfo:\n    name: str\n    job_id: str\n    provider: str\n    status: str\n    labels: dict[str, str]\n```\n\n### Step 2.2: Path translator\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/path_translator.py` (new)\n\n```python\nclass PathTranslator:\n    def translate(self, host_path: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Convert host path to Docker bind mount path.\n        Windows: C:\\\\Users\\\\Grove\\\\.ssh → /c/Users/Grove/.ssh\n        Others: no change needed.\n        \"\"\"\n\n    def get_host_uid_gid(self) -> tuple[int, int]:\n        \"\"\"Get UID/GID. Windows/WSL2: (1000, 1000). Linux/macOS: os.getuid/getgid.\"\"\"\n```\n\n### Step 2.3: Credential providers\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/credential_providers.py` (new)\n\n- Base class `CredentialProvider` with abstract methods: `detect()`, `get_docker_config()`, `get_validation_command()`\n- `ClaudeAuthProvider` — detects `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` env var and `~/.claude/` dir; `applies_to: [\"claude\"]`\n- `GitSshProvider` — detects `~/.ssh/` with key files; `applies_to: [\"*\"]`\n- `GitConfigProvider` — detects `~/.gitconfig`; `applies_to: [\"*\"]`\n- `GitHubCliProvider` — detects `~/.config/gh/` (Linux/macOS) or `%APPDATA%\\GitHub CLI\\` (Windows); `applies_to: [\"*\"]`\n- `CustomMountProvider` — user-defined from settings; `applies_to: [\"*\"]`\n- Registry: `ALL_PROVIDERS` list for iteration\n- `gather_credentials(provider_name: str, settings: dict) -> list[DockerCredentialConfig]` — filter by `applies_to`, check settings toggles, detect, return configs\n\n### Step 2.4: Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_credential_providers.py` (new)\n\n- Test each provider's detection logic with mocked filesystem/env\n- Test path translation: Windows, Linux, macOS paths\n- Test Docker config generation (correct mount specs and env vars)\n- Test `applies_to` filtering (Claude-only creds skipped for OpenCode)\n- Test UID/GID detection per platform\n- Test `gather_credentials` end-to-end filtering\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Access Profiles\n\n**Goal:** Implement profile resolution, variable substitution, and mount translation.\n\n### Step 3.1: Profile service\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/access_profile_service.py` (new)\n\n- `resolve_profile(explicit: str | None, model: str, settings: dict) -> AccessProfile` — priority: explicit > model_defaults > \"full-access\"\n- `substitute_variables(mount_path: str, feature: str | None) -> str` — replace `${FEATURE}`, `${PROJECT_ROOT}`\n- `to_docker_mounts(profile: AccessProfile, project_root: Path, feature: str | None, translator: PathTranslator) -> list[dict]` — convert MountSpecs to Docker volume dicts\n- `validate_profile(profile: dict) -> list[str]` — at least one mount, paths relative, no `..`, valid modes\n- Network policy resolution: `profile.network ?? global_network`\n- OpenCode + network-disabled check: fail with clear error\n\n### Step 3.2: Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_access_profiles.py` (new)\n\n- Test profile resolution (explicit > model default > fallback)\n- Test variable substitution\n- Test mount translation to Docker volumes\n- Test validation rules\n- Test network policy resolution\n- Test OpenCode + network-disabled fails with clear error\n\n---\n\n## Phase 4: Container Lifecycle Management\n\n**Goal:** Implement `ContainerManager` for creating, monitoring, and tearing down containers.\n\n### Step 4.1: ContainerManager\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/container_manager.py` (new)\n\n- `docker` Python SDK as new dependency (add to requirements/pyproject)\n- Class `ContainerManager`:\n  - `__init__(self, session_id: str)` — generate unique session ID per Vista server start\n  - `create_loop_container(job_id, provider_name, project_root, credentials, profile_mounts, image, network, env_extra) -> ContainerInfo`\n    - Build volume mounts: profile mounts (project root → `/workspace/`) + credential mounts\n    - Build env vars from credentials + extras (`DEVCONTAINER=true`)\n    - Set labels: `managed-by=vista-ralph`, `vista-job-id`, `vista-provider`, `vista-session`, `vista-project`\n    - Container naming: `vista-ralph-{job_id[:8]}`\n    - `command=\"sleep infinity\"` to keep alive for exec\n    - `extra_hosts={\"host.docker.internal\": \"host-gateway\"}`\n    - `user=f\"{uid}:{gid}\"` from PathTranslator\n  - `exec_in_container(container_name, command, workdir, env, stdout_handle) -> ExecHandle` — docker exec, return PID\n  - `remove_container(container_name)` — stop + remove\n  - `cleanup_orphans() -> list[str]` — find containers with `managed-by=vista-ralph` where `vista-session != current`, remove them\n  - `shutdown_all()` — stop + remove all containers for current session\n  - `list_containers() -> list[ContainerInfo]`\n  - `is_docker_available() -> tuple[bool, str]` — check Docker daemon reachability, return (available, message)\n  - `ensure_image(image_name) -> str` — check if image exists, build if not from Dockerfile\n\n### Step 4.2: Docker image (Dockerfile)\n\n**File:** `vista/docker/Dockerfile` (new)\n\n- Based on claudebox reference Dockerfile with modifications:\n  - Inherit key structure: debian:bookworm, git, node, nvm, claude-code, gh, python, uv\n  - Build args: `USER_ID`, `GROUP_ID`, `NODE_VERSION`\n  - `DEVCONTAINER=true`\n  - `WORKDIR /workspace`\n  - Simplified entrypoint (no firewall, no zsh customization): just `sleep infinity` or `bash`\n  - Pre-install: `jq`, `curl` (needed for OpenCode proxy calls)\n  - Keep user creation with UID/GID matching\n\n### Step 4.3: OpenCodeServeManager\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/opencode_serve_manager.py` (new)\n\n- Class `OpenCodeServeManager`:\n  - `__init__(self, port: int)` — from settings\n  - `ensure_running()` — start `opencode serve --port {port} --hostname 127.0.0.1` if not running; health check via `GET http://localhost:{port}/doc`\n  - `create_session(job_id, cwd) -> str` — POST to opencode serve API to create session\n  - `close_session(job_id)` — close session on serve\n  - `stop()` — terminate the process\n  - `is_running() -> bool` — check process alive + health check\n\n### Step 4.4: Vista proxy endpoint\n\n**File:** `vista/server/routes/sandbox.py` (new)\n\n```python\nrouter = APIRouter(prefix=\"/api/sandbox\", tags=[\"sandbox\"])\n\n@router.post(\"/opencode/{session_id}/message\")\nasync def opencode_proxy_message(session_id: str, request: Request):\n    \"\"\"Forward message from container to opencode serve on host.\"\"\"\n\n@router.get(\"/status\")\nasync def sandbox_status():\n    \"\"\"Return Docker availability, image status.\"\"\"\n\n@router.put(\"/settings\")\nasync def update_sandbox_settings(body):\n    \"\"\"Toggle sandbox.enabled.\"\"\"\n\n@router.post(\"/credentials/validate\")\nasync def validate_credentials():\n    \"\"\"Run credential validation in temp container.\"\"\"\n\n@router.post(\"/image/build\")\nasync def build_image():\n    \"\"\"Trigger image rebuild.\"\"\"\n```\n\n### Step 4.5: Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_container_manager.py` (new)\n\n- Unit tests for container naming and label generation\n- Unit tests for volume mount construction\n- Unit tests for Docker availability detection\n- Mock-based tests for create/exec/remove flow\n- Test orphan cleanup logic\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_opencode_serve_manager.py` (new)\n\n- Test ensure_running with mock subprocess\n- Test session create/close with mock HTTP\n- Test health check logic\n\n---\n\n## Phase 5: RalphService Integration\n\n**Goal:** Add sandbox branch to `RalphService.create_job()` so loops route through Docker when enabled.\n\n### Step 5.1: Modify `create_job()` in RalphService\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/ralph_service.py` (modify)\n\n- At the start of `create_job()`, check `config.is_sandbox_enabled()`\n- **If sandbox disabled**: current behavior unchanged (subprocess.Popen with PowerShell/bash)\n- **If sandbox enabled**:\n  1. Resolve access profile via `access_profile_service.resolve_profile()`\n  2. Gather credentials via `credential_providers.gather_credentials(provider.name, settings)`\n  3. Always generate `loop.sh` (bash, never PowerShell — container is Linux)\n  4. For Claude Code: use existing `LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE` with `shell=\"sh\"` (invocation block already supports bash via `provider.get_invocation(\"sh\")`)\n  5. For OpenCode: use new `OPENCODE_SANDBOX_LOOP_TEMPLATE`\n  6. Call `container_manager.create_loop_container(...)` to create container\n  7. Call `container_manager.exec_in_container(...)` to run loop.sh\n  8. Store additional fields in job.json: `sandbox: true`, `container: \"vista-ralph-{job_id}\"`, `opencode_session: \"...\"` (OpenCode only)\n\n### Step 5.2: New loop template for OpenCode sandbox\n\n**File:** `vista/portable/ralph.py` (modify — add `OPENCODE_SANDBOX_LOOP_TEMPLATE`)\n\n- Bash script that:\n  - Reads PROMPT + task + progress (same as current template)\n  - Uses `curl` to POST to `http://$VISTA_HOST:$VISTA_PORT/api/sandbox/opencode/$OPENCODE_SESSION/message`\n  - Sends prompt + model as JSON body\n  - Pushes via git after each iteration\n  - Checks completion markers\n\n### Step 5.3: Modify `stop_job()`\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/ralph_service.py` (modify)\n\n- If `job.get(\"sandbox\")`:\n  - Kill the exec PID (same as now)\n  - If `job.get(\"opencode_session\")`: close the serve session\n  - Remove the container via `container_manager.remove_container()`\n- If not sandbox: current behavior\n\n### Step 5.4: Modify `get_job_status()`\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/ralph_service.py` (modify)\n\n- When sandbox is active and PID is not running, also check container status\n- Container gone + PID gone = apply same completion detection logic\n\n### Step 5.5: Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_ralph_service.py` (modify)\n\n- Test `create_job()` routes to ContainerManager when sandbox enabled\n- Test `create_job()` uses local subprocess when sandbox disabled\n- Test Claude Code loops use bash loop template\n- Test OpenCode loops use proxy loop template\n- Test job.json includes sandbox metadata\n- Test `stop_job()` with sandbox: kills PID, removes container, closes session\n\n---\n\n## Phase 6: App Lifecycle Integration\n\n**Goal:** Wire ContainerManager and OpenCodeServeManager into Vista's startup/shutdown lifecycle.\n\n### Step 6.1: Modify app lifespan\n\n**File:** `vista/server/app.py` (modify)\n\n- In `lifespan()` startup:\n  - If sandbox enabled: initialize `ContainerManager` with a new `session_id`\n  - Run `container_manager.cleanup_orphans()` — log removed containers\n  - Run credential validation (results logged to server output)\n  - Check Docker availability — log result\n  - Store manager instances in a module-level or app-state variable accessible to services\n- In `lifespan()` shutdown:\n  - `container_manager.shutdown_all()` — remove all managed containers\n  - `opencode_serve_manager.stop()` — stop serve if running\n- Register sandbox routes\n\n### Step 6.2: Module initialization\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/sandbox_init.py` (new)\n\n- `init_sandbox() -> tuple[ContainerManager | None, OpenCodeServeManager | None]`\n  - If sandbox not enabled, return (None, None)\n  - Create ContainerManager with session_id\n  - Create OpenCodeServeManager with port from settings\n  - Return instances\n- Global accessor functions: `get_container_manager()`, `get_opencode_serve_manager()`\n\n---\n\n## Phase 7: Dashboard UI\n\n**Goal:** Add sandbox toggle to Ralph settings page with inline Docker status.\n\n### Step 7.1: API endpoints\n\nAlready covered in Phase 4 (`vista/server/routes/sandbox.py`):\n- `GET /api/sandbox/status` — returns `{docker_available, docker_running, image_built, image_name}`\n- `PUT /api/sandbox/settings` — writes `{enabled: true|false}`\n\n### Step 7.2: Frontend toggle\n\n**File:** `vista/server/views/ralph_settings.html` (modify) or `vista/server/views/static/js/ralph-settings.js` (modify)\n\n- Add \"Docker Sandbox\" section after existing ralph settings\n- Toggle control bound to `ralph.sandbox.enabled`\n- When toggled ON: call `GET /api/sandbox/status`, display inline status:\n  - Green dot: \"Docker running\"\n  - Amber dot: \"Building image...\"\n  - Red dot: \"Docker not running\" + guidance\n  - Red dot: \"Docker Desktop required\" + install guidance\n- When toggled OFF: hide status text\n- Status checked on page load (if toggle ON) and on toggle change\n- No polling — manual refresh\n\n### Step 7.3: Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_sandbox_api.py` (new)\n\n- Test `GET /api/sandbox/status` returns correct state\n- Test `PUT /api/sandbox/settings` with enabled true/false\n- Test sandbox status endpoint handles Docker not available\n\n---\n\n## Phase 8: Integration Testing\n\n**Goal:** End-to-end validation of the full sandbox flow.\n\n### Step 8.1: Integration tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/integration/test_sandbox_lifecycle.py` (new)\n\n- Full `ralph_start` → `ralph_status` → `ralph_stop` with sandbox (Claude path) — requires Docker\n- Full cycle with sandbox (OpenCode path via serve proxy) — requires Docker + opencode\n- `ralph_summary` reads artifacts produced inside container\n- Orphan cleanup across Vista restarts\n- Concurrent loops in separate containers\n- Bypass mode: `sandbox.enabled = false` runs identically to pre-sandbox behavior\n\n---\n\n## New Files Summary\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `vista/server/services/sandbox_settings.py` | Settings validation |\n| `vista/server/models/sandbox.py` | Data models (CredentialDetection, DockerMount, AccessProfile, etc.) |\n| `vista/server/services/path_translator.py` | Host-to-Docker path conversion |\n| `vista/server/services/credential_providers.py` | Credential detection and Docker config generation |\n| `vista/server/services/access_profile_service.py` | Profile resolution, variable substitution, mount translation |\n| `vista/server/services/container_manager.py` | Docker container lifecycle |\n| `vista/server/services/opencode_serve_manager.py` | Host-side opencode serve management |\n| `vista/server/services/sandbox_init.py` | Module-level initialization and global accessors |\n| `vista/server/routes/sandbox.py` | Sandbox API endpoints (status, settings, proxy, validation) |\n| `vista/docker/Dockerfile` | Modified claudebox image for Vista |\n| `vista/tests/test_sandbox_settings.py` | Settings tests |\n| `vista/tests/test_credential_providers.py` | Credential provider tests |\n| `vista/tests/test_access_profiles.py` | Access profile tests |\n| `vista/tests/test_container_manager.py` | Container manager tests |\n| `vista/tests/test_opencode_serve_manager.py` | OpenCode serve manager tests |\n| `vista/tests/test_sandbox_api.py` | Sandbox API endpoint tests |\n| `vista/tests/integration/test_sandbox_lifecycle.py` | End-to-end integration tests |\n\n## Modified Files Summary\n\n| File | Changes |\n|------|---------|\n| `vista/server/config.py` | Add `_SANDBOX_DEFAULTS`, `get_sandbox_settings()`, `is_sandbox_enabled()`, etc. |\n| `vista/server/services/ralph_service.py` | Sandbox branch in `create_job()`, `stop_job()`, `get_job_status()` |\n| `vista/portable/ralph.py` | Add `OPENCODE_SANDBOX_LOOP_TEMPLATE` |\n| `vista/server/app.py` | Sandbox lifecycle in startup/shutdown, register sandbox routes |\n| `vista/server/views/ralph_settings.html` | Sandbox toggle + inline status |\n| `vista/tests/test_ralph_service.py` | Add sandbox-specific test cases |\n\n## New Dependencies\n\n| Package | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|\n| `docker` | Python Docker SDK for container management |\n| `httpx` (or `aiohttp`) | Async HTTP client for opencode serve proxy (if not already present via FastAPI) |\n\nNote: `httpx` is likely already available via FastAPI/Starlette. The `docker` package is the main new dependency.\n\n## Implementation Order\n\nThe phases are designed to be built incrementally, each building on the last:\n\n```\nPhase 1 (Settings)        → Foundation for all other phases\nPhase 2 (Credentials)     → Needed by ContainerManager\nPhase 3 (Profiles)        → Needed by ContainerManager\nPhase 4 (Container+Serve) → Core sandbox infrastructure\nPhase 5 (RalphService)    → Integration with existing loop execution\nPhase 6 (App Lifecycle)   → Startup/shutdown wiring\nPhase 7 (Dashboard UI)    → User-facing toggle\nPhase 8 (Integration)     → End-to-end validation\n```\n\nPhases 2 and 3 can be developed in parallel since they have no interdependencies.\n\n## Spec Alignment Checklist\n\n| Domain Requirement | Spec | Implementation Phase |\n|---|---|---|\n| Prevent file access outside project | access-profiles, container-lifecycle | Phase 3, 4 |\n| Eliminate credential complexity for OpenCode | credential-management, container-lifecycle | Phase 2, 4 |\n| Claudebox as base image | container-lifecycle | Phase 4.2 |\n| Transparent sandbox (infrastructure concern) | ralph-mcp-integration | Phase 5 |\n| Agent access to feature specs | access-profiles (\"full-access\" default) | Phase 3 |\n| Full bypass when disabled | settings, ralph-mcp-integration | Phase 1, 5 |\n| Container-per-loop isolation | container-lifecycle | Phase 4 |\n| Orphan cleanup on startup | container-lifecycle | Phase 6 |\n| Single dashboard toggle | dashboard-ui | Phase 7 |\n| Zero Docker knowledge required | dashboard-ui, settings | Phase 1, 7 |\n| Credential auto-detection | credential-management | Phase 2 |\n| Credential validation at startup | credential-management | Phase 6 |\n| OpenCode serve management | container-lifecycle | Phase 4.3 |\n| Vista proxy for OpenCode | ralph-mcp-integration | Phase 4.4, 5.2 |\n| Path translation (Windows→Docker) | credential-management | Phase 2.2 |\n| UID/GID matching | credential-management | Phase 2.2 |\n| Docker availability check | dashboard-ui, container-lifecycle | Phase 4.1, 7 |\n| Settings validation | settings | Phase 1.2 |\n| No changes to MCP tool interface | ralph-mcp-integration | Phase 5 (transparent) |\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":232,"cache_read_input_tokens":103018,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":232},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14b921d9-eeaf-453d-9533-337d6f497996","uuid":"bd208838-bc90-4816-815e-2d3d80c505be"}
