{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E1afjFAKCnDWwNqg6Zvu6a","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Implementation Plan: Docker Sandbox for Ralph Loops\n     2→\n     3→## Overview\n     4→\n     5→This plan implements Docker-based sandboxing for ralph loops, using a modified claudebox container image. The feature has two execution paths: **Claude Code** (runs natively inside container) and **OpenCode** (calls host-side `opencode serve` via Vista proxy). The sandbox is opt-in via `sandbox.enabled` toggle and fully transparent to the MCP tool interface.\n     6→\n     7→---\n     8→\n     9→## Phase 1: Foundation — Settings, Config, Data Models\n    10→\n    11→### 1.1 Sandbox Settings Schema & Config Loading\n    12→\n    13→**File: `vista/server/config.py`**\n    14→\n    15→- Add `_SANDBOX_DEFAULTS` dict matching the full schema from the settings spec:\n    16→  ```python\n    17→  _SANDBOX_DEFAULTS = {\n    18→      \"enabled\": False,\n    19→      \"image\": \"vista-ralph:latest\",\n    20→      \"network\": True,\n    21→      \"opencode_serve\": {\"port\": 4096, \"auto_start\": True},\n    22→      \"credentials\": {\n    23→          \"claude_auth\": True, \"git_ssh\": True,\n    24→          \"git_config\": True, \"github_cli\": False, \"custom\": [],\n    25→      },\n    26→      \"profiles\": {\n    27→          \"full-access\": {\"mounts\": [{\"path\": \".\", \"mode\": \"rw\"}]},\n    28→          \"feature-scoped\": {\"mounts\": [\n    29→              {\"path\": \".vista/features/${FEATURE}\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n    30→              {\"path\": \".vista/ralph/${FEATURE}\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n    31→              {\"path\": \"src\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n    32→              {\"path\": \"tests\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n    33→              {\"path\": \".git\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n    34→          ]},\n    35→          \"research-only\": {\"mounts\": [{\"path\": \".\", \"mode\": \"ro\"}], \"network\": False},\n    36→      },\n    37→      \"model_defaults\": {},\n    38→  }\n    39→  ```\n    40→- Add functions:\n    41→  - `get_sandbox_settings() -> dict` — merges `ralph.sandbox` from settings.json with defaults\n    42→  - `is_sandbox_enabled() -> bool` — quick check\n    43→  - `get_sandbox_profile(name: str) -> dict | None`\n    44→  - `get_sandbox_credentials() -> dict`\n    45→  - `get_opencode_serve_settings() -> dict`\n    46→  - `save_sandbox_settings(sandbox_config: dict) -> None` — validates and writes back\n    47→- Add validation logic:\n    48→  - `enabled` is bool\n    49→  - `image` is string\n    50→  - `network` is bool\n    51→  - `opencode_serve.port` is int 1024-65535\n    52→  - Credential toggles are bools\n    53→  - Custom mounts have required fields\n    54→  - Profiles have at least one mount\n    55→  - Mount paths are relative (no `..` traversal)\n    56→  - Mount modes are `\"rw\"` or `\"ro\"`\n    57→  - Profile names are alphanumeric + hyphens\n    58→  - Invalid config on load: log warning, apply defaults for invalid fields\n    59→\n    60→**Tests:**\n    61→- Unit tests for defaults application (missing section, partial, empty)\n    62→- Unit tests for validation (invalid modes, missing fields, path traversal rejection)\n    63→- Unit tests for settings write-back (preserves other sections)\n    64→\n    65→### 1.2 Data Models\n    66→\n    67→**New file: `vista/server/models/sandbox.py`**\n    68→\n    69→Define dataclasses used across the sandbox feature:\n    70→\n    71→```python\n    72→@dataclass\n    73→class MountSpec:\n    74→    path: str        # Relative to project root, supports ${FEATURE}\n    75→    mode: str        # \"rw\" or \"ro\"\n    76→\n    77→@dataclass\n    78→class AccessProfile:\n    79→    name: str\n    80→    mounts: list[MountSpec]\n    81→    network: bool | None  # None = inherit global\n    82→\n    83→@dataclass\n    84→class CredentialDetection:\n    85→    found: bool\n    86→    method: str           # \"env_var\", \"config_dir\", \"config_file\", \"not_found\"\n    87→    source_path: str\n    88→    display_info: str\n    89→\n    90→@dataclass\n    91→class DockerMount:\n    92→    host_path: str\n    93→    container_path: str\n    94→    mode: str\n    95→\n    96→@dataclass\n    97→class DockerCredentialConfig:\n    98→    env_vars: dict[str, str]\n    99→    mounts: list[DockerMount]\n   100→\n   101→@dataclass\n   102→class ContainerInfo:\n   103→    name: str\n   104→    job_id: str\n   105→    provider: str\n   106→    status: str\n   107→    session_id: str\n   108→```\n   109→\n   110→---\n   111→\n   112→## Phase 2: Credential Management\n   113→\n   114→### 2.1 Path Translation\n   115→\n   116→**New file: `vista/server/services/sandbox/path_translator.py`**\n   117→\n   118→```python\n   119→class PathTranslator:\n   120→    def translate(self, host_path: str) -> str:\n   121→        \"\"\"Convert host path to Docker bind mount path.\n   122→        Windows: C:\\\\Users\\\\Grove\\\\.ssh → /c/Users/Grove/.ssh\n   123→        Others: no change needed.\n   124→        \"\"\"\n   125→```\n   126→\n   127→- Detect platform via `platform.system()`\n   128→- Windows: convert drive letter pattern `X:\\...` to `/x/...`\n   129→- Linux/macOS: passthrough\n   130→\n   131→### 2.2 UID/GID Detection\n   132→\n   133→**In `path_translator.py` or standalone utility:**\n   134→\n   135→```python\n   136→def get_host_uid_gid() -> tuple[int, int]:\n   137→    \"\"\"Windows/WSL2: (1000, 1000). Linux/macOS: os.getuid(), os.getgid().\"\"\"\n   138→```\n   139→\n   140→### 2.3 Credential Providers\n   141→\n   142→**New file: `vista/server/services/sandbox/credential_providers.py`**\n   143→\n   144→Implement the `CredentialProvider` base class and four built-in providers:\n   145→\n   146→1. **`ClaudeAuthProvider`** — `applies_to: [\"claude\"]`\n   147→   - Detects `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` env var, then `~/.claude/` directory\n   148→   - Docker config: env var forwarding + `~/.claude/` mount (rw)\n   149→   - Validation: `claude --version`\n   150→\n   151→2. **`GitSshProvider`** — `applies_to: [\"*\"]`\n   152→   - Detects `~/.ssh/` with key files\n   153→   - Docker config: `~/.ssh/` mount (ro)\n   154→   - Validation: `ssh -T git@github.com`\n   155→\n   156→3. **`GitConfigProvider`** — `applies_to: [\"*\"]`\n   157→   - Detects `~/.gitconfig`\n   158→   - Docker config: `~/.gitconfig` mount (ro)\n   159→   - Validation: `git config user.name && git config user.email`\n   160→\n   161→4. **`GitHubCliProvider`** — `applies_to: [\"*\"]`\n   162→   - Detects `~/.config/gh/` (Linux/macOS) or `%APPDATA%\\GitHub CLI\\` (Windows)\n   163→   - Docker config: mount (ro)\n   164→   - Validation: `gh auth status`\n   165→\n   166→5. **`CustomMountProvider`** — from settings `custom` array\n   167→   - Detects: host path exists\n   168→   - Docker config: as specified\n   169→   - Validation: `test -r {container_path}`\n   170→\n   171→### 2.4 Credential Gathering\n   172→\n   173→```python\n   174→def gather_credentials(provider_name: str, settings: dict) -> list[DockerCredentialConfig]:\n   175→    \"\"\"Iterate providers, filter by applies_to + enabled, detect, return configs.\"\"\"\n   176→```\n   177→\n   178→**Tests:**\n   179→- Unit tests per provider: detection with mocked filesystem/env\n   180→- Unit tests for path translation: Windows, Linux, macOS\n   181→- Unit tests for Docker config generation\n   182→- Unit tests for `applies_to` filtering\n   183→\n   184→---\n   185→\n   186→## Phase 3: Access Profiles\n   187→\n   188→### 3.1 Profile Resolution\n   189→\n   190→**New file: `vista/server/services/sandbox/access_profiles.py`**\n   191→\n   192→```python\n   193→def resolve_profile(explicit: str | None, model: str, settings: dict) -> AccessProfile:\n   194→    \"\"\"Priority: explicit > model_defaults > 'full-access'.\"\"\"\n   195→\n   196→def substitute_variables(mount_path: str, feature: str) -> str:\n   197→    \"\"\"Replace ${FEATURE}, ${PROJECT_ROOT} in mount paths.\"\"\"\n   198→\n   199→def to_docker_mounts(profile: AccessProfile, project_root: Path, translator: PathTranslator) -> list[dict]:\n   200→    \"\"\"Convert profile mounts to Docker bind mount dicts.\"\"\"\n   201→```\n   202→\n   203→- Validate: paths relative, no `..`, at least one mount\n   204→- Special case: `\".\"` → mount entire project root as `/workspace/`\n   205→- Skip non-existent mount paths with warning (not error)\n   206→- Error if OpenCode + `network: false` profile\n   207→\n   208→**Tests:**\n   209→- Unit tests for profile resolution chain\n   210→- Unit tests for variable substitution\n   211→- Unit tests for mount translation\n   212→- Unit tests for validation rules\n   213→- Unit test: OpenCode + network-disabled = error\n   214→\n   215→---\n   216→\n   217→## Phase 4: Container Lifecycle Management\n   218→\n   219→### 4.1 ContainerManager\n   220→\n   221→**New file: `vista/server/services/sandbox/container_manager.py`**\n   222→\n   223→Depends on `docker` Python SDK (new dependency: `pip install docker`).\n   224→\n   225→```python\n   226→class ContainerManager:\n   227→    def __init__(self, session_id: str):\n   228→        self.docker = docker.from_env()\n   229→        self.session_id = session_id\n   230→\n   231→    async def create_loop_container(\n   232→        self, job_id, provider_name, project_root, credentials, image, network=True\n   233→    ) -> ContainerInfo\n   234→\n   235→    async def exec_in_container(\n   236→        self, container_name, command, workdir=\"/workspace\", env=None, stdout_handle=None\n   237→    ) -> ExecHandle\n   238→\n   239→    async def remove_container(self, container_name) -> None\n   240→    async def cleanup_orphans(self) -> list[str]\n   241→    async def shutdown_all(self) -> None\n   242→    def list_containers(self) -> list[ContainerInfo]\n   243→```\n   244→\n   245→Key implementation details:\n   246→- Container created with `command=\"sleep infinity\"`, loop runs via `docker exec`\n   247→- Labels: `managed-by=vista-ralph`, `vista-job-id`, `vista-provider`, `vista-session`, `vista-project`\n   248→- `extra_hosts={\"host.docker.internal\": \"host-gateway\"}` for Linux compatibility\n   249→- `user=f\"{uid}:{gid}\"` from `get_host_uid_gid()`\n   250→- `DEVCONTAINER=true` env var\n   251→\n   252→### 4.2 Docker Image Management\n   253→\n   254→```python\n   255→async def ensure_image(self, image_name=\"vista-ralph:latest\") -> str:\n   256→    \"\"\"Check if image exists locally. If not, build from bundled Dockerfile.\"\"\"\n   257→```\n   258→\n   259→- Bundle a simplified Dockerfile in `vista/server/data/sandbox/Dockerfile` based on claudebox\n   260→- Build args: `USER_ID`, `GROUP_ID`, `NODE_VERSION`\n   261→- Store image hash in settings to detect Dockerfile changes\n   262→\n   263→### 4.3 Orphan Cleanup\n   264→\n   265→- On Vista startup: query containers with label `managed-by=vista-ralph` where `vista-session != current_session`\n   266→- Stop and remove orphans\n   267→- Log removed container names\n   268→\n   269→**Tests:**\n   270→- Unit tests for container naming and label generation\n   271→- Unit tests for volume mount construction\n   272→- Integration tests (real Docker): create → exec → remove\n   273→- Integration test: orphan cleanup\n   274→\n   275→---\n   276→\n   277→## Phase 5: OpenCode Serve Management\n   278→\n   279→### 5.1 OpenCodeServeManager\n   280→\n   281→**New file: `vista/server/services/sandbox/opencode_serve_manager.py`**\n   282→\n   283→```python\n   284→class OpenCodeServeManager:\n   285→    def __init__(self, port: int = 4096):\n   286→        self.port = port\n   287→        self.process: subprocess.Popen | None = None\n   288→        self.sessions: dict[str, str] = {}  # job_id → session_id\n   289→\n   290→    async def ensure_running(self) -> None\n   291→    async def create_session(self, job_id: str, cwd: str) -> str\n   292→    async def close_session(self, job_id: str) -> None\n   293→    async def stop(self) -> None\n   294→    def is_running(self) -> bool\n   295→```\n   296→\n   297→- Starts `opencode serve --port {port} --hostname 127.0.0.1`\n   298→- Health check: `GET http://localhost:{port}/doc`\n   299→- Auto-restart on failure\n   300→\n   301→### 5.2 Vista Proxy Endpoint\n   302→\n   303→**New file: `vista/server/routes/sandbox.py`**\n   304→\n   305→```python\n   306→router = APIRouter(prefix=\"/api/sandbox\", tags=[\"sandbox\"])\n   307→\n   308→@router.post(\"/opencode/{session_id}/message\")\n   309→async def opencode_proxy_message(session_id: str, request: Request):\n   310→    \"\"\"Forward message to opencode serve session on host.\"\"\"\n   311→\n   312→@router.get(\"/status\")\n   313→async def sandbox_status():\n   314→    \"\"\"Returns { docker_available, docker_running, image_built, image_name }.\"\"\"\n   315→\n   316→@router.put(\"/settings\")\n   317→async def sandbox_settings_update(body: dict):\n   318→    \"\"\"Write sandbox.enabled toggle.\"\"\"\n   319→\n   320→@router.post(\"/credentials/validate\")\n   321→async def validate_credentials():\n   322→    \"\"\"Run credential validation in temp container.\"\"\"\n   323→\n   324→@router.post(\"/image/build\")\n   325→async def build_image():\n   326→    \"\"\"Trigger sandbox image build.\"\"\"\n   327→```\n   328→\n   329→**Tests:**\n   330→- Integration test: opencode serve start, health check, session create/close, stop\n   331→- API test: proxy endpoint forwards correctly\n   332→\n   333→---\n   334→\n   335→## Phase 6: RalphService Integration\n   336→\n   337→### 6.1 Modify `create_job()` in `vista/server/services/ralph_service.py`\n   338→\n   339→Add sandbox branch to `create_job()`:\n   340→\n   341→```python\n   342→def create_job(self, project_root, slug, mode, task_description, provider, model, iterations):\n   343→    # ... existing setup (job_id, job_dir, task_file, prompt, loop script) ...\n   344→\n   345→    sandbox_settings = config.get_sandbox_settings()\n   346→    if sandbox_settings.get(\"enabled\"):\n   347→        return self._create_sandbox_job(\n   348→            job_dir, project_root, slug, mode, task_description,\n   349→            provider, model, iterations, sandbox_settings\n   350→        )\n   351→    else:\n   352→        # Current behavior: local subprocess\n   353→        return self._create_local_job(...)\n   354→```\n   355→\n   356→**`_create_sandbox_job` flow (Claude Code):**\n   357→1. Generate `loop.sh` (always bash in container)\n   358→2. Gather credentials (claude_auth + git_ssh + git_config)\n   359→3. Resolve access profile\n   360→4. `container_manager.create_loop_container(...)`\n   361→5. `container_manager.exec_in_container(command=[\"bash\", loop.sh])`\n   362→6. Track exec PID + container name in job.json\n   363→\n   364→**`_create_sandbox_job` flow (OpenCode):**\n   365→1. Ensure `opencode serve` running on host\n   366→2. Create serve session\n   367→3. Generate `loop.sh` from `OPENCODE_SANDBOX_LOOP_TEMPLATE`\n   368→4. Gather credentials (git_ssh + git_config only, no AI creds)\n   369→5. `container_manager.create_loop_container(...)`\n   370→6. `container_manager.exec_in_container(command=[\"bash\", loop.sh], env={VISTA_HOST, VISTA_PORT, OPENCODE_SESSION, MODEL})`\n   371→7. Track exec PID + container name + session_id in job.json\n   372→\n   373→### 6.2 New Loop Script Template\n   374→\n   375→**Add to `vista/portable/ralph.py`:**\n   376→\n   377→`OPENCODE_SANDBOX_LOOP_TEMPLATE` — bash script that calls Vista proxy via `curl` instead of `opencode run`. (Full template is in the ralph-mcp-integration spec.)\n   378→\n   379→### 6.3 Modify Loop Script Generation\n   380→\n   381→When sandbox is enabled:\n   382→- Always generate `loop.sh` (bash), never `loop.ps1`\n   383→- For Claude: use existing `LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE` with `shell=\"sh\"` (already works)\n   384→- For OpenCode: use new `OPENCODE_SANDBOX_LOOP_TEMPLATE`\n   385→\n   386→### 6.4 Modify `stop_job()`\n   387→\n   388→```python\n   389→def stop_job(self, project_root, job_id):\n   390→    job = self._load_job(...)\n   391→    if job.get(\"sandbox\"):\n   392→        self._kill_pid(job[\"pid\"])\n   393→        if job.get(\"opencode_session\"):\n   394→            await opencode_serve_manager.close_session(job_id)\n   395→        await container_manager.remove_container(f\"vista-ralph-{job_id}\")\n   396→    else:\n   397→        # Current behavior\n   398→        self._kill_pid(job[\"pid\"])\n   399→```\n   400→\n   401→### 6.5 Modify `get_job_status()`\n   402→\n   403→When sandbox is active, also check container status (is container still running?).\n   404→\n   405→### 6.6 Job Metadata Extension\n   406→\n   407→When sandbox is active, `job.json` includes:\n   408→```json\n   409→{\n   410→  \"sandbox\": true,\n   411→  \"container\": \"vista-ralph-{job_id}\",\n   412→  \"opencode_session\": \"sess_xyz789\"  // OpenCode only\n   413→}\n   414→```\n   415→\n   416→**Tests:**\n   417→- Unit test: `create_job()` routes to container when `sandbox.enabled = true`\n   418→- Unit test: `create_job()` uses local subprocess when `sandbox.enabled = false`\n   419→- Unit test: Claude loops use bash template\n   420→- Unit test: OpenCode loops use proxy template\n   421→- Unit test: job.json includes sandbox metadata\n   422→- Unit test: `stop_job()` removes container + closes session\n   423→- Integration test: full `ralph_start` → `ralph_status` → `ralph_stop` cycle\n   424→\n   425→---\n   426→\n   427→## Phase 7: Credential Validation\n   428→\n   429→### 7.1 Validation Flow\n   430→\n   431→**In `vista/server/services/sandbox/credential_validation.py`:**\n   432→\n   433→```python\n   434→async def validate_credentials(\n   435→    credential_providers: list[CredentialProvider],\n   436→    container_manager: ContainerManager,\n   437→    image: str,\n   438→) -> list[ValidationResult]:\n   439→    \"\"\"\n   440→    1. Detect all enabled credentials on host\n   441→    2. Create temp container with credential mounts\n   442→    3. Run validation command per credential inside container\n   443→    4. Collect pass/fail\n   444→    5. Tear down temp container\n   445→    \"\"\"\n   446→```\n   447→\n   448→- Runs automatically at Vista startup when `sandbox.enabled = true`\n   449→- Results logged to Vista server log\n   450→- Also available via `POST /api/sandbox/credentials/validate`\n   451→\n   452→**Tests:**\n   453→- Integration test: full validation flow with real Docker\n   454→\n   455→---\n   456→\n   457→## Phase 8: Vista App Startup Integration\n   458→\n   459→### 8.1 Modify `vista/server/app.py` Lifespan\n   460→\n   461→In the `lifespan` context manager:\n   462→\n   463→**Startup:**\n   464→1. Generate unique session_id\n   465→2. If `sandbox.enabled`:\n   466→   - Attempt `docker.from_env()` — if fails, log error, mark sandbox unavailable\n   467→   - Run `container_manager.cleanup_orphans()`\n   468→   - Run credential validation (log results)\n   469→   - Ensure Docker image exists (build if needed)\n   470→3. Initialize `ContainerManager(session_id)`\n   471→4. Initialize `OpenCodeServeManager(port)` (lazy — doesn't start serve until first OpenCode loop)\n   472→\n   473→**Shutdown:**\n   474→1. `container_manager.shutdown_all()` — stop and remove all managed containers\n   475→2. `opencode_serve_manager.stop()` — stop serve if running\n   476→\n   477→### 8.2 Register Sandbox Routes\n   478→\n   479→Add `sandbox` router to `app.py`:\n   480→```python\n   481→from server.routes import sandbox\n   482→app.include_router(sandbox.router)\n   483→```\n   484→\n   485→---\n   486→\n   487→## Phase 9: Dashboard UI\n   488→\n   489→### 9.1 Sandbox Toggle in Ralph Settings\n   490→\n   491→**File: `vista/server/views/ralph_settings.html`**\n   492→\n   493→Add a \"Docker Sandbox\" toggle section:\n   494→- Toggle control bound to `sandbox.enabled`\n   495→- When ON: call `GET /api/sandbox/status` and display inline status:\n   496→  - Green dot: \"Docker running\"\n   497→  - Amber dot: \"Building image...\"\n   498→  - Red dot: \"Docker not running\" + guidance\n   499→  - Red dot: \"Docker Desktop required\" + install guidance\n   500→- When OFF: no status check\n   501→\n   502→**API used:**\n   503→- `GET /api/sandbox/status` → `{ docker_available, docker_running, image_built, image_name }`\n   504→- `PUT /api/sandbox/settings` → `{ enabled: true|false }`\n   505→\n   506→**Tests:**\n   507→- API test: status returns correct Docker/image state\n   508→- API test: settings toggle saves correctly\n   509→\n   510→---\n   511→\n   512→## Phase 10: Docker Image Bundling\n   513→\n   514→### 10.1 Modified Claudebox Dockerfile\n   515→\n   516→**New file: `vista/server/data/sandbox/Dockerfile`**\n   517→\n   518→Based on the claudebox Dockerfile with modifications:\n   519→- Slimmer (remove zsh, tmux, delta, fzf — optional tooling)\n   520→- Keep: git, Node.js, Claude Code CLI, Python, bash, gh CLI, jq, curl\n   521→- Build args: `USER_ID`, `GROUP_ID`, `NODE_VERSION`\n   522→- `DEVCONTAINER=true` env var\n   523→- `WORKDIR /workspace`\n   524→- `ENTRYPOINT [\"sleep\", \"infinity\"]` (simpler than claudebox entrypoint — we use `docker exec`)\n   525→\n   526→### 10.2 Docker Ignore\n   527→\n   528→**New file: `vista/server/data/sandbox/.dockerignore`**\n   529→\n   530→Standard ignores for build context.\n   531→\n   532→---\n   533→\n   534→## Dependency Summary\n   535→\n   536→| New Dependency | Purpose | Install |\n   537→|---|---|---|\n   538→| `docker` (Python SDK) | Docker API access | `pip install docker` |\n   539→\n   540→This goes in the plugin's requirements/dependencies. Since the plugin runs as an MCP server (Python process), the `docker` package needs to be available at runtime. It should be added as an optional dependency — sandbox features gracefully degrade if `docker` is not installed.\n   541→\n   542→---\n   543→\n   544→## File Creation / Modification Summary\n   545→\n   546→### New Files\n   547→\n   548→| File | Purpose |\n   549→|---|---|\n   550→| `vista/server/models/sandbox.py` | Dataclasses: MountSpec, AccessProfile, DockerMount, etc. |\n   551→| `vista/server/services/sandbox/__init__.py` | Package init |\n   552→| `vista/server/services/sandbox/path_translator.py` | Host-to-Docker path conversion + UID/GID |\n   553→| `vista/server/services/sandbox/credential_providers.py` | 5 credential providers + gathering logic |\n   554→| `vista/server/services/sandbox/access_profiles.py` | Profile resolution, variable substitution, Docker mount conversion |\n   555→| `vista/server/services/sandbox/container_manager.py` | Container lifecycle: create, exec, remove, orphan cleanup, image management |\n   556→| `vista/server/services/sandbox/opencode_serve_manager.py` | Host-side `opencode serve` process management |\n   557→| `vista/server/services/sandbox/credential_validation.py` | Credential validation flow |\n   558→| `vista/server/routes/sandbox.py` | API: status, settings toggle, proxy, credential validate, image build |\n   559→| `vista/server/data/sandbox/Dockerfile` | Modified claudebox Dockerfile for Vista sandbox |\n   560→| `vista/server/data/sandbox/.dockerignore` | Build context ignore |\n   561→| `vista/tests/test_sandbox_settings.py` | Settings schema tests |\n   562→| `vista/tests/test_credential_providers.py` | Credential provider tests |\n   563→| `vista/tests/test_access_profiles.py` | Profile resolution tests |\n   564→| `vista/tests/test_container_manager.py` | Container lifecycle tests |\n   565→| `vista/tests/test_path_translator.py` | Path translation tests |\n   566→\n   567→### Modified Files\n   568→\n   569→| File | Change |\n   570→|---|---|\n   571→| `vista/server/config.py` | Add `_SANDBOX_DEFAULTS`, `get_sandbox_settings()`, `is_sandbox_enabled()`, etc. |\n   572→| `vista/server/services/ralph_service.py` | Add sandbox branch in `create_job()`, `stop_job()`, `get_job_status()` |\n   573→| `vista/server/app.py` | Startup: init ContainerManager, orphan cleanup, credential validation. Shutdown: container cleanup. Register sandbox routes. |\n   574→| `vista/portable/ralph.py` | Add `OPENCODE_SANDBOX_LOOP_TEMPLATE` |\n   575→| `vista/server/views/ralph_settings.html` | Add sandbox toggle + inline status |\n   576→| `vista/settings.json` | No structural change (defaults applied at runtime), but example updated |\n   577→\n   578→---\n   579→\n   580→## Build Order (Recommended)\n   581→\n   582→The phases should be implemented sequentially, with each phase building on the previous:\n   583→\n   584→1. **Phase 1** (Settings + Data Models) — foundation for everything else\n   585→2. **Phase 2** (Credentials) — needed by container creation\n   586→3. **Phase 3** (Access Profiles) — needed by container creation\n   587→4. **Phase 4** (ContainerManager) — core container lifecycle\n   588→5. **Phase 5** (OpenCode Serve) — second execution path\n   589→6. **Phase 6** (RalphService Integration) — ties it all together\n   590→7. **Phase 7** (Credential Validation) — startup-time verification\n   591→8. **Phase 8** (App Startup) — lifecycle hooks\n   592→9. **Phase 9** (Dashboard UI) — user-facing toggle\n   593→10. **Phase 10** (Docker Image) — bundled Dockerfile\n   594→\n   595→Phases 2 + 3 can be done in parallel. Phases 7 + 9 + 10 can be done in parallel after Phase 6 is complete.\n   596→\n   597→---\n   598→\n   599→## Risk & Edge Cases\n   600→\n   601→| Risk | Mitigation |\n   602→|---|---|\n   603→| Docker not installed | Graceful degradation: sandbox marked unavailable, loops run locally |\n   604→| Docker SDK import failure | Lazy import; if `docker` package missing, sandbox features disabled with clear error |\n   605→| WSL2 bind mount performance | Acceptable per NFR; document in known limitations |\n   606→| Port conflict for opencode serve | Try next available port; log error |\n   607→| Concurrent loops on same project files | Git operations may conflict; acceptable per spec (documented) |\n   608→| Orphaned containers after crash | Cleanup on startup via session_id comparison |\n   609→| UID/GID mismatch | Use host UID/GID as build args (Windows defaults to 1000:1000) |\n   610→| `~/.claude/` must be rw | Explicitly mounted read-write (differs from claudebox copy pattern) |\n   611→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14b921d9-eeaf-453d-9533-337d6f497996","uuid":"dfdfcb74-1eff-4ddf-ae82-ec5c536fc46d","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/.vista/ralph/docker-sandbox-2bd3e57b/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","content":"# Implementation Plan: Docker Sandbox for Ralph Loops\n\n## Overview\n\nThis plan implements Docker-based sandboxing for ralph loops, using a modified claudebox container image. The feature has two execution paths: **Claude Code** (runs natively inside container) and **OpenCode** (calls host-side `opencode serve` via Vista proxy). The sandbox is opt-in via `sandbox.enabled` toggle and fully transparent to the MCP tool interface.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Foundation — Settings, Config, Data Models\n\n### 1.1 Sandbox Settings Schema & Config Loading\n\n**File: `vista/server/config.py`**\n\n- Add `_SANDBOX_DEFAULTS` dict matching the full schema from the settings spec:\n  ```python\n  _SANDBOX_DEFAULTS = {\n      \"enabled\": False,\n      \"image\": \"vista-ralph:latest\",\n      \"network\": True,\n      \"opencode_serve\": {\"port\": 4096, \"auto_start\": True},\n      \"credentials\": {\n          \"claude_auth\": True, \"git_ssh\": True,\n          \"git_config\": True, \"github_cli\": False, \"custom\": [],\n      },\n      \"profiles\": {\n          \"full-access\": {\"mounts\": [{\"path\": \".\", \"mode\": \"rw\"}]},\n          \"feature-scoped\": {\"mounts\": [\n              {\"path\": \".vista/features/${FEATURE}\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n              {\"path\": \".vista/ralph/${FEATURE}\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n              {\"path\": \"src\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n              {\"path\": \"tests\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n              {\"path\": \".git\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n          ]},\n          \"research-only\": {\"mounts\": [{\"path\": \".\", \"mode\": \"ro\"}], \"network\": False},\n      },\n      \"model_defaults\": {},\n  }\n  ```\n- Add functions:\n  - `get_sandbox_settings() -> dict` — merges `ralph.sandbox` from settings.json with defaults\n  - `is_sandbox_enabled() -> bool` — quick check\n  - `get_sandbox_profile(name: str) -> dict | None`\n  - `get_sandbox_credentials() -> dict`\n  - `get_opencode_serve_settings() -> dict`\n  - `save_sandbox_settings(sandbox_config: dict) -> None` — validates and writes back\n- Add validation logic:\n  - `enabled` is bool\n  - `image` is string\n  - `network` is bool\n  - `opencode_serve.port` is int 1024-65535\n  - Credential toggles are bools\n  - Custom mounts have required fields\n  - Profiles have at least one mount\n  - Mount paths are relative (no `..` traversal)\n  - Mount modes are `\"rw\"` or `\"ro\"`\n  - Profile names are alphanumeric + hyphens\n  - Invalid config on load: log warning, apply defaults for invalid fields\n\n**Tests:**\n- Unit tests for defaults application (missing section, partial, empty)\n- Unit tests for validation (invalid modes, missing fields, path traversal rejection)\n- Unit tests for settings write-back (preserves other sections)\n\n### 1.2 Data Models\n\n**New file: `vista/server/models/sandbox.py`**\n\nDefine dataclasses used across the sandbox feature:\n\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass MountSpec:\n    path: str        # Relative to project root, supports ${FEATURE}\n    mode: str        # \"rw\" or \"ro\"\n\n@dataclass\nclass AccessProfile:\n    name: str\n    mounts: list[MountSpec]\n    network: bool | None  # None = inherit global\n\n@dataclass\nclass CredentialDetection:\n    found: bool\n    method: str           # \"env_var\", \"config_dir\", \"config_file\", \"not_found\"\n    source_path: str\n    display_info: str\n\n@dataclass\nclass DockerMount:\n    host_path: str\n    container_path: str\n    mode: str\n\n@dataclass\nclass DockerCredentialConfig:\n    env_vars: dict[str, str]\n    mounts: list[DockerMount]\n\n@dataclass\nclass ContainerInfo:\n    name: str\n    job_id: str\n    provider: str\n    status: str\n    session_id: str\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Credential Management\n\n### 2.1 Path Translation\n\n**New file: `vista/server/services/sandbox/path_translator.py`**\n\n```python\nclass PathTranslator:\n    def translate(self, host_path: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Convert host path to Docker bind mount path.\n        Windows: C:\\\\Users\\\\Grove\\\\.ssh → /c/Users/Grove/.ssh\n        Others: no change needed.\n        \"\"\"\n```\n\n- Detect platform via `platform.system()`\n- Windows: convert drive letter pattern `X:\\...` to `/x/...`\n- Linux/macOS: passthrough\n\n### 2.2 UID/GID Detection\n\n**In `path_translator.py` or standalone utility:**\n\n```python\ndef get_host_uid_gid() -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"Windows/WSL2: (1000, 1000). Linux/macOS: os.getuid(), os.getgid().\"\"\"\n```\n\n### 2.3 Credential Providers\n\n**New file: `vista/server/services/sandbox/credential_providers.py`**\n\nImplement the `CredentialProvider` base class and four built-in providers:\n\n1. **`ClaudeAuthProvider`** — `applies_to: [\"claude\"]`\n   - Detects `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` env var, then `~/.claude/` directory\n   - Docker config: env var forwarding + `~/.claude/` mount (rw)\n   - Validation: `claude --version`\n\n2. **`GitSshProvider`** — `applies_to: [\"*\"]`\n   - Detects `~/.ssh/` with key files\n   - Docker config: `~/.ssh/` mount (ro)\n   - Validation: `ssh -T git@github.com`\n\n3. **`GitConfigProvider`** — `applies_to: [\"*\"]`\n   - Detects `~/.gitconfig`\n   - Docker config: `~/.gitconfig` mount (ro)\n   - Validation: `git config user.name && git config user.email`\n\n4. **`GitHubCliProvider`** — `applies_to: [\"*\"]`\n   - Detects `~/.config/gh/` (Linux/macOS) or `%APPDATA%\\GitHub CLI\\` (Windows)\n   - Docker config: mount (ro)\n   - Validation: `gh auth status`\n\n5. **`CustomMountProvider`** — from settings `custom` array\n   - Detects: host path exists\n   - Docker config: as specified\n   - Validation: `test -r {container_path}`\n\n### 2.4 Credential Gathering\n\n```python\ndef gather_credentials(provider_name: str, settings: dict) -> list[DockerCredentialConfig]:\n    \"\"\"Iterate providers, filter by applies_to + enabled, detect, return configs.\"\"\"\n```\n\n**Tests:**\n- Unit tests per provider: detection with mocked filesystem/env\n- Unit tests for path translation: Windows, Linux, macOS\n- Unit tests for Docker config generation\n- Unit tests for `applies_to` filtering\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Access Profiles\n\n### 3.1 Profile Resolution\n\n**New file: `vista/server/services/sandbox/access_profiles.py`**\n\n```python\ndef resolve_profile(explicit: str | None, model: str, settings: dict) -> AccessProfile:\n    \"\"\"Priority: explicit > model_defaults > 'full-access'.\"\"\"\n\ndef substitute_variables(mount_path: str, feature: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Replace ${FEATURE}, ${PROJECT_ROOT} in mount paths.\"\"\"\n\ndef to_docker_mounts(profile: AccessProfile, project_root: Path, translator: PathTranslator) -> list[dict]:\n    \"\"\"Convert profile mounts to Docker bind mount dicts.\"\"\"\n```\n\n- Validate: paths relative, no `..`, at least one mount\n- Special case: `\".\"` → mount entire project root as `/workspace/`\n- Skip non-existent mount paths with warning (not error)\n- Error if OpenCode + `network: false` profile\n\n**Tests:**\n- Unit tests for profile resolution chain\n- Unit tests for variable substitution\n- Unit tests for mount translation\n- Unit tests for validation rules\n- Unit test: OpenCode + network-disabled = error\n\n---\n\n## Phase 4: Container Lifecycle Management\n\n### 4.1 ContainerManager\n\n**New file: `vista/server/services/sandbox/container_manager.py`**\n\nDepends on `docker` Python SDK (new dependency: `pip install docker`).\n\n```python\nclass ContainerManager:\n    def __init__(self, session_id: str):\n        self.docker = docker.from_env()\n        self.session_id = session_id\n\n    async def create_loop_container(\n        self, job_id, provider_name, project_root, credentials, image, network=True\n    ) -> ContainerInfo\n\n    async def exec_in_container(\n        self, container_name, command, workdir=\"/workspace\", env=None, stdout_handle=None\n    ) -> ExecHandle\n\n    async def remove_container(self, container_name) -> None\n    async def cleanup_orphans(self) -> list[str]\n    async def shutdown_all(self) -> None\n    def list_containers(self) -> list[ContainerInfo]\n```\n\nKey implementation details:\n- Container created with `command=\"sleep infinity\"`, loop runs via `docker exec`\n- Labels: `managed-by=vista-ralph`, `vista-job-id`, `vista-provider`, `vista-session`, `vista-project`\n- `extra_hosts={\"host.docker.internal\": \"host-gateway\"}` for Linux compatibility\n- `user=f\"{uid}:{gid}\"` from `get_host_uid_gid()`\n- `DEVCONTAINER=true` env var\n\n### 4.2 Docker Image Management\n\n```python\nasync def ensure_image(self, image_name=\"vista-ralph:latest\") -> str:\n    \"\"\"Check if image exists locally. If not, build from bundled Dockerfile.\"\"\"\n```\n\n- Bundle a simplified Dockerfile in `vista/server/data/sandbox/Dockerfile` based on claudebox\n- Build args: `USER_ID`, `GROUP_ID`, `NODE_VERSION`\n- Store image hash in settings to detect Dockerfile changes\n\n### 4.3 Orphan Cleanup\n\n- On Vista startup: query containers with label `managed-by=vista-ralph` where `vista-session != current_session`\n- Stop and remove orphans\n- Log removed container names\n\n**Tests:**\n- Unit tests for container naming and label generation\n- Unit tests for volume mount construction\n- Integration tests (real Docker): create → exec → remove\n- Integration test: orphan cleanup\n\n---\n\n## Phase 5: OpenCode Serve Management\n\n### 5.1 OpenCodeServeManager\n\n**New file: `vista/server/services/sandbox/opencode_serve_manager.py`**\n\n```python\nclass OpenCodeServeManager:\n    def __init__(self, port: int = 4096):\n        self.port = port\n        self.process: subprocess.Popen | None = None\n        self.sessions: dict[str, str] = {}  # job_id → session_id\n\n    async def ensure_running(self) -> None\n    async def create_session(self, job_id: str, cwd: str) -> str\n    async def close_session(self, job_id: str) -> None\n    async def stop(self) -> None\n    def is_running(self) -> bool\n```\n\n- Starts `opencode serve --port {port} --hostname 127.0.0.1`\n- Health check: `GET http://localhost:{port}/doc`\n- Auto-restart on failure\n\n### 5.2 Vista Proxy Endpoint\n\n**New file: `vista/server/routes/sandbox.py`**\n\n```python\nrouter = APIRouter(prefix=\"/api/sandbox\", tags=[\"sandbox\"])\n\n@router.post(\"/opencode/{session_id}/message\")\nasync def opencode_proxy_message(session_id: str, request: Request):\n    \"\"\"Forward message to opencode serve session on host.\"\"\"\n\n@router.get(\"/status\")\nasync def sandbox_status():\n    \"\"\"Returns { docker_available, docker_running, image_built, image_name }.\"\"\"\n\n@router.put(\"/settings\")\nasync def sandbox_settings_update(body: dict):\n    \"\"\"Write sandbox.enabled toggle.\"\"\"\n\n@router.post(\"/credentials/validate\")\nasync def validate_credentials():\n    \"\"\"Run credential validation in temp container.\"\"\"\n\n@router.post(\"/image/build\")\nasync def build_image():\n    \"\"\"Trigger sandbox image build.\"\"\"\n```\n\n**Tests:**\n- Integration test: opencode serve start, health check, session create/close, stop\n- API test: proxy endpoint forwards correctly\n\n---\n\n## Phase 6: RalphService Integration\n\n### 6.1 Modify `create_job()` in `vista/server/services/ralph_service.py`\n\nAdd sandbox branch to `create_job()`:\n\n```python\ndef create_job(self, project_root, slug, mode, task_description, provider, model, iterations):\n    # ... existing setup (job_id, job_dir, task_file, prompt, loop script) ...\n\n    sandbox_settings = config.get_sandbox_settings()\n    if sandbox_settings.get(\"enabled\"):\n        return self._create_sandbox_job(\n            job_dir, project_root, slug, mode, task_description,\n            provider, model, iterations, sandbox_settings\n        )\n    else:\n        # Current behavior: local subprocess\n        return self._create_local_job(...)\n```\n\n**`_create_sandbox_job` flow (Claude Code):**\n1. Generate `loop.sh` (always bash in container)\n2. Gather credentials (claude_auth + git_ssh + git_config)\n3. Resolve access profile\n4. `container_manager.create_loop_container(...)`\n5. `container_manager.exec_in_container(command=[\"bash\", loop.sh])`\n6. Track exec PID + container name in job.json\n\n**`_create_sandbox_job` flow (OpenCode):**\n1. Ensure `opencode serve` running on host\n2. Create serve session\n3. Generate `loop.sh` from `OPENCODE_SANDBOX_LOOP_TEMPLATE`\n4. Gather credentials (git_ssh + git_config only, no AI creds)\n5. `container_manager.create_loop_container(...)`\n6. `container_manager.exec_in_container(command=[\"bash\", loop.sh], env={VISTA_HOST, VISTA_PORT, OPENCODE_SESSION, MODEL})`\n7. Track exec PID + container name + session_id in job.json\n\n### 6.2 New Loop Script Template\n\n**Add to `vista/portable/ralph.py`:**\n\n`OPENCODE_SANDBOX_LOOP_TEMPLATE` — bash script that calls Vista proxy via `curl` instead of `opencode run`. (Full template is in the ralph-mcp-integration spec.)\n\n### 6.3 Modify Loop Script Generation\n\nWhen sandbox is enabled:\n- Always generate `loop.sh` (bash), never `loop.ps1`\n- For Claude: use existing `LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE` with `shell=\"sh\"` (already works)\n- For OpenCode: use new `OPENCODE_SANDBOX_LOOP_TEMPLATE`\n\n### 6.4 Modify `stop_job()`\n\n```python\ndef stop_job(self, project_root, job_id):\n    job = self._load_job(...)\n    if job.get(\"sandbox\"):\n        self._kill_pid(job[\"pid\"])\n        if job.get(\"opencode_session\"):\n            await opencode_serve_manager.close_session(job_id)\n        await container_manager.remove_container(f\"vista-ralph-{job_id}\")\n    else:\n        # Current behavior\n        self._kill_pid(job[\"pid\"])\n```\n\n### 6.5 Modify `get_job_status()`\n\nWhen sandbox is active, also check container status (is container still running?).\n\n### 6.6 Job Metadata Extension\n\nWhen sandbox is active, `job.json` includes:\n```json\n{\n  \"sandbox\": true,\n  \"container\": \"vista-ralph-{job_id}\",\n  \"opencode_session\": \"sess_xyz789\"  // OpenCode only\n}\n```\n\n**Tests:**\n- Unit test: `create_job()` routes to container when `sandbox.enabled = true`\n- Unit test: `create_job()` uses local subprocess when `sandbox.enabled = false`\n- Unit test: Claude loops use bash template\n- Unit test: OpenCode loops use proxy template\n- Unit test: job.json includes sandbox metadata\n- Unit test: `stop_job()` removes container + closes session\n- Integration test: full `ralph_start` → `ralph_status` → `ralph_stop` cycle\n\n---\n\n## Phase 7: Credential Validation\n\n### 7.1 Validation Flow\n\n**In `vista/server/services/sandbox/credential_validation.py`:**\n\n```python\nasync def validate_credentials(\n    credential_providers: list[CredentialProvider],\n    container_manager: ContainerManager,\n    image: str,\n) -> list[ValidationResult]:\n    \"\"\"\n    1. Detect all enabled credentials on host\n    2. Create temp container with credential mounts\n    3. Run validation command per credential inside container\n    4. Collect pass/fail\n    5. Tear down temp container\n    \"\"\"\n```\n\n- Runs automatically at Vista startup when `sandbox.enabled = true`\n- Results logged to Vista server log\n- Also available via `POST /api/sandbox/credentials/validate`\n\n**Tests:**\n- Integration test: full validation flow with real Docker\n\n---\n\n## Phase 8: Vista App Startup Integration\n\n### 8.1 Modify `vista/server/app.py` Lifespan\n\nIn the `lifespan` context manager:\n\n**Startup:**\n1. Generate unique session_id\n2. If `sandbox.enabled`:\n   - Attempt `docker.from_env()` — if fails, log error, mark sandbox unavailable\n   - Run `container_manager.cleanup_orphans()`\n   - Run credential validation (log results)\n   - Ensure Docker image exists (build if needed)\n3. Initialize `ContainerManager(session_id)`\n4. Initialize `OpenCodeServeManager(port)` (lazy — doesn't start serve until first OpenCode loop)\n\n**Shutdown:**\n1. `container_manager.shutdown_all()` — stop and remove all managed containers\n2. `opencode_serve_manager.stop()` — stop serve if running\n\n### 8.2 Register Sandbox Routes\n\nAdd `sandbox` router to `app.py`:\n```python\nfrom server.routes import sandbox\napp.include_router(sandbox.router)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 9: Dashboard UI\n\n### 9.1 Sandbox Toggle in Ralph Settings\n\n**File: `vista/server/views/ralph_settings.html`**\n\nAdd a \"Docker Sandbox\" toggle section:\n- Toggle control bound to `sandbox.enabled`\n- When ON: call `GET /api/sandbox/status` and display inline status:\n  - Green dot: \"Docker running\"\n  - Amber dot: \"Building image...\"\n  - Red dot: \"Docker not running\" + guidance\n  - Red dot: \"Docker Desktop required\" + install guidance\n- When OFF: no status check\n\n**API used:**\n- `GET /api/sandbox/status` → `{ docker_available, docker_running, image_built, image_name }`\n- `PUT /api/sandbox/settings` → `{ enabled: true|false }`\n\n**Tests:**\n- API test: status returns correct Docker/image state\n- API test: settings toggle saves correctly\n\n---\n\n## Phase 10: Docker Image Bundling\n\n### 10.1 Modified Claudebox Dockerfile\n\n**New file: `vista/server/data/sandbox/Dockerfile`**\n\nBased on the claudebox Dockerfile with modifications:\n- Slimmer (remove zsh, tmux, delta, fzf — optional tooling)\n- Keep: git, Node.js, Claude Code CLI, Python, bash, gh CLI, jq, curl\n- Build args: `USER_ID`, `GROUP_ID`, `NODE_VERSION`\n- `DEVCONTAINER=true` env var\n- `WORKDIR /workspace`\n- `ENTRYPOINT [\"sleep\", \"infinity\"]` (simpler than claudebox entrypoint — we use `docker exec`)\n\n### 10.2 Docker Ignore\n\n**New file: `vista/server/data/sandbox/.dockerignore`**\n\nStandard ignores for build context.\n\n---\n\n## Dependency Summary\n\n| New Dependency | Purpose | Install |\n|---|---|---|\n| `docker` (Python SDK) | Docker API access | `pip install docker` |\n\nThis goes in the plugin's requirements/dependencies. Since the plugin runs as an MCP server (Python process), the `docker` package needs to be available at runtime. It should be added as an optional dependency — sandbox features gracefully degrade if `docker` is not installed.\n\n---\n\n## File Creation / Modification Summary\n\n### New Files\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `vista/server/models/sandbox.py` | Dataclasses: MountSpec, AccessProfile, DockerMount, etc. |\n| `vista/server/services/sandbox/__init__.py` | Package init |\n| `vista/server/services/sandbox/path_translator.py` | Host-to-Docker path conversion + UID/GID |\n| `vista/server/services/sandbox/credential_providers.py` | 5 credential providers + gathering logic |\n| `vista/server/services/sandbox/access_profiles.py` | Profile resolution, variable substitution, Docker mount conversion |\n| `vista/server/services/sandbox/container_manager.py` | Container lifecycle: create, exec, remove, orphan cleanup, image management |\n| `vista/server/services/sandbox/opencode_serve_manager.py` | Host-side `opencode serve` process management |\n| `vista/server/services/sandbox/credential_validation.py` | Credential validation flow |\n| `vista/server/routes/sandbox.py` | API: status, settings toggle, proxy, credential validate, image build |\n| `vista/server/data/sandbox/Dockerfile` | Modified claudebox Dockerfile for Vista sandbox |\n| `vista/server/data/sandbox/.dockerignore` | Build context ignore |\n| `vista/tests/test_sandbox_settings.py` | Settings schema tests |\n| `vista/tests/test_credential_providers.py` | Credential provider tests |\n| `vista/tests/test_access_profiles.py` | Profile resolution tests |\n| `vista/tests/test_container_manager.py` | Container lifecycle tests |\n| `vista/tests/test_path_translator.py` | Path translation tests |\n\n### Modified Files\n\n| File | Change |\n|---|---|\n| `vista/server/config.py` | Add `_SANDBOX_DEFAULTS`, `get_sandbox_settings()`, `is_sandbox_enabled()`, etc. |\n| `vista/server/services/ralph_service.py` | Add sandbox branch in `create_job()`, `stop_job()`, `get_job_status()` |\n| `vista/server/app.py` | Startup: init ContainerManager, orphan cleanup, credential validation. Shutdown: container cleanup. Register sandbox routes. |\n| `vista/portable/ralph.py` | Add `OPENCODE_SANDBOX_LOOP_TEMPLATE` |\n| `vista/server/views/ralph_settings.html` | Add sandbox toggle + inline status |\n| `vista/settings.json` | No structural change (defaults applied at runtime), but example updated |\n\n---\n\n## Build Order (Recommended)\n\nThe phases should be implemented sequentially, with each phase building on the previous:\n\n1. **Phase 1** (Settings + Data Models) — foundation for everything else\n2. **Phase 2** (Credentials) — needed by container creation\n3. **Phase 3** (Access Profiles) — needed by container creation\n4. **Phase 4** (ContainerManager) — core container lifecycle\n5. **Phase 5** (OpenCode Serve) — second execution path\n6. **Phase 6** (RalphService Integration) — ties it all together\n7. **Phase 7** (Credential Validation) — startup-time verification\n8. **Phase 8** (App Startup) — lifecycle hooks\n9. **Phase 9** (Dashboard UI) — user-facing toggle\n10. **Phase 10** (Docker Image) — bundled Dockerfile\n\nPhases 2 + 3 can be done in parallel. Phases 7 + 9 + 10 can be done in parallel after Phase 6 is complete.\n\n---\n\n## Risk & Edge Cases\n\n| Risk | Mitigation |\n|---|---|\n| Docker not installed | Graceful degradation: sandbox marked unavailable, loops run locally |\n| Docker SDK import failure | Lazy import; if `docker` package missing, sandbox features disabled with clear error |\n| WSL2 bind mount performance | Acceptable per NFR; document in known limitations |\n| Port conflict for opencode serve | Try next available port; log error |\n| Concurrent loops on same project files | Git operations may conflict; acceptable per spec (documented) |\n| Orphaned containers after crash | Cleanup on startup via session_id comparison |\n| UID/GID mismatch | Use host UID/GID as build args (Windows defaults to 1000:1000) |\n| `~/.claude/` must be rw | Explicitly mounted read-write (differs from claudebox copy pattern) |\n","numLines":611,"startLine":1,"totalLines":611}}}
